{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point","id":907459,"title":"Changing What You Don't Like, or Missing the Point","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-04T22:36:48-07:00","id":907459,"title":"Changing What You Don't Like, or Missing the Point","content":"I've been noticing a trend on the various ChroD Forums: it seems that just about every gameline has developed an alternate fanbase that dislikes some core aspect of the gameline and proposes hacks to change the gameline in question. Meanwhile, there are fans of the game as written who consider such hacks to be missing the point of the game. This is an attempt to catalog this phenomenon. <br /> <br /> Note: I'm trying not to pass judgment. Some of these, I like; others, I don't. That's not the point of the catalog. If you want to advocate for one side or the other on any of these points, I won't try to stop you. But let's at least complete the catalog first, OK? <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Vampire:</b> I'm not familiar enough with the gameline to know, nor do I visit the forum frequently enough to have picked up on anything here. Anyone want to help me out? <br /> \u2022 <b>Werewolf:</b> There are those who dislike the animism baked into the gameline, and have explored ways to strip it out. <br /> \u2022 <b>Mage:</b> I'm not as familiar with this gameline's dissidents; but I know that there are some who try to stretch Mage to handle magic user concepts that it isn't designed to handle. <br /> \u2022 <b>Promethean:</b> This is an easy one: there's a vocal faction that doesn't like the game's focus on becoming human. <br /> \u2022 <b>Changeling:</b> There are some who want a more traditional concept of \u201cchangeling\u201d: a fae thrust into mortal society and trying to fit in. <br /> \u2022 <b>Hunter:</b> some would like to see Hunter support Heroic Mortals: not people with access to Endowments, but hunters who are nevertheless a cut above your average mortal. This ranges from traits designed to mitigate the uneven playing field regular mortals have to deal with all the way to giving hunters a power stat. <br /> \u2022 <b>Geist:</b> I don't know if this qualifies, but I've seen a general misperception of this gameline as \u201cZombie: the Walking Dead\u201d. <br /> \u2022 <b>Mummy:</b> non-Iremite Arisen.<br /> \u2022 <b>Demon:</b> scrapping the tech- overtones.<br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> I don't know. If there's one gameline with which I'm less familiar than Vampire, it's this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T22:51:40-07:00","id":907463,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that the Changeling one is &quot;I want my character to have had a pleasant Durance&quot; and/or &quot;I want to shirk the abuse metaphor entirely.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T23:02:06-07:00","id":907468,"title":"","content":"Yeah; that's probably a better way to phrase it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T23:22:34-07:00","id":907477,"title":"","content":"Not wanting to take this thread off track, I'll keep this note short. For me most &quot;missing the point&quot; arguments are themselves missing the point. Table top RP is a flexible medium, the first rule in every single splat-book is the Golden Rule: Change What You Don't Like.<br /> <br /> Not certain how to add to this thread constructively, but since I'm a prime offender in the changing shit category I suppose I'll list what I like to change and why.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>General: </b>X-Splats, I remove them where possible in favor of Z-Splats or 0-Splats.<ul><li><i>I think they are good for getting people started, and hopping into the game, but become increasingly restrictive the more you play. For instance, I find Bloodlines more interesting than Clans, and think Sin-Eater has enough character variety with the different Geister that Thresholds are wholly unnecessary.</i></li> </ul><b>General: </b>Supernal Population, I tent to think the books paint a world with too many enormouslypowerful supernaturals. I try to reduce the count of &quot;big-splats&quot; in favor of the little ones (revenants, wolf-blooded, thaumaturges, etc.)<ul><li><i>This might be a running crossover thing, but I find it hard to run &quot;big&quot; stories in a city in which there are 50+ Mages, or one hundred some odd vampires. Cutting down on the big splats also lets me make all of those present stand out, the PCs feel a little more special, and keeps the big players tightly focused around the story.</i></li> </ul><i><b>General: </b></i>Human villain splats (Seers of the Throne, The Pure, Heroes, Alchemists, etc.) my hate for them runs deep.<ul><li><i>This one runs deep, and is definitely a personal preference, but I find &quot;bad guy groups&quot; fairly unnecessary. They are frequently used either as mustache twirling evils, or as (in my opinion) poor strawmen through which to poo-poo existing groups (1%ers are a popular one now days). I prefer the GRRM approach, a world of people with complex motivations who are heroes in their own tales and villains in others. <i>Weird cosmic <b>evils</b> also aren't my thing. Or, rather, I prefer my cosmic entities so alien that applying the concepts of good and evil to them is a stupendous waste of time...actually, just toss out the ideas of good and evil altogether, that'd be nice.</i></i></li> <li><i>There is a near 100% chance some one is going to go for my throat for saying this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i></li> </ul><i><b>Werewolf</b>: Freer access to Gauru, less punishing Kuruth.</i><ul><li><i>Ever notice how <b>all the Forsaken art</b> has Uratha running about doing not fighty things in Gauru? As a person who is a strongly visual thinker this bothers me a lot. The Kuruth change on the other hand, that's mostly for crossover, and the fact that no one really likes going into Death Rage save when it's really, clearly appropriate.</i></li> </ul><i><b>Mage</b></i>: More limits, more style.<ul><li><i>Mages are a tad on the powerful side for my liking. I find the constant slinging of such a wide variety of spells without clear <u>narrative limits</u> (those being limits that are easily displayed without explaining game mechanics) to be destructive to individual character variety. It's a preference thing for sure, but I favor Mages who have clear niches in which they are terrifyingly potent, and clear limits which even the unawakened might exploit.</i></li> </ul><i>\u200b<b>Promethean: </b></i>Less explicit focus on becoming human.<ul><li><i>I'm not one of those who dislikes the Humanism of Promethean, but I do greatly dislike how the game handles it. Prometheans learning to be human, and to live within the world is great. Prometheans actively intending to become human, and having a mechanical, built-in drive by which they can approach it sours me greatly. So when I do approach the New Dawn, I do it much like the Mummy Storyteller section, secretly, without clarity, and wholly individual.</i></li> </ul><b><i>Demon: </i></b>Less God-Machine focus.<ul><li><i>I'm not one who dislikes the God-Machine, or tech Demons, but for crossover Demons are a hard inclusion. They almost inevitably bring in story elements that may have nothing to do with the setting. So I refocus around Glitches and let their cover breaches sort themselves out within the context of the existing narrative.</i></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There, hopefully that counts as constructive, if it doesn't I'll remove it. As Dataweaver said, please lets not argue about the &quot;correctness&quot; of house rules. If you must excoriate me for &quot;missing the point&quot; I've got a whole <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\">hub thread</a> for people to yelling at me.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Some other Mage ones, not mine, but I've had to mod discussions on the following topics more than once:<ul><li>Atlantis, and how much some people hate it.</li> <li>Non-Hermetic Magic, and how some see Awakening as &quot;Order of Hermes: The Too Damn Narrow&quot;</li> <li>Arcadia, and the game of crossover terms.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 06-05-2016, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T23:37:40-07:00","id":907482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907477#post907477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not wanting to take this thread off track, I'll keep this note short. For me most &quot;missing the point&quot; arguments are themselves missing the point. Table top RP is a flexible medium, the first rule in every single splat-book is the Golden Rule: Change What You Don't Like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this isn't intended to be a criticism of either side of these debates. At one point or another, I've been on both sides; and it's not as simple as telling the \u201cmissing the point\u201d side that the \u201cchange what you don't like\u201d side has the right of it, or vice versa: quite often, <i>both sides</i> have valid points to make.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh yeah; Mage. I can't believe I overlooked this one, given that I myself have been one of the loudest voices criticizing it: the sheer harshness of 2e's handling of Sleepers and the Sleeping Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-05-2016, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T23:50:58-07:00","id":907486,"title":"","content":"I'm conflicted because I'm a diehard thematic purist (these games were meant to be personal horror and shoukd remain as such), but then there are entire gamelines that I basically just ignore because they don't fit what I want from things. Ultimately, your table is your table, but the problem with coming into dedicated forums like we have here and coming at people who are ostensibly fans of the games the way they are makes discussion of alternatives incredibly difficult.<br /> <br /> I had a thread about this ages ago where it was &quot;which gamelines exist, which ones don't, and ehich are heavily modified in your own canon?&quot; and I think maybe it should come back. Lemme try and find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T23:58:53-07:00","id":907490,"title":"","content":"I've noted in both Werewolf and Vampire that there's a lot of people who want aspects of Apocalypse and Masquerade in them, from the more familial clans and generations to the war against the Wyrm. Focused more on Requiem, there's people wanting vampires to be less inimical to humans. This tends to range from things like removing the Beast to not having to drink blood. There's some people who like the concept of werewolf but, for whatever reason, don't like the 'werewolf' part. This too has multiple forms, with some wanting the 'spirit police' angle of first edition available to humans, or keep the shapeshifting but be a variety of other animals, werebears, weredeer, and so forth. Some people seem to want a more clear good versus evil view in Hunter and don't want the cancer cells, corruption in the conspiracies or morally ambiguous protagonists. There's a lot of different things people want from Geist, usually with a tendency towards a particular game or show that's popular at the time. I don't think it's really fair to say these are alternate versions so much as hopes for second edition.<br /> <br /> The people who want different things from Beast seem to want either to be actually able to play the Horror without having to get your Inheritance to do it, and playable and less reprehensible Heroes. I think they managed to get them to be less hateful monsters in the rewrites but its way down my list of things to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:08:30-07:00","id":907494,"title":"","content":"My personal beef is primarily with Mage, which I've always argued has something of a thematic disconnect with the rest of the CofD; in a world about horror and mystery, having godlike power and focusing on finding answers seems to somewhat miss the point. They're the line with the least drawbacks, and while one can warn about the dangers of hubris or point to all the scary Abyssal beasties they, it stands to reason that Awakening is gonna be a straight upgrade from mortal life for most people. Look at the &quot;Who are you in the CofD?&quot; thread and see all the people excited to have magic powers.<br /> <br /> That's not to say it isn't a fantastic game - it is! - but it feels like one of dark urban fantasy more than anythig else. Wizards aren't a classic monster archetype like vampires or mummies, so their inclusion has always felt odd, whether in oWoD's &quot;steampunk space battles in Jupiter's orbit&quot; or in CofD's &quot;you get to see the Truth everyone else is blind to,&quot; and I think that really hurts it.<br /> <br /> Wht especially calls my complaints into focus is the existence of Unknown Armies, a game about... people in the modern day driven by obsession who use magic powers. That's a game where obsession and magic break down individual's sanity and their ability to relate to normal people, and they destroy themselves in their pursuits of power and desire to reshape reality. That's personal horror in a game about secret wizards, and makes Mage look all the sillier for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:08:42-07:00","id":907495,"title":"","content":"Some of my observations from years and years of (mostly) lurking.<br /> <br /> <b>VtR - </b>At least during the first few years of the NWoD, the biggest complaints i can remember was that it wasn't Masquerade.No Malkavians,No Tzimisce, and other familiar VtM elementswere left out of the new version and quite a few people were rather salty about it.More recently I have seen the threads pop up where the intent was to remove some of the more horrific elements of the setting (especially the abuse, addiction and sexuality metaphors).<br /> <br /> <b>WtF</b> - The complaints I saw here were mostly mechanical; players wanted the Uratha to be the same type of full bleed bad-asses the Garou were in WtA. While 2nd Edition bridged alot of this gap, a player expecting the same raw power from a uratha as they got ffrom a Garou is going to be disappointed. I also see alot of requests to make the Pure a less directly antagonistic faction. While the <i>Anshega </i>are nearly always described as violent, hateful zealots, many players enjoy giving the devil his due and would prefer their antagonists to be more sympathetic(sometimes more sympathetic than the so-called protagonists).<br /> <br /> <b>MtAw</b> - Atlantis and Edition War. The idea of Atlantis being presented as a setting fact did not sit well with many. While I always assumed the story of Atlantis was a parable, others felt they were beholden to a concept that carries a lot of real-world pop culture baggage. Probably after that, the most common concern was that paradigm was no longer a important part of magic. Many players like being able to define their &quot;truth&quot; and change the world with it, rather than the truth being an absolute thing that they had to uncover. Related was the distinct lack of Virtual Adept/Son's of Ether style enlightened science. I think the fan game Genius the Transgression was essentially born out of the desire to restore Enlightened science to the setting.<br /> <br /> <b>PtC</b> - Transhumanism and such. This one is contentious. The argument to seemed to be a degree a cognitive dissonance. A Promethean is a powerful, almost unstoppable being. The idea that anyone would give up such might to be just a regular Joe Monday seemed flat out wrong to many players, who would rather explore the limits of their condition than to look for ways out of it. While I personally like the humanist themes (after playing many, many games where the players become world crushing titans crackling with raw power, the idea of just wanting to be A Person was amazingly refreshing).<br /> <br /> <b>HtV</b> - What I have seen here is mostly mechanics for giving hunters more of an edge. Even an experienced hunter can't wade into a room full of vampires, guns blazing and expect to walk out with their organs intact, and for some that inability to truly go head to head is a missed opportunity.<br /> <br /> <b>CtD</b> - Didn't pay enough attention to Changeling to see what the biggest cracks in the base were, but I have run into people who liked the idea of Changelings who were forced out of Arcadia rather than escaping.<br /> <br /> <b>GtSE</b> - Didn't learn enough about the setting, but I did hear there were numerous mechanical issues with the main power set.<br /> <br /> <b>MtC</b> - The tightly focused settings and themes were both a blessing and a curse. Some enjoyed the history and mythology of Irem. Others would have preferred something more global, where they could play a mummy from one of the many other cultures that practiced mummification.<br /> <br /> <b>DtD - </b>The Techno-Gnostic themes and aesthetics seem to be off-putting for many who were expecting a more traditional heaven vs hell experience. Never mind that it utterly ignores the material in the popular and well-received <i>Inferno</i> source book. As others have observed, DtD is probably the hardest material to incorporate into a pre-existing campaign or cross - over game.<br /> <br /> <b>BtP</b> - While I don't recall all the specific issues, there were enough of them that the text had to be revised after the first draft was released. One I do recall was the presentation of &quot;Heroes&quot; - the title being ironic and a little mocking for what were presented as disturbed and unstable murderers didn't sit well with some. There was also some desire for them to be presented in a more sympathetic (and perhaps playable) light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":".  oh yeah - Demon 06-05-2016, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:14:04-07:00","id":907498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907482#post907482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this isn't intended to be a criticism of either side of these debates. At one point or another, I've been on both sides; and it's not as simple as telling the \u201cmissing the point\u201d side that the \u201cchange what you don't like\u201d side has the right of it, or vice versa: quite often, <i>both sides</i> have valid points to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly. Though, at least from a mod perspective, I find it more often the case that both sides are arguing entirely different things. The purists are arguing how the game is intended to be, and the hackers are arguing about what they want it to be. The arguments flare up when one side is unwilling or unable to accept that the other desires to change/retain some aspect of the game. Seriously, if more people could look at a post and say, &quot;Welp, this one's not for me&quot; this forum would be a much nicer place (for me).<br /> <br /> Now, to make this post productive:<ul><li><b>Vampire</b>: A lot of people don't like the decent into monstrosity, and want hacks/bloodlines/spells/coils that allow them to skip out on the entire humanity side of the game altogether. The same can be said of each Covenant, especially the Order of the Dragon (so many &quot;Coils of Humanity&quot;)</li> <li><b>Werewolf: </b>I said this in my post, but I said a lot there. Less restrictions of Gauru. Some want to run around in furry murder ball mode, others (myself included) would just be happy if the text matched up with the art.</li> <li><b>Beast: </b>Some, myself included, think Heroes are immensely boring antagonists and would love to see them beefed up and/or made slightly more complex.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:27:25-07:00","id":907503,"title":"","content":"Vampire: The biggest one I've seen is disliking Humanity and the themes of struggling against the Beast. The strongest dissenters seem to want it to be easier - or even just a given - that vampires have an emotional balance with what they are as the default. VtR 2e generally makes this worse because the new Humanity system is meant to be even more present and the struggle to maintain it much more central.<br /> <br /> Promethean: Also has a lot of people that don't like the Disquiet side of the game and the themes of isolation it stems from.<br /> <br /> Beast: A few here. First, there are people that don't like the Beast/Hero relationship because they've painted various real world analogs on to it and the implications of doing so are always messy. The game focuses strongly on a cycle of abuse rather than one way oppressive conflicts, but a lot of people seem to want it to be less muddled as beasts abuse and in the process create those that abuse them in return. Second, there's the, &quot;I want a monster true form,&quot; group that doesn't like that beasts remain human looking instead of turning into creatures of legend. There's also people that really don't like the inherent and explicit crossover intentions of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:44:43-07:00","id":907508,"title":"","content":"Nofather is close to my thinking. I think there's a lot of baggage from previous incarnations of these game, where applicable. One thing that characterized the old World of Darkness was its arching oppressiveness. Vampire characters struggled against the pyramid of Cainite power, steered by the hands of sleeping giants. Werewolves fought the encroaching doom of the Apocalypse. Mages were crushed under the heel of the Technocracy's jackboots, Oblivion, Banality, yadda, yadda. When there wasn't clear cut good and evil, there was at least a force devouring personal agency, which was where the punk aspect of the games came in.<br /> <br /> And then what we now call Chronicles came, and those divides and bright lines narrowed and dimmed. And some of us embraced it wholeheartedly, and others with one hand. All of which is fine. But I think those doubts are part of &quot;missing the point&quot;. Now vampires aren't dragooned, they're complicit. Werewolves aren't fighting the lost cause, they're murdering on the monthly because that's what they do. Mages lose sight of their humanity rather than trying to exalt it. And for some, that's a downer. <br /> <br /> This is a hobby for die-hard fantasists. I don't know how many people are coming to the Chronicles from D&amp;D or similar works, but they will bring their preferences with them. They might open up to the horror aspect, or they might want to poach a system they find mostly suitable to their needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:56:12-07:00","id":907510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907477#post907477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not wanting to take this thread off track, I'll keep this note short. For me most &quot;missing the point&quot; arguments are themselves missing the point. Table top RP is a flexible medium, the first rule in every single splat-book is the Golden Rule: Change What You Don't Like.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, it's usually not phrased that way. More frequently it's as whatever feature being broken/self-evidently awful and I have come to fix it. That tends to be the thing people take issue with.<br /> <br /> Further people often are missing the point, and can benefit from having large parts of the game broken down and explained. It's happened to me more than once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T02:30:15-07:00","id":907539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point#post907459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 <b>Promethean:</b> This is an easy one: there's a vocal faction that doesn't like the game's focus on becoming human.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I'm many times pointed as one of those - I'm more a bit dissapointed with that games do not explore <i>others </i>answers to the question what should be New Dawn for Prometheans. Is becoming human bad? No, for some characters. Hell, I'm the first one to play Aurum one Created if I can, aiming for being human! But I advocate for free ending of Pilgrimage for all Prometheans, not locking those that are not studying to become humans in to Centimani. Looking for other Pilgrimage ending should not mean that you are cracking monster.<br /> <br /> Still, after seeing how <b>Promethean</b> 2E is developed I can agree that my POV is all hack and respect that at this stage. Does not mean I will not end posting them on forum - just that I mark as all with my hacks: 'Don't like basic idea, do not write in topic - you will save nerves yourself and us all that are interested in it.'<br /> <br /> Basiclly what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> wrote - if topic is Hack and you do not like premise - just move away from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T02:54:01-07:00","id":907547,"title":"","content":"Vampire is a complex one in terms of its themes, even the different editions of Masquerade and Requiem have a different thematic focus. Regardless of what the author intended theme is though, it always gets stripped out for the same thing, <i>blood-powered superheroes</i>. The is the most common altering I've seen across Masquerade and Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T03:51:23-07:00","id":907557,"title":"","content":"Note that this topic is specifically about ChroD games; Masquerade et AL only apply to the extent that people try to hack ChroD games to resemble WoD games.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> \u2014 rather than \u201cif you don't like it, go away\u201d, I prefer \u201cif you don't have anything constructive to say, don't say anything\u201d.<br /> <br /> And\u2026 back to work. See you in the morning!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T05:58:51-07:00","id":907580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907495#post907495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>CtD</b> - Didn't pay enough attention to Changeling to see what the biggest cracks in the base were, but I have run into people who liked the idea of Changelings who were forced out of Arcadia rather than escaping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small nitpick, it's CtL (Changeling the Lost) not CtD (Changeling the Dreaming) CtD is the CWoD changeling gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T06:08:29-07:00","id":907585,"title":"","content":"A trend? Phenomeon? You make it sound like its some passing fad or inexplicable thing. People changing games and houseruling them have happened since pretty much the dawn of time. Sports, board games, card games, video games, you name it. And, given the CofD's subjective nature as a storytelling game instead of a minitures-based war game, this comes off as more lore changes than just mechanics changes. And remember - house rules and hacks are critical to game lines. Hell. I remember, not long before Armory Reloaded came out, there was a thread about what houserules people use. Myself and a few others posted that we turned vampire's bullet-bashing feature to general everything-to-bashing. That ended up as one of the hacks in that book. And now? Its part of 2e core assumptions about vampires.<br /> <br /> These are games. They're written so people have <i>fun</i> with them above all else. Some people don't want to sit down and have deep introspection - they want to blow off steam after a stressful week of work by immersing themselves in a fantasy. And that's cool. And, for the people who say &quot;If you don't like a game, then play something else?&quot; I'm going to paraphrase Anita Sarkeesian for a moment - its okay to like aspects of a game but be criticial of other aspects. You might like one aspect of a game (delving into base emotions ala Vampire) without other aspects (sex metaphor). And that's fine - you can make the game what you will.<br /> <br /> As well? Trying to reduce everything to an &quot;Us versus Them&quot; binary system is problematic. You simply cannot put people into two separate camps and expect it to be anything approaching realistic. Most things in reality operate and a sliding scale instead of nice, neat holes. Its like trying to break all gamers into &quot;roll&quot; players and &quot;role&quot; players. The truth is that most actual players fall between the two extremes. Sure, you have some extremists, but that's the exception, not the rule, and that doesn't touch on players who don't fit neatly into either category, or combination thereof.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its a general trend across ALL CofD games that there are people who are less interested in the moral aspects of the games (and, yes, there are asops in every game; they are designed to provoke thought) and want to do &quot;superheroes with fangs.&quot; Remove Humanity and Touchstones in vampire, downplay the balance-your-territory aspects in werewolf, the insanity and abuse aspects of Changeling, and more. Some players want to play monsters without the soul searching. Everyone is different, and expecting all these issues to resonate with everyone is an exercise doomed to failure. I honesetly think that the alternative-Dawn crowd are the result of this mindset - they're interested in playing the game for fun without the soul searching, and the New Dawn kind of means their fun must come to an end at some point.<br /> <br /> Take the above mentality to an extreme, and we end up with the &quot;hero splat&quot; crowd. People that want the CofD to include elements of Good versus Evil, much like most fantasy games out there. There's been focus on a lot of different ways to do this, but generally, we end up with flame wars as someone or another ends up insulting things that people like while arguing about the fact we don't have a good definition of Good to use as a basis (usually people end up with some variation on Western / Christian values as the default, which is what sparks the controversy).<br /> <br /> In VtR, there's a common trend to try and recreate the old Masquerade clans in the new setting. Tremere and Tziminscee tend to show up quite commonly.<br /> <br /> In WtF, lots of people hate the overreliance on Spirit, and prefer a stronger focus on being half-wolf, half-man. They want less shamanism built so fundamentally into the game.<br /> <br /> In MtAw, there's a lot of gripes about mechanics. Infinite powers means infinite potential for abuse, with little in the way of drawbacks or penalties, and the antagonism towards crossover. There's also a number of people that dislike the firm establishment of the Seers as permanent evil force (anti-hero splat philosophy). Lastly, your bit about &quot;magic user concepts the game isn't desgined to support?&quot; That is more of a question of cultural magics - MtAw <i>culture</i> is firmly Western, and claiming that they're global means we have issues of cultural imperialism and appropriation to the point of being insensitive about other cultures and their mystical traditions. Its the same complaints about Mummy - one Mediteranian culture to rule them all. 2e has gotten slightly better, but overtones remain, and time will tell if the problem was fixed or remains.<br /> <br /> In Promethean, another issue that comes up is that the game is that, despite inclusion of Galatea, Tammuz, and more, the game is fundamentally based entirely on Frankenstein, to the point that everyone is made from corpses and &quot;Fire Bad!&quot; Why does it make sense for a marble statue with an affinity for the divine wind to be weak to flames? Another issue was how, in 1e, you were actively discouraged from playing two members of the same Lineage in a throng. Why tell a group what they can or can't play?<br /> <br /> CtL has some mechanical concerns, and the Gentry bits that pretty much have canned answers that seem to satisfy people at this point. I tend to see more posts about mechanics questions that changing any part of the game. I think the sheer flexibility of the game prevents most issues.<br /> <br /> HtV? Lots of people see this game as a continuation of a mortal game. Not much else to really say.<br /> <br /> GtSE is another super flexible game. The only real complaints I've heard from people are 1) they wish Synergy actually was more about the balance of human/geist, 2) there were ways to actually kill an antagonistic Bound, and 3) slightly less flexible because they weren't sure what to do in the game (basically, they want more direction).<br /> <br /> Mummy... its either a game you like, or don't. I haven't seen a lot of middle ground here.<br /> <br /> Demon is a rather ironic problem - while many games end up with issues about not being culturally flexible enough, DtD has issues with not being Catholic style God and devils.<br /> <br /> Beast has had issues from before the game was even released. Being natural sadists and harming people, unflattering depicttion of heroes, people having trouble grasping the idea behind a &quot;crossover focused game,&quot; the nature of the Horror, and more. Possibly one of the most problematic games to come out. Then, there's complaints of power levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-05-2016, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T06:14:00-07:00","id":907586,"title":"","content":"My issues with games usually revolve around built in restrictions on whether or not you can play certain groups. The most prominent example being Beast having totally unplayable heroes. I do get that there are word limits preventing the groups from being included (like the pure tribes in WtF 2e), but when situations come around like Beast going &quot;no, you don't get to play these people&quot; it ticks me off. Anytime a gameline tries to tell me I can't play an antagonist and it doesn't have incredibly compelling reason (like angels in demon or true fae in changeling) I tend to try and find my way around it with homerules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T07:02:49-07:00","id":907615,"title":"","content":"It's been said before, but one of the proposed hacks I see for almost every game is the removal of the morality/integrity stat, or aspects of it, such as Touchstones. There seem to be various reasons people claim for this. Some folks say they don't like personal horror and feel Integity is too closely tied to that theme. Others say they don't like &quot;punishment mechanics&quot; and feel that Integrity threatens people with character discontinuation if they play the wrong way or engage in wrong behaviors. Some say they don't like the games to take any kind of moral stance and feel that Integrity sets an objective standard of morality that must be followed.<br /> <br /> Another one I've seen a lot is more of a mechanical thing: removing &quot;story game&quot; elements from the rules. Opinions vary on what constitues a story game element, but common candidates include Conditions and/or Beats, Aspirations, opt-in Dramatic Failures, Virtue/Vice and their gameline-specific analogues, Morality/Integrity and their gameline-specific analogues, and generally anything that encourages players to make decisions for their character based on factors external to the character or the narrative.<br /> <br /> Another common one is the removal of various subsystems. Social Maneuvering is a common one. Personally, I don't use the Investigation rules. Some folks don't like extended actions. Integrity, again, is a big one to cut. Some gameline-specific subsystems like feeding rolls in vampire, tracking mechanics in werewolf, focused mage sight in mage (that's one that I would probably remove too if I ran mage) etc.<br /> <br /> RE: Missing the point vs. it's your game, of course it's a complicated issue. It's more than just two opposed camps, (almost) everyone has been on both sides of this argument to some extent depending on the particular element being hacked. My general opinion is, these game elements are designed with intentionality, and one should understand the intent of an element and the effect it has on the theme and mood of a game before hacking it out. I'll argue for or against the removal of different elements based on my own tastes, but ultimately what your group finds fun is more important than the authorial intent, but that intent should be understood before being changed. I also think there does come a point where too many changes or changes too fundamental to the game can put you into square peg, round hole territory. There is value in being able to recognize when what you want from the game and what the game is trying to deliver are just too far removed from each other for you to have a satisfying experience. But it's never as simple as &quot;you're missing the point&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:24:35-07:00","id":907672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907586#post907586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issues with games usually revolve around built in restrictions on whether or not you can play certain groups. The most prominent example being Beast having totally unplayable heroes. I do get that there are word limits preventing the groups from being included (like the pure tribes in WtF 2e), but when situations come around like Beast going &quot;no, you don't get to play these people&quot; it ticks me off. Anytime a gameline tries to tell me I can't play an antagonist and it doesn't have incredibly compelling reason (like angels in demon or true fae in changeling) I tend to try and find my way around it with homerules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I totally understand that.<br /> Not being able to play an antagonist is complicated. At least give proper importance to them, as is given to the player characters<br /> In my case my problem is the fact that the three pure tribes are not available in the first chapter and poorly described in prey chapter. I know probably they didnt have the word count to put them there, but the first thing you ask yourself when you finish reading 1st or 2ed book is: <i>But what kind of stories I do? Ok the characters are done, the pack is done, the territory is ok, Now what?&quot;</i> Its a good thing being a tool kit, but for me a clear direction is what motivates new players to read more and love the game. They want to see the exemples they have read in action, if there are none what they should expect?<br /> Many people I saw always end up questioning: <i>&quot;But why should we play Werewolf for the sake of being a werewolf? I dont understand the main antagonist, what are we fighting for? </i><br /> <br /> <b>Forsaken will always be my favorite</b>, but I understand how many players end preferring the apocalypse or masquerade for easy understanding the cosmology and antagonists.<br /> <br /> <i><b>tl;dr The game should give more examples of how using the antagonists and how they can be as interesting as the player characters.</b></i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>;n907586</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Ever notice how <b>all the Forsaken art</b> has Uratha running about doing not fighty things in Gauru? As a person who is a strongly visual thinker this bothers me a lot. </i>&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My god in the Pack book this bothered me like hell. The art often do not match the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","user":"magisanctum","date":". 06-05-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T10:06:21-07:00","id":907696,"title":"","content":"The thing about Forsaken in Gauru form and artwork vs gameplay is sort of an interesting problem. Gauru form tends to be over represented in art because its an easy shorthand to illustrate that the game is about werewolves and you are looking at a werewolf doing a thing. The restrictions on Gauru form in gameplay comes from Werewolf the Apocalypse in CWoD, not as a holdover though like other weird baggage that has mostly been excised but rather as a reaction against the abuse of Crinos form in that game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T10:19:07-07:00","id":907704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907696#post907696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Forsaken in Gauru form and artwork vs gameplay is sort of an interesting problem. Gauru form tends to be over represented in art because its an easy shorthand to illustrate that the game is about werewolves and you are looking at a werewolf doing a thing. The restrictions on Gauru form in gameplay comes from Werewolf the Apocalypse in CWoD, not as a holdover though like other weird baggage that has mostly been excised but rather as a reaction against the abuse of Crinos form in that game line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The artists should know that they are not drawing for apocalypse. Or at least the writers should advise them -Hey the werewolf form you become a killing machine, you cannot make tea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T10:46:47-07:00","id":907724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907672#post907672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I totally understand that.<br /> Not being able to play an antagonist is complicated. At least give proper importance to them, as is given to the player characters<br /> In my case my problem is the fact that the three pure tribes are not available in the first chapter and poorly described in prey chapter. I know probably they didnt have the word count to put them there, but the first thing you ask yourself when you finish reading 1st or 2ed book is: <i>But what kind of stories I do? Ok the characters are done, the pack is done, the territory is ok, Now what?&quot;</i> Its a good thing being a tool kit, but for me a clear direction is what motivates new players to read more and love the game. They want to see the exemples they have read in action, if there are none what they should expect?<br /> Many people I saw always end up questioning: <i>&quot;But why should we play Werewolf for the sake of being a werewolf? I dont understand the main antagonist, what are we fighting for? </i><br /> <br /> <b>Forsaken will always be my favorite</b>, but I understand how many players end preferring the apocalypse or masquerade for easy understanding the cosmology and antagonists.<br /> <br /> <i><b>tl;dr The game should give more examples of how using the antagonists and how they can be as interesting as the player characters.</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> My god in the Pack book this bothered me like hell. The art often do not match the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get that a lot (forsaken is tied with awakening for my favourite gameline), I was actually intending to include the pure tribes and their 2e treatment in my comment (afterall I was very disappointed with how they were represented in the core), but I felt it detracted from my point and for a different reason to what you seem to wish they were given more treatment for. My view is there's a difference between &quot;you can't play these groups / this group&quot; and &quot;we didn't devote the word-count to these groups / this group&quot;, I am far far far (would four 'far's be too much here?) more bothered by the attitude of &quot;you shouldn't want to play these so you don't get the rules to do so&quot; which can be implied from the former, compared to &quot;we prefer you play these people so they're the ones we devoted more space to&quot; as is implied from the latter. I am fine with an antagonist being non-playable, if it has a really compelling reason such as being incredibly inhuman, like an angel or strix, otherwise it's going to bother me that the books are trying to prevent me from playing a story focusing on the antagonists with the presented mechanics. I won't go into much more detail on my feelings on that topic here though, as I doubt I'll bring anything new to the table on the topic, I don't want to derail this thread, and knowing me I'll wind up on an unproductive rant about the presentation of heroes in beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T10:51:41-07:00","id":907727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907696#post907696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Forsaken in Gauru form and artwork vs gameplay is sort of an interesting problem. Gauru form tends to be over represented in art because its an easy shorthand to illustrate that the game is about werewolves and you are looking at a werewolf doing a thing. The restrictions on Gauru form in gameplay comes from Werewolf the Apocalypse in CWoD, not as a holdover though like other weird baggage that has mostly been excised but rather as a reaction against the abuse of Crinos form in that game line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find that a bit annoying myself, I would love to see forsaken art give a larger focus on the other 4 forms (especially urshul, I mean, who wouldn't want to see a wolf the size of a horse in artwork?) and give gauru the same sort of reverence the uratha do, that is, rarely using it except when necessary and appropriate for the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T11:44:42-07:00","id":907768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907727#post907727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I find that a bit annoying myself, I would love to see forsaken art give a larger focus on the other 4 forms (especially urshul, I mean, who wouldn't want to see a wolf the size of a horse in artwork?) and give gauru the same sort of reverence the uratha do, that is, rarely using it except when necessary and appropriate for the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! until today I find it extremely hard to imagine the actual size of Urshul.<br /> The big problem with the art of<i>&quot;Gauru drinking tea&quot; is</i> that makes you think somehow you can remain controlled in this form. The first time I started reading Forsaken long time ago I remember to this day that I searched looking for a way to maintain control in Gauru, ofcourse at the end frustratingly I did not found anything about it.<br /> Misleading arts can be a very very bad influence for new players who want to understand the game as a whole, where he will seek visual references for the mechanics except in the book? For our hobbie that is all about imagination this can ruin the life of a player or a GM.<br /> <br /> Note: There are many arts of werewolves running along with apparently magaths. Until recently i've been understanding wrongly what is a magath and WHY they are bad company. <i>I had to redesign the totem's pack with a game in progress.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","user":"magisanctum","date":". 06-05-2016, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T11:59:24-07:00","id":907778,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that in 2e, there IS a way to maintain control in Gauru. Or at least hold the form and do other things other than combat. The Father's Form Gift works fine, and there's plenty of reason to use that Gift if you've invested in merits to boost a specific form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-05-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T12:57:09-07:00","id":907811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907672#post907672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My god in the Pack book this bothered me like hell. The art often do not match the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Father's Form is a thing nowadays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:37:24-07:00","id":907890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A trend? Phenomeon? You make it sound like its some passing fad or inexplicable thing. People changing games and houseruling them have happened since pretty much the dawn of time. Sports, board games, card games, video games, you name it. And, given the CofD's subjective nature as a storytelling game instead of a minitures-based war game, this comes off as more lore changes than just mechanics changes. And remember - house rules and hacks are critical to game lines. Hell. I remember, not long before Armory Reloaded came out, there was a thread about what houserules people use. Myself and a few others posted that we turned vampire's bullet-bashing feature to general everything-to-bashing. That ended up as one of the hacks in that book. And now? Its part of 2e core assumptions about vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I'm talking about, though. I'll grant that, technically, every house rule is about \u201cchanging something I don't like\u201d; but there's a difference between \u201cnot liking\u201d the fact that vampires only converted bullet damage to Bashing and not liking the fact that Werewolf makes heavy use of the Hisil and its denizens. (I choose this example because I'm a fan of hacks that allow you to downplay or even remove spirits from a Werewolf game; it's not about such a hack being inherently <i>bad</i>. But I <i>do</i> understand why most WtF fans think it's missing the point.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are games. They're written so people have <i>fun</i> with them above all else. Some people don't want to sit down and have deep introspection - they want to blow off steam after a stressful week of work by immersing themselves in a fantasy. And that's cool. And, for the people who say &quot;If you don't like a game, then play something else?&quot; I'm going to paraphrase Anita Sarkeesian for a moment - its okay to like aspects of a game but be criticial of other aspects. You might like one aspect of a game (delving into base emotions ala Vampire) without other aspects (sex metaphor). And that's fine - you can make the game what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And ironically, most \u201cmissing the point\u201d arguments I've seen lately <i>start out with</i> \u201cof course, you're free to do whstever you want; but there's why X is a bad idea/something I'd never do\u201d. EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907615#post907615\">what Charlaquin said</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well? Trying to reduce everything to an \u201cUs versus Them\u201d binary system is problematic. You simply cannot put people into two separate camps and expect it to be anything approaching realisticthe</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Good thing I wasn't trying to do that. But thanks for clarifying that point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a general trend across ALL CofD games that there are people who are less interested in the moral aspects of the games (and, yes, there are aesops in every game; they are designed to provoke thought) and want to do &quot;superheroes with fangs.&quot; Remove Humanity and Touchstones in vampire, downplay the balance-your-territory aspects in werewolf, the insanity and abuse aspects of Changeling, and more. Some players want to play monsters without the soul searching. Everyone is different, and expecting all these issues to resonate with everyone is an exercise doomed to failure. I honestly think that the alternative-Dawn crowd are the result of this mindset - they're interested in playing the game for fun without the soul searching, and the New Dawn kind of means their fun must come to an end at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know of a few who would disagree with that characterization. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the above mentality to an extreme, and we end up with the \u201chero splat\u201d crowd. People that want the CofD to include elements of Good versus Evil, much like most fantasy games out there. There's been focus on a lot of different ways to do this, but generally, we end up with flame wars as someone or another ends up insulting things that people like while arguing about the fact we don't have a good definition of Good to use as a basis (usually people end up with some variation on Western / Christian values as the default, which is what sparks the controversy).</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In MtAw, there's a lot of gripes about mechanics. Infinite powers means infinite potential for abuse, with little in the way of drawbacks or penalties, and the antagonism towards crossover. There's also a number of people that dislike the firm establishment of the Seers as permanent evil force (anti-hero splat philosophy).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cMages don't have enough downsides\u201d and \u201cthe Seers aren't nuanced enough\u201d. Gotcha. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, your bit about \u201cmagic user concepts the game isn't desgined to support?\u201d That is more of a question of cultural magics - MtAw <i>culture</i> is firmly Western, and claiming that they're global means we have issues of cultural imperialism and appropriation to the point of being insensitive about other cultures and their mystical traditions. Its the same complaints about Mummy - one Mediteranian culture to rule them all. 2e has gotten slightly better, but overtones remain, and time will tell if the problem was fixed or remains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I was thinking of some posts lately along the lines of \u201c[insert fantasy setting here] features magic users, so Mage should support that.\u201d Dresden Files and Harry Potter are the most well known, but not the only ones. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Promethean, another issue that comes up is that the game is that, despite inclusion of Galatea, Tammuz, and more, the game is fundamentally based entirely on Frankenstein, to the point that everyone is made from corpses and \u201cFire Bad!\u201d Why does it make sense for a marble statue with an affinity for the divine wind to be weak to flames? Another issue was how, in 1e, you were actively discouraged from playing two members of the same Lineage in a throng. Why tell a group what they can or can't play?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the former point, I've not only seen such posts; I personally tend to agree with them: during the Open Development of 2e, I argued for incorporating something like 1e's Constructs option into the core. That said, this isn't whether or not I like any given hack; just, which ones tend to give rise to \u201cmissing the point\u201d reactions, deservedly or not. On the latter point, I haven't seen what you're talking about. At the risk of derailing the thread, how did 1e actively discourage you from playing two members of the same Lineage in a throng?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907585#post907585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast has had issues from before the game was even released. Being natural sadists and harming people, unflattering depiction of heroes, people having trouble grasping the idea behind a \u201ccrossover focused game,\u201d the nature of the Horror, and more. Possibly one of the most problematic games to come out. Then, there's complaints of power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. I'll grant that what I know of the game comes from its early development; I never stuck around enough to buy the final product. But now tha you mention it, I <i>do</i> recall a number of fans preferring the first draft notions over the revisions that were made, to the point that they intended to house-rule the first draft stuff back in. Yeah, I think that qualifies, in an odd sort of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-05-2016, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:54:48-07:00","id":907900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907724#post907724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I get that a lot (forsaken is tied with awakening for my favourite gameline), I was actually intending to include the pure tribes and their 2e treatment in my comment (afterall I was very disappointed with how they were represented in the core), but I felt it detracted from my point and for a different reason to what you seem to wish they were given more treatment for. My view is there's a difference between \u201cyou can't play these groups / this group\u201d and \u201cwe didn't devote the word-count to these groups / this group\u201d, I am far far far (would four 'far's be too much here?) more bothered by the attitude of \u201cyou shouldn't want to play these so you don't get the rules to do so\u201d which can be implied from the former, compared to \u201cwe prefer you play these people so they're the ones we devoted more space to\u201d as is implied from the latter. I am fine with an antagonist being non-playable, if it has a really compelling reason such as being incredibly inhuman, like an angel or strix, otherwise it's going to bother me that the books are trying to prevent me from playing a story focusing on the antagonists with the presented mechanics. I won't go into much more detail on my feelings on that topic here though, as I doubt I'll bring anything new to the table on the topic, I don't want to derail this thread, and knowing me I'll wind up on an unproductive rant about the presentation of heroes in beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, thanks for bringing it up; it shows up a lot: as you mentioned, Werewolf's Pure; but also Mage's Seers, Promethean's alchemists, and Beast's Heroes. Again, I'm not advocating for or against any of these; but there <i>are</i> factions in each gameline's fanbase that get rankled that these antagonists aren't available to players, and counter-factions who argue that making them playable would run counter to the intent of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:05:45-07:00","id":907906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907778#post907778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that in 2e, there IS a way to maintain control in Gauru. Or at least hold the form and do other things other than combat. The Father's Form Gift works fine, and there's plenty of reason to use that Gift if you've invested in merits to boost a specific form.</div> </div> </div> </div>True; but \u201cdrinking tea in Gauru form\u201d doesn't strike me as the sort of thing the Gift was designed for. I'll grant that the Gift makes the various \u201cnon-violent Gauru\u201d illustrations <i>plausible</i>; but there's still merit to the argument that the sheer number of such illustrations gives a misleading impression of the game. <br /> <br /> That said, I think this qualifies as topic drift. This isn't a general \u201cwhat I don't like about gameline X\u201d; it's specifically about dislikes that lead to rules hacks which then trigger a \u201cmissing the point\u201d reaction from other fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:17:15-07:00","id":907922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907557#post907557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> \u2014 rather than \u201cif you don't like it, go away\u201d, I prefer \u201cif you don't have anything constructive to say, don't say anything\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quick followup to this: as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> pointed out, sometimes a \u201cyou're missing the point\u201d post <i>is</i> an attempt to be constructive, by trying to convey what the original intent was. And yes, sometimes it's just threadcrapping. <br /> <br /> And\u2026 back to work. See you in the morning![/QUOTE]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:05:59-07:00","id":907953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907890#post907890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll grant that, technically, every house rule is about \u201cchanging something I don't like\u201d; but there's a difference between \u201cnot liking\u201d the fact that vampires only converted bullet damage to Bashing and not liking the fact that Werewolf makes heavy use of the Hisil and its denizens. (I choose this example because I'm a fan of hacks that allow you to downplay or even remove spirits from a Werewolf game; it's not about such a hack being inherently <i>bad</i>. But I <i>do</i> understand why most WtF fans think it's missing the point.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Except... not really. Its only a question on how much work you'll be putting into the game to make the hack work, and if the hack will be fun for the people playing with said hacks. There may come a point where its not worth the trade off, and may be beyond the skill of the people in question, but it is entirely a subjective matter that depends on the individuals involved.<br /> <br /> Even in the case of removing the Hisil, the &quot;point&quot; of the game is entirely subjective. The only two points that are consistant across the CofD games, as far as I can tell, are 1) provoke thought on social issues, and 2) have fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True. And ironically, most \u201cmissing the point\u201d arguments I've seen lately <i>start out with</i> \u201cof course, you're free to do whstever you want; but there's why X is a bad idea/something I'd never do\u201d. </div> </div> </div> I don't think you should be telling someone that their ideas or bad or why you wouldn't do it, but rather just say &quot;not for me&quot; and avoid the thread. Its one thing to give a critical analysis and break things down on why they might go wrong; that's constructive criticism, and generally a good thing. Its another to just say you would never do something or its bad. The latter is just threadcrapping and potentially be kind of intimidating to new people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah. Good thing I wasn't trying to do that. But thanks for clarifying that point. </div> </div> </div> But you kinda did. The first post you mention sides. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907482#post907482\">Take a look at Post number 5 as well. </a> You are talking about &quot;sides.&quot; Any time you reduce people to binary groups, or try to polarize things into groups, it just creates misunderstandings and mischaracterizations. It may be a trick the brain uses to process information easier, but its not entirely accurate either.<br /> <br /> You might not even realize you are doing it, but that's exactly what you are doing as soon as you try to put people into &quot;sides.&quot; Life is a spectrum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know of a few who would disagree with that characterization. </div> </div> </div> In case it needs to be said, this is all my opinion. I fully expect people to disagree. Not quite sure why its noteworthy, but whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cMages don't have enough downsides\u201d and \u201cthe Seers aren't nuanced enough\u201d. Gotcha. </div> </div> </div> Not just downsides that are lacking. Its that their magic is sickenly powerful, one shot kills to the point only another mage with the proper shielding or an ephemeral with sickenly large Resistance stat can match. Its that the mages don't come off as monsters, even with the promise that they are. One of the most annoying things I feel about mages is that they're not even valid targets for Hunters to go after. Its like they're in their own little world. For those who like crossover games, mage is all but outright incompatable.<br /> <br /> I could go on, but I've recently come to the conclusion that 2e Mage simply has too much in it that doesn't work for what I want, and will not be investing in the game at anymore, nor posting on that forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, I was thinking of some posts lately along the lines of \u201c[insert fantasy setting here] features magic users, so Mage should support that.\u201d Dresden Files and Harry Potter are the most well known, but not the only ones. </div> </div> </div> *shrugs* Dresden and Potter are actually highly doable. Those two are more of a question of the settings and the tiny details not matching up, rather than the magic. Its like throwing Dresden into Potterverse and suddenly expecting the detective to be able to still do things exactly the same. You can see where that would be an issue. <i> &quot;What do you mean children are given time magics and they're not ravening psychopaths out to detroy the world?!?!?&quot; </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the risk of derailing the thread, how did 1e actively discourage you from playing two members of the same Lineage in a throng? </div> </div> </div>In general, having two or more of the same Lineage spread Disquiet faster, leading to pressure to avoid that at all cost. It felt restrictive in concept for a number of people. Mind you, it wasn't a problem most of the time, but it was one I noticed come up a few times at the start. That was years ago, though, so I imagine people simply adapted to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907906#post907906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True; but \u201cdrinking tea in Gauru form\u201d doesn't strike me as the sort of thing the Gift was designed for.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I think that tea drinking is exactly what this is meant to do. Tea drinking, and pretty much any other kind of everyday stuff, including watching movies, give your kids back rides while holding onto their legs so they don't fall off, etc.<br /> <br /> What else would it be for? Certainly not combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-05-2016, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:33:11-07:00","id":907964,"title":"","content":"Controversial tittle aside, MCN does an excellent job summarizing the issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:36:40-07:00","id":907966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907906#post907906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True; but \u201cdrinking tea in Gauru form\u201d doesn't strike me as the sort of thing the Gift was designed for. I'll grant that the Gift makes the various \u201cnon-violent Gauru\u201d illustrations <i>plausible</i>; but there's still merit to the argument that the sheer number of such illustrations gives a misleading impression of the game.<br /> <br /> That said, I think this qualifies as topic drift. This isn't a general \u201cwhat I don't like about gameline X\u201d; it's specifically about dislikes that lead to rules hacks which then trigger a \u201cmissing the point\u201d reaction from other fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this particular topic? Even with Father's Form, there's Breaking Points implied in taking the Killing Form without any intent to kill whatsoever.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:43:24-07:00","id":907974,"title":"","content":"I appreciate that the gauru form is probably the more recognizable werewolf one, but yeah as a reader looking at these pictures and seeing a gauru form werewolf with a bunch of people makes me think they're going to just start slaughtering them, despite the intent of the art being otherwise. Enjoyed the picture on p60, however. Most of Forsaken's art lacks bloodshed and even overt violence. I was commenting to my wife, after seeing a picture of an alligator that ate another alligator, that it would be interesting to see something like that in the book, a massive wolf with half of a werewolf hanging out of its mouth.<br /> <br /> Father's Form seemed to have been a nod to people who wanted to be able to lounge around and drink tea or have sex in gauru form. There doesn't seem to be a particular in-game intent for you to do anything with it other than be in gauru and not have the Rage associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T05:06:03-07:00","id":908267,"title":"","content":"I'm laughing so hard with everybody using the term &quot;drinking tea gauru&quot; that I found an werewolf using father's form AND drinking tea.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://img03.deviantart.net/599e/i/2006/228/c/6/werewolf_drinking_tea_by_tabery_kyou.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://img03.deviantart.net/599e/i/2006/228/c/6/werewolf_drinking_tea_by_tabery_kyou.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://img03.deviantart.net/599e/i/2006/228/c/6/werewolf_drinking_tea_by_tabery_kyou.png\" target=\"_blank\"> http://img03.deviantart.net/599e/i/2006/228/c/6/werewolf_drinking_tea_by_tabery_kyou.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T05:14:33-07:00","id":908270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907974#post907974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Father's Form seemed to have been a nod to people who wanted to be able to lounge around and drink tea or have sex in gauru form. There doesn't seem to be a particular in-game intent for you to do anything with it other than be in gauru and not have the Rage associated with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or I don't know. Binding spirits into circles and fetishes with rites that rely on the Strength attribute. Or attempt to inflict a Tell on a human, with another rite, and not end up outright killing him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T22:11:45-07:00","id":908886,"title":"","content":"I will admit I have different issues with different rules. The new social maneuvering rules frustrate me the most because First impressions don't make sense. Time constraints usually have nothing at all to do with how much someone likes you unless it's some sort of court situation and you are going for long term political issues. Otherwise time constraints have usually no bearing on anything but tertiary factors. Also using all or nothing is bad because that isn't how it works at all and forces the players to actually lose rp nuance. Every other game out there recognizes that the time between rolls should take into account what you are doing. Courting? Long, trying to convince someone you have a mutually beneficial plan? hours to minutes. But by the new social rules, if the girl likes me enough I can charm her in seconds and it may take me weeks to convince my rivals to team up against an immediate threat. it just doesn't make any sense and requires hacking from the get go. Or losing all the appeal of a social system by making anything important an all or nothing rll even if it makes no sense with the characters.<br /> <br /> Mage; like others, I found the paths too generic, unlike the other core &quot;types&quot; it only implied to have anything to do with your character. Being an Irraka, Ventrue, Galatean, Torn, ect said more about you as a character than a Moros. Add in that in general if you rejected Atlantis there isn't much story or creative vibrancy built into the setting. Mages are just powerful and have less of an inbuilt struggle or drive. WereWolves hunt, Vamps feed, Prom create ruin and seek humanity, even Sin Eaters have at least a mechanical pull to interfere with ghosts. Add in that NPC mages are the most likely to be described as leading normalish lives and they seem at a weird angle for the rest of the setting. Mage is about Awesome people doing Awesome things. Nothing wrong with that but the setting seems to have a less dramatic pull. Add in that, like above, Hermetic magic is just so limiting and seems a needless hindrance when it would be simple to use the paths as different magical types instead. <br /> <br /> Werewolf- The new Harmony is weird for me, I love it and hate it. Storywise and how the mechanics effect things like changing/Karuth I love but the actual Breaking points don't really seem to work. Killing a human is a breaking point despite it saying in other places that Werewolves don't need to concern themselves with Human safety unless it is their pack, but killing a Werewolf isn't? Or are they saying killing a werewolf is a deliberate break from the oath of the Moon with a -2 penalty and ignoring the new change to murder? So Iron Masters and BloodTalons are doomed spiritually speaking? Killing a pack of Pure and now Huge mechanical penalties are in place and just seems to not be a natural progress of things. Also how they mechanically balance against each other. Personally, if the ST is trusted I feel it is a better game to have the ST judge what is a breaking point for each player as that seems more fair and makes sense in world and out with the story. <br /> <br /> Just really want a dramatic world but the rules need to work with that world and lend it credibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T22:30:43-07:00","id":908891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=908886#post908886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage; like others, I found the paths too generic, unlike the other core &quot;types&quot; it only implied to have anything to do with your character. Being an Irraka, Ventrue, Galatean, Torn, ect said more about you as a character than a Moros.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the opposite, I mean, at least moros is meant to reflect a part of you. Torn, ventrue, and galatean have nothing to do with your personality at all, they're things that happen to you, and even Irraka might not make any sense for a character that has been it as there auspice (the books admit that sometimes even auspice does not necessarily fit the werewolf but the persons is still expected to do there role even if they aren't any good at that thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T23:46:36-07:00","id":908933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=908891#post908891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the opposite, I mean, at least moros is meant to reflect a part of you. Torn, ventrue, and galatean have nothing to do with your personality at all, they're things that happen to you, and even Irraka might not make any sense for a character that has been it as there auspice (the books admit that sometimes even auspice does not necessarily fit the werewolf but the persons is still expected to do there role even if they aren't any good at that thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that and agree with you except for Galatean but personally, it felt like, story speaking, it offers little to the character as customization or input. An Irraka is the clever hunter who is expected to use their wits and stealth. A Ventrue has the inhumanity and social aspects while also feeding into the type of vampire from Dracula Lore. A Galatean I will disagree about and say that is your entire being starting out and does say a lot about personality (humours) and how you react. Moros means you learned Death and Matter, this could mean you are moody or getting into the Hades Motif, or you were close to Death, or you awakened when you nearly died or it could mean you Awakened and that is where you went with no clear reason why. An irraka in play who is a bad Irraka or doesn't fit is a story because of expectations and there are many stories to be had growing into a role or bucking how someone may believe you should fit it. But a Moros who is flighty might be thought as weird but not much else. A Moros doesn't have a social expectation, a type of background, or a sense of history. If he starts with Death and Matter he's a Moros no other element need apply. In some ways it doesn't even add anything unique just a jumpstart with Arcana which are open to all paths.<br /> <br /> Take Fairest in Changeling. A Draconic, a flowering, and a bright one could be wildly different from durance, personality, outlook, and history, but they all imply superiority and beauty. Instead of just giving them starting powers everyone can have, they give them negatives and positives that are unique to them and giving a mechanical and dramatic flair. It implies more about the character and gives the player more hooks into the story. I feel like every Core book does that except Mage. With the paths being based on the main Mechanics it also is the most limiting. Most choose their path often entirely on not the idea or how cool it sounds, or party roles, but what spells you want. Just how often I see new players pick their roles. &quot;I want to be a Life/Death Mage so Thrysus or Moros well i like Matter more than spirit so Moros!&quot; But introduce Changeling and someone comes up with a Beast &quot;Card Shark&quot; which informs them what type of character/history with their imaginations being tickled and the mechanics not being how they view the thing as a whole.<br /> <br /> The others color style of play and add customization to character Mechanically and storywise but Moros mostly seems to just say what your main powers are, a huge Mechanical effect, but not much color on the drama","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T00:08:02-07:00","id":908947,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11938\" data-vbnamecard=\"11938\">3Comrades</a>, have you actually read the Path descriptions? Because it sounds like you are wildly misinformed about Paths and what they represent in the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T00:54:56-07:00","id":908966,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I have but that is all based on 1st ed haven't gotten 2nd ed yet. I've played 2 games and ran a third and know it really well. Astral Realms is one of my favorite supplemental books, but I have no idea how 2nd ed might have changed it and actually really excited and hopeful for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T01:07:48-07:00","id":908974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=908886#post908886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will admit I have different issues with different rules. The new social maneuvering rules frustrate me the most because First impressions don't make sense. Time constraints usually have nothing at all to do with how much someone likes you unless it's some sort of court situation and you are going for long term political issues. Otherwise time constraints have usually no bearing on anything but tertiary factors. Also using all or nothing is bad because that isn't how it works at all and forces the players to actually lose rp nuance. Every other game out there recognizes that the time between rolls should take into account what you are doing. Courting? Long, trying to convince someone you have a mutually beneficial plan? hours to minutes. But by the new social rules, if the girl likes me enough I can charm her in seconds and it may take me weeks to convince my rivals to team up against an immediate threat. it just doesn't make any sense and requires hacking from the get go. Or losing all the appeal of a social system by making anything important an all or nothing rll even if it makes no sense with the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Social Manuevering rules are badly explained. A lot of people have struggled to use them well, because they don't quite understand the frame to hang them on.<br /> <br /> The most common mistake people make is to assume that they're a complete replacement for all social actions. They're not. If you don't have time to do Social Manuevering, then you don't use Social Manuevering. If you're expecting a multi-stage process that takes a long time, you should actually consider doing multiple runs of Social Manuevering, probably interspersed with a lot of simple one-shot rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T01:23:39-07:00","id":908982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=908974#post908974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Social Manuevering rules are badly explained. A lot of people have struggled to use them well, because they don't quite understand the frame to hang them on.<br /> <br /> The most common mistake people make is to assume that they're a complete replacement for all social actions. They're not. If you don't have time to do Social Manuevering, then you don't use Social Manuevering. If you're expecting a multi-stage process that takes a long time, you should actually consider doing multiple runs of Social Manuevering, probably interspersed with a lot of simple one-shot rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels like it with some of the 2nd ed cores. If players can pick powers exclusively dealing with the system and a good chunk of powers available mention social maneuvering, I feel forced to use it and figure out a way to make it work. I can't rule out swaths of powers available, so i have to figure out how to apply social maneuvering to mean something while ignoring the weird time constraints of first impressions. So I feel forced to homebrew out the gate.<br /> <br /> The time constraints make each roll matter, but they don't make sense in most situations. Maybe limit how many rolls they can do based on impression?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T02:32:18-07:00","id":908999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907906#post907906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True; but \u201cdrinking tea in Gauru form\u201d doesn't strike me as the sort of thing the Gift was designed for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact. My art notes for <i>Fathers Form</i> was a couple of Uratha in Gauru form sitting on the couch, playing some kind of game console, sharing a pizza and having a few beers. Because fuck it, they *could*.<br /> <br /> (I was overruled <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T02:36:41-07:00","id":909002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907974#post907974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Father's Form seemed to have been a nod to people who wanted to be able to lounge around and drink tea or have sex in gauru form. There doesn't seem to be a particular in-game intent for you to do anything with it other than be in gauru and not have the Rage associated with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rites. Pack Tactics themes, Intimidation, Communing with your Uratha nature.<br /> <br /> Depending on the type of game, <i>Father's Form</i> has a lot of potential uses. But it's primary intent is to give people the option if they want it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:46:21-07:00","id":909043,"title":"","content":"Beast: Some of us want Beasts or Beast like beings for other primal emotions then fear.<br /> <br /> Mage: I wouldn't mind the horror elements being played up after signs of sorcery. Like maybe a book on the consquences of various spells and other assorted magic.<br /> <br /> Vampire: I people have asked for various changes to blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: it actually more changing breeds, but many didn't like the eco warrior theme amoung other issues.<br /> <br /> Mummy: I wish it had been 2e instead of 1e<br /> <br /> Demon: Alot of people found it too matrixy. Personally I would have prefered possessed done up for 2e, but Demon does have its cool elements.<br /> <br /> Giest: I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Changeling: None cruel True Fae, aka nice True Fae. I do think this is easier in 2e, because you have the Loyalist Seeming,so you can play a nice Loyalist of a nice Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T09:08:38-07:00","id":909209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=908982#post908982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It feels like it with some of the 2nd ed cores. If players can pick powers exclusively dealing with the system and a good chunk of powers available mention social maneuvering, I feel forced to use it and figure out a way to make it work. I can't rule out swaths of powers available, so i have to figure out how to apply social maneuvering to mean something while ignoring the weird time constraints of first impressions. So I feel forced to homebrew out the gate.<br /> <br /> The time constraints make each roll matter, but they don't make sense in most situations. Maybe limit how many rolls they can do based on impression?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you heard me at all.<br /> <br /> The system <i>does</i> work. The problem is that you're trying to apply it to situations where it's not applicable. If the time constraints don't make sense, chances are very strong that you're misusing the system. But as I said, it's poorly explained, so I wouldn't say that that's your fault: it's a tool in the toolbox but it's really hard to tell how to use it.<br /> <br /> I mean, here's another thing: the time constraints aren't on permission for you to take actions. They're on the speed at which you progress. You can take lots of actions in between opening Doors; they just won't open any Doors. You can also force Doors, which changes the pacing of the system entirely, and is actually what you want to be doing in a lot of situations.<br /> <br /> If I find the time, I'll try to write up something more comprehensive to explain how I think it should be used. But I've been pretty short on time lately, so it would be lovely if someone else chimed in on this first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:43:51-07:00","id":909330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=909043#post909043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire: I people have asked for various changes to blood sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on that? Blood Sorcery is just a class of Discipline that only uses ritual effects instead of powers at each level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mummy: I wish it had been 2e instead of 1e </div> </div> </div>That's... not really a change? I'm pretty sure we'll get a 2e version at some point anyway. It's just unclear if it will be more like <i>Mortal Remains</i> or a full new core book. It doesn't seem like it needs the kind of changes we're seeing so far to justify a brand new line compared to just updating the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon: Alot of people found it too matrixy. Personally I would have prefered possessed done up for 2e, but Demon does have its cool elements. </div> </div> </div>Demon is 2e... it just was released before they were doing full core books for 2e game-lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changeling: None cruel True Fae, aka nice True Fae. I do think this is easier in 2e, because you have the Loyalist Seeming,so you can play a nice Loyalist of a nice Fae. </div> </div> </div>Not trying to get into &quot;that's missing the point,&quot; but True Fae aren't cruel or nice by default. They're inhuman. The clash of their inhuman motivations and a changeling's human reactions are inevitably going to turn into a negative experience (at least for PCs, otherwise why would they leave?). A &quot;cruel&quot; True Fae can provide a &quot;nice&quot; experience (I had a ST that had a rather mean True Fae with an adamant Loyalist follower because the Durance had helped the Loyalist kick their drug addiction and find new purpose), and a &quot;nice&quot; True Fae can provide a &quot;cruel&quot; experience (a lot of the Fairest Durances are written this way in the books).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:58:03-07:00","id":909345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=909330#post909330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you elaborate on that? Blood Sorcery is just a class of Discipline that only uses ritual effects instead of powers at each level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if this is what the person you quoted meant, but it does remind me of something I often butt heads against. 2e blood magic is just broken. Not broken powerful or underpowered, as in that the mechanics simply don't work with the rituals as presented.<br /> <br /> Its a complete cluster to the point that you have to either 1) use the Themes in Blood Sorcery, which many dislike, or 2) houserule things to work different. Well, there's now option 3) use rituals in Secrets of the Covenant, which seems to fix the core book problems by using loopholes. I honestly don't know anyone that's not using one of those three things to cast these magics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-07-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T14:53:28-07:00","id":909505,"title":"","content":"The largest &quot;changing what you don't like things&quot; thing I've heard for Geist are &quot;Make it more like Wraith&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:38:35-07:00","id":909527,"title":"","content":"I get really profoundly irked by people that wanted Demon to be more traditional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:22:38-07:00","id":909567,"title":"","content":"I think I remember people suggesting Cruac not cost max humanity for example. There have been a variety of others I don't remember them all.<br /> <br /> What I meant by nice True Fae is are Gentry who are cruel on purpose or by accident, so I guess you could say Gentry with a measure of sanity.<br /> <br /> Like I said, this is more workable in 2e by said sane Gentry producing kind Loyalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:28:12-07:00","id":909574,"title":"","content":"And, by traditional, we invariably end up meaning &quot;Catholic-style.&quot; If we had Catholic style, we'd have people complaining about there being a dominant religion in the CofD. We go around, we get people who want the big G back. You simply can't win with this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:38:36-07:00","id":909584,"title":"","content":"The thing that gets my goat is that there are a fair number of the complaints which are based on a misunderstanding of the game. The folks that do that are often inventing a problem <b>for themselves</b> that isn't actually there because they're going off of their own half-remembered reading paired with the latest brilliant observation about <i>Chronicles of Darkness </i>out of 4chan.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should clarify, I'm not angry because &quot;they're getting it <i>wrong!</i>&quot; but because their issue is based on a misunderstanding, I just want to help them resolve that understanding so they can decide if they're cool with things or not as a person fully informed on whatever they're thinking about. If you don't like <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> because you didn't read it that closely the first time and someone on another website said something incorrect about it, I'd rather show you how that's not the case so you can decide, fully informed, whether you like it or not. At that point, do as you will.<br /> <br /> Though I feel that's a very different kind of disagreement from the one where people are saying that they, say, don't want Prometheans to become human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-07-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:47:44-07:00","id":909638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=909527#post909527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get really profoundly irked by people that wanted Demon to be more traditional.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's such a difficult complaint for me to wrap my head around, because when I read Demon I see a profoundly traditional fallen angel story with a coat of scifi paint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:41:37-07:00","id":909748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=909638#post909638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's such a difficult complaint for me to wrap my head around, because when I read Demon I see a profoundly traditional fallen angel story with a coat of scifi paint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. You Fall because, for whatever, reason, you can no longer serve a Creator that you view as flawed. It's powerful and nearly everywhere, but it makes mistakes. That's an incredibly relevant narrative.<br /> <br /> Beyond all that, The Matrix is how most people first discover Gnostic themes anyway, there's a severe lack of espionage RPGs on the market and precisely none of those are Gnostic espionage games, and if you want something dealing with a classic Biblical narrative you have both Demon: the Fallen and In Nomine, a pair of absolutely fantastic games that don't need to be retread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T23:05:08-07:00","id":909868,"title":"","content":"I like demon and the lack of Christian ties but not so fond of the God Machine itself. But that is entirely personal. It's a little too alien for me but I can see the appeal and think it was marvelously well thought out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:42:31-07:00","id":910136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=909574#post909574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, by traditional, we invariably end up meaning &amp;quot;Catholic-style.&amp;quot; If we had Catholic style, we'd have people complaining about there being a dominant religion in the CofD. We go around, we get people who want the big G back. You simply can't win with this one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly my preference would have been for niether Catholic or Godmachine, but rather an Expanded Inferno setting.<br /> <br /> The possessed were awesome, the various types of demons were awesome. Hell the side bar on Empyreans was awesome.<br /> <br /> But there was no religious prefernces in it, just possible choices.<br /> <br /> I still think 2e could be prime time to expand Inferno into its own gameline, perhaps after Deviant.<br /> <br /> And I don't see it stepping on Demon: The Descents toes at all, the themes are totally different, DtD avoided focusing on vice, and DtD's occult stuff is more weird science with occultish over tones, then Inferno Vice based magic.<br /> <br /> And DtD isn't the only setting with its own type of demons, Mage 2e as Daemons, including Wraith and Imps, has fiends from the lower depths, used to have Goetic demons back in 1e, Changeling 2e has Incubi, Succubi, Cambions, the Dearheart Darklings (basically the Succubi Kith), Giest has parts of the Underworld that are basically hells, with some of the inhabitant resembling demons, Werewolves have the Court of Indulgence and the even darker Maeljins, Vampire has its own demons, Duat is basically its own type of hell.<br /> <br /> So there is no reason they couldn't have Inferno: The Damned or Inferno: The Possessed.<br /> <br /> This isn't a shot at DtD, which is awesome at what it does, just a personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:45:32-07:00","id":910137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=909638#post909638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's such a difficult complaint for me to wrap my head around, because when I read Demon I see a profoundly traditional fallen angel story with a coat of scifi paint.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see it the exact opposite way, a sci fi story, with a coat of fallen angel/demon paint.<br /> <br /> Its still cool for all that, so I'm not trying to bash it, I just think it still leaves room for an Inferno line, sort of like getting to have your cake and eat it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:48:24-07:00","id":910141,"title":"","content":"Actually as Inferno demons aren't fallen angels, (although I can see them happily encouraging Godmachine Angels to fall into DtD demons), that's more conceptual room for a full fleshed out 2e, Inferno game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:06:15-07:00","id":910153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910136#post910136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly my preference would have been for niether Catholic or Godmachine, but rather an Expanded Inferno setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Inferno is also heavily set on the Catholic mindset of Vice / sin. Several books in 2e are already known for describing the Inferno as the Christian themed Hell. You can't get away from that here. Even if we're not dealing with fallen angels (the whole point of the Demon game lines), Inferno is still heavily Catholic inspired and tied into that religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:16:26-07:00","id":910166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910137#post910137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see it the exact opposite way, a sci fi story, with a coat of fallen angel/demon paint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is The Matrix the scifi story you think it looks like? Because that was a Gnostic Messiah story with The Machine as an allegory for the Demiurge.<br /> <br /> Besides that, all of the Fallen Angel aspects of DtD are inseparable from the game - falling from service to a higher power, gaining autonomy as a result, fighting or fleeing its remaining servants, bargaining for the souls of mortals, striving to create your own space free from the influence of the higher power, a false human visage and a true angelic form that becomes more and more demonic as your power grows, miracles that draw upon your memories of being an angel to access the rules that God put into place for its Angels to use, blasphemies that exploit those rules to produce greater and more powerful results at a cost... On the other hand, all of the scifi stuff can be changed without impacting the game. Drop the &quot;Machine&quot; from God-Machine, re-name the demonic form abilities, etc. there's a whole thread over on the DtD forums brainstorming more biblical names for everything, and they could all be used without impacting how the game is actually played.<br /> <br /> That's how you can tell what's the core of the story and what's the paint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910137#post910137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its still cool for all that, so I'm not trying to bash it, I just think it still leaves room for an Inferno line, sort of like getting to have your cake and eat it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it definitely leaves room for Inferno. Descent is about Fallen Angels, Inferno is about Demons. As much as Milton may have popularized the trend of conflating the two, there's still a significant divide between how a lot of people conceptualize each. Not only that, Descent is distinctly Gnostic, while Inferno is pretty much Agnostic. That also makes a huge difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T11:46:16-07:00","id":910221,"title":"","content":"Heh. I set up a topic a while back specifically for translating between DtF and Inferno, with an eye toward using elements of the former to leverage the latter into a full-on greater template existing side by side with DtD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:43:20-07:00","id":910292,"title":"","content":"I will add to problem with Gauru form in 1st is not just the art but the fluff too. When i first started reading Forsaken the fluff + art would sell me the &quot;apocalypse&quot; idea of the gauru form while the reality didnt.<br /> <br /> I specially recall a fluff piece of a Uratha woman about to give birth when a mage teleports into steal her baby because........because and she transform killing the baby and the text leave it pretty clear the Mage is death. Which is a pretty evocative piece in itself 6+ years since i read it and i still remember is proof enough but it doesnt hold up with the game mechanics. A mage with that level of space is gonna paint the walls with the Uratha.<br /> <br /> In my experiece, a chunk of the &quot;Lets hack this&quot; crowd also come from people feeling that disconnect between setting/fluff/mechanics. <br /> <br /> In the case of 2ed i see where lots of hack and whatnot come from because they are very oppressive games. Not in the same sense of OWoD setting. 2Ed sells you 1 type of game per splat and they run that kind of game very well (Retaining ones humanity for vamp, The hunt story for Werewolf....etc) but as soon as you want to do something else with it i found out quickly that is extremely difficult (example, unless the pack fix this i cannot see how one can run a heavy politic game in werewolf).<br /> <br /> This is not bad exactly. In OWoD you had to fight the system too but while it was a lesser fight you had to do it with everything you wanna play in it. So its kinda a screwdriver vs swiss army knife. The Swiss Army can do lots of stuff but noone particularly well while the Screwdriver can do 1 thing very well but one thing only.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:52:23-07:00","id":910301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910292#post910292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(example, unless the pack fix this i cannot see how one can run a heavy politic game in werewolf).</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't find the addition of protectorates does this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:53:15-07:00","id":910303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910292#post910292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of 2ed i see where lots of hack and whatnot come from because they are very oppressive games. Not in the same sense of OWoD setting. 2Ed sells you 1 type of game per splat and they run that kind of game very well (Retaining ones humanity for vamp, The hunt story for Werewolf....etc) but as soon as you want to do something else with it i found out quickly that is extremely difficult (example, unless the pack fix this i cannot see how one can run a heavy politic game in werewolf).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it does. Protectorates; sample packs that ditch the whole Alpha-Omega idea; Packs exclusively comprised of Wolfblooded, etc, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:16:59-07:00","id":910317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910292#post910292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, The hunt story for Werewolf....etc) but as soon as you want to do something else with it i found out quickly that is extremely difficult (example, unless the pack fix this i cannot see how one can run a heavy politic game in werewolf).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>For me this is the spirits who add a lot of political play. You don't want to constantly throw your weight around as a WW, need to keep on good terms with powerful spirits/gain gifts, and play the Spirit <i><b>Courts</b>. </i>Just saying, it's in built in the system to have a very political game, and why I feel the animist element is so important. The defining member of your pack (the totem) often joins for protective and political reasons. Elodoths are shown to naturally be political to aid their packs.<br /> <br /> Once the Hisil itself can be seen as a high stakes constant political battle for their lives/sustenance even the most violent of Spirits can be Politically swayed. Nearly every favor to even Talk to a spirit can employ Politics. Increase the influence of one over the other, use ties against them, put goals into motion in the physical world and even those who hate the Uratha will be inclined to help and to trade a favor or two, including keeping their own broods in line.<br /> <br /> It's completely possible to nearly run an almost pure political game, especially if you are playing the Fire Touched who like to convert their enemies and have a much more equal say with the spirits. Now that the Hunt doesn't just mean kill, you can have a very nuanced political play. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:21:03-07:00","id":910357,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910301#post910301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't find the addition of protectorates does this?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really. The book tell you that sometimes pack form together a protectorate to collectively hunt prey, they can be very organized and have tittles or not.....and thats it. No clue how to organize it.....how that works, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910317#post910317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me this is the spirits who add a lot of political play. You don't want to constantly throw your weight around as a WW, need to keep on good terms with powerful spirits/gain gifts, and play the Spirit <i><b>Courts</b>. </i>Just saying, it's in built in the system to have a very political game, and why I feel the animist element is so important. The defining member of your pack (the totem) often joins for protective and political reasons. Elodoths are shown to naturally be political to aid their packs.<br /> <br /> Once the Hisil itself can be seen as a high stakes constant political battle for their lives/sustenance even the most violent of Spirits can be Politically swayed. Nearly every favor to even Talk to a spirit can employ Politics. Increase the influence of one over the other, use ties against them, put goals into motion in the physical world and even those who hate the Uratha will be inclined to help and to trade a favor or two, including keeping their own broods in line.<br /> <br /> It's completely possible to nearly run an almost pure political game, especially if you are playing the Fire Touched who like to convert their enemies and have a much more equal say with the spirits. Now that the Hunt doesn't just mean kill, you can have a very nuanced political play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the same problem with protectorates. Its says spirits have ranks, it tells you they form courts but not how that courts works and how their politics function. Which is even worse because we are talking about Alien entities so their motivations and what they want is even more obscure.<br /> <br /> But the politics in werewolf is only an example. I talked to Vampire players about characters they just cant play because of the narrow definition of Humanity. Im reading mage 2ed and i find myself struggling to create NPCs whose motivations arent always &quot;obsession with mystery&quot; or that apparently every consilium needs a public mystery for the concilium to exist (which as side not, it kinda invalidates boston). So many werewolf powers are tie to the hunt, that running a story with the hunt in second plane is kind a shot in the kneecaps.<br /> <br /> The narrow focus is great for players because it gives you a clear statement of what you suppose to do but makes difficult to run other types of history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-08-2016, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:34:55-07:00","id":910371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> No, not really. The book tell you that sometimes pack form together a protectorate to collectively hunt prey, they can be very organized and have tittles or not.....and thats it. No clue how to organize it.....how that works, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book literally lists dozen of examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Thats the same problem with protectorates. Its says spirits have ranks, it tells you they form courts but not how that courts works and how their politics function. Which is even worse because we are talking about Alien entities so their motivations and what they want is even more obscure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits feed on essence, most of which is harvested from human-like activities. Bribery and politics isn't so hard to implement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> But the politics in werewolf is only an example. I talked to Vampire players about characters they just cant play because of the narrow definition of Humanity. Im reading mage 2ed and i find myself struggling to create NPCs whose motivations arent always &quot;obsession with mystery&quot; or that apparently every consilium needs a public mystery for the concilium to exist (which as side not, it kinda invalidates boston). So many werewolf powers are tie to the hunt, that running a story with the hunt in second plane is kind a shot in the kneecaps.<br /> <br /> The narrow focus is great for players because it gives you a clear statement of what you suppose to do but makes difficult to run other types of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess you are making a bunch of werewolves, vampires and mages, but aren't making enough persons out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T16:47:04-07:00","id":910403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNo, not really. The book tell you that sometimes pack form together a protectorate to collectively hunt prey, they can be very organized and have tittles or not.....and thats it. No clue how to organize it.....how that works, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because different protectorates are organized differently. Come up with something you think sounds cool and roll with it. It seems like you're trying to use the game's freeform nature as an example of why it's too restrictive, and that just doesn't follow logically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThats the same problem with protectorates. Its says spirits have ranks, it tells you they form courts but not how that courts works and how their politics function. Which is even worse because we are talking about Alien entities so their motivations and what they want is even more obscure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence. They want Essence. Specifically, Essence that resonates with their Influences. Spirits achieve higher Rank when they spread their Influence, thereby giving them easier access to more Essence. Lesser spirits flock to greater spirits with like Influences in hopes of feeding from the Essence generated by the environments the greater spirits' Influences cultivate. Greater spirits use lesser spirits as agents to help them further spread their Influences. Courts of spirits with opposing Influences compete for territory and resources. It's like, basic feudal politics and also spelled out in the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBut the politics in werewolf is only an example. I talked to Vampire players about characters they just cant play because of the narrow definition of Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to give me an example or two here, because this sounds less like &quot;the game won't let me play my concept&quot; and more like &quot;I don't want my character's actions to have consequences&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIm reading mage 2ed and i find myself struggling to create NPCs whose motivations arent always &quot;obsession with mystery&quot; or that apparently every consilium needs a public mystery for the concilium to exist (which as side not, it kinda invalidates boston).</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do things other than investigate Mysteries. Mysteries are a central part of the theme of the game, but they're not the only things Mages are ever motivated by.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo many werewolf powers are tie to the hunt, that running a story with the hunt in second plane is kind a shot in the kneecaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves frame most of what they do in terms of &quot;the hunt&quot;. They don't go shopping, they hunt for groceries. They don't apply for jobs, they hunt for employment. They don't go to war, they hunt their enemies. Werewolf powers being focused on the hunt is more a case of werewolves employing Texas sharpshooter fallacy on a grand scale than those powers actually being narrow in application.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe narrow focus is great for players because it gives you a clear statement of what you suppose to do but makes difficult to run other types of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by other types of history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:38:32-07:00","id":910492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910403#post910403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because different protectorates are organized differently. Come up with something you think sounds cool and roll with it. It seems like you're trying to use the game's freeform nature as an example of why it's too restrictive, and that just doesn't follow logically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sactum &amp; sigils is a bad book to get an idea of a concilium, it gives you lots of examples of how Concilium get elected, how concilium do justice, how concilium are compose. But what doesnt give you is how those options interact with each other.<br /> <br /> DaveB Broken diamond actual play is a good example of a concilium. It explains the same points of Sactum and sigil with the difference that instead of throwing empty examples with no correlation with each other it shows how each element interact witch each other. E<br /> <br /> Now does this mean That Broken diamonds concilium structure is the one true way? No, but at least it is A fully structure that i can begin with, understand and tweak. It is explained how and why it works and thus, when i wanna change that structure i know how removing something affect other things. Quoting you here<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907615#post907615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general opinion is, these game elements are designed with intentionality, and one should understand the intent of an element and the effect it has on the theme and mood of a game before hacking it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also is not exactly freeform. Give me a buckets of legos and tell me to build whatever i want is freeform. Giving me a bucket of legos and tell me build a lego engine without any instructions is not really freeform. You are giving me enough limits to constrain me (make a lego engine) but enough freedom to hinder me (I can reach there however i want, so no instructions).<br /> <br /> This is the same, giving the barebones of a social structure (A protectorate is a coallition of pack for hunting something bigger) and expecting me to fill the blanks with little if any guidance is paying lip service to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910403#post910403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence. They want Essence. Specifically, Essence that resonates with their Influences. Spirits achieve higher Rank when they spread their Influence, thereby giving them easier access to more Essence. Lesser spirits flock to greater spirits with like Influences in hopes of feeding from the Essence generated by the environments the greater spirits' Influences cultivate. Greater spirits use lesser spirits as agents to help them further spread their Influences. Courts of spirits with opposing Influences compete for territory and resources. It's like, basic feudal politics and also spelled out in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how spirit react to a spirit who has uratha agents? Is he a traitor or is he the guy with the nuke? What about the difference between a spirit who is part of a pack and one that has werewolf owing him favors, is there socially a difference? How much a court affect its enviroment on the other side? How a court is organized is a pyramid structure? Is it a council like court? What a lord spirit could ask a uratha to do? Is simply provoking a spike of fear any valuable to a higher member of a court? Or its barely a blip in his radar and not worth his notice? Why do they fight for territory? How if the humans move more the shadows than the spirit can then why would they want a territory thats not favors them? Why spirit fight each other when they essence is incompatible if eating each other makes them abominations?<br /> <br /> That is just from the top of my head the question that the book raises and fails to answer. At least in the Core, again maybe the pack explain this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907615#post907615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have to give me an example or two here, because this sounds less like &quot;the game won't let me play my concept&quot; and more like &quot;I don't want my character's actions to have consequences&quot; to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It went like this, a few years ago, we test the then called, Strix Chronicle (i clarify in case they change a rule since then) and one of the guys wanted to play a monk (a modern version of one, it was a french term that it escape me now) that spend years in a tower only with his book studying (he was like a &quot;living&quot; library for his sire). The character idea was a highly moral vampire who study morality and other subjects in his Library sequestered from the world and decided to go outside to finally make his tesis after 70+ years studying as a vampire.<br /> <br /> The concept was shot down by the ST. The rules said that that character cannot had a high morality (or even function, i dont remember exactly which of the two it was 2+ years ago) because he lacked human connections (touch stones, i think) and/or because of his age (again. 2+ years ago).<br /> <br /> The ST wasnt being an asshole he felt bad but as we were trying to test the new system we didnt wanna start tweaking them from the get go. That was his Character concept, it wasnt a trenchcoat katana pc but actually a pretty interesting concept but as the game is so focused on the human conections and fighting the beast playing something else is kinda difficult.<br /> <br /> But i think we derailed the conversation enough of what some people tends to wanna hack on CoFD. So i gonna do what i should have done, ignore Epshy and bow out of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-08-2016, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T20:57:06-07:00","id":910531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910492#post910492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how spirit react to a spirit who has uratha agents? Is he a traitor or is he the guy with the nuke? What about the difference between a spirit who is part of a pack and one that has werewolf owing him favors, is there socially a difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is covered in the Pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much a court affect its enviroment on the other side? How a court is organized is a pyramid structure? Is it a council like court? </div> </div> </div>Centers of spiritual activity strengthen and defend centers of real world activity, or non-activity. It's basically a pyramid, with those closer to the top being more powerful and less numerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What a lord spirit could ask a uratha to do? Is simply provoking a spike of fear any valuable to a higher member of a court? Or its barely a blip in his radar and not worth his notice? Why do they fight for territory? </div> </div> </div>Some of this is covered in the core book, a spirit can ask a Uratha to do anything, some will ignore them some will view them more as tools. Spirits aren't all the same. One Rank 4 spirit of a forest might be a manipulative oracle while another Rank 4 spirit of the forest a brute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How if the humans move more the shadows than the spirit can then why would they want a territory thats not favors them? Why spirit fight each other when they essence is incompatible if eating each other makes them abominations? </div> </div> </div>I don't understand the first question. They fight each other for the same reason people do, territory and resources. A spirit can attack other spirits without absorbing its essence, and becoming a magath usually takes more than one feeding anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-09-2016, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:04:13-07:00","id":910534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910492#post910492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sactum &amp; sigils is a bad book to get an idea of a concilium, it gives you lots of examples of how Concilium get elected, how concilium do justice, how concilium are compose. But what doesnt give you is how those options interact with each other.<br /> <br /> DaveB Broken diamond actual play is a good example of a concilium. It explains the same points of Sactum and sigil with the difference that instead of throwing empty examples with no correlation with each other it shows how each element interact witch each other. E<br /> <br /> Now does this mean That Broken diamonds concilium structure is the one true way? No, but at least it is A fully structure that i can begin with, understand and tweak. It is explained how and why it works and thus, when i wanna change that structure i know how removing something affect other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking about supplement books and actual plays here. Supplement books and actual plays are great ways to expand on a concept, but they take time. Werewolf 2e has been out for a little over a year, it's going to take some time before we start seeing that kind of stuff. There's only so much room in the core book, so the writers give us what we need to play and count on us to use our imaginations to expand on it. There will be more supplement books eventually and as people play some groups will create and post actual plays, but these things take time. Have a little patience, or use 1e supplement books to give you ideas in the mean time, don't call the game &quot;oppressive&quot; because it didn't have room in the core book to give you all the examples you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bQuoting you here<br /> <br /> Also is not exactly freeform. Give me a buckets of legos and tell me to build whatever i want is freeform. Giving me a bucket of legos and tell me build a lego engine without any instructions is not really freeform. You are giving me enough limits to constrain me (make a lego engine) but enough freedom to hinder me (I can reach there however i want, so no instructions).<br /> <br /> This is the same, giving the barebones of a social structure (A protectorate is a coallition of pack for hunting something bigger) and expecting me to fill the blanks with little if any guidance is paying lip service to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about an RPG here, not leggos. It presents a setting and leaves you to create your own stories within the setting. I'm sorry you don't feel like putting in the work to design your own protectorates, but that's really not the game's fault. You can absolutely play Werewolf with inter-pack politics, as long as you're willing to do the legwork yourself, or keep your fingers crossed that they might publish a supplement with advice on running such Chronicles and wait for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo how spirit react to a spirit who has uratha agents? Is he a traitor or is he the guy with the nuke? What about the difference between a spirit who is part of a pack and one that has werewolf owing him favors, is there socially a difference? How much a court affect its enviroment on the other side? How a court is organized is a pyramid structure? Is it a council like court? What a lord spirit could ask a uratha to do? Is simply provoking a spike of fear any valuable to a higher member of a court? Or its barely a blip in his radar and not worth his notice? Why do they fight for territory? How if the humans move more the shadows than the spirit can then why would they want a territory thats not favors them? Why spirit fight each other when they essence is incompatible if eating each other makes them abominations?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above. None of the above. Some of the above. It depends on the individual spirits and their natures. These are the kinds of questions a Storyteller should be asking themselves when designing a chronicle with a heavy focus on spirit politics. Make characters, give them motivations, goals, and agendas. Make some of them coincide and some of them conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat is just from the top of my head the question that the book raises and fails to answer. At least in the Core, again maybe the pack explain this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because there isn't just one answer to any of those questions. Different characters will have different answers, and it's the ST's job to populate their campaign world with characters, not the writers'. Maybe later supplement books will have more example characters, maybe not, in the mean time you should be coming up with your own answers that suit the needs of your own game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIt went like this, a few years ago, we test the then called, Strix Chronicle (i clarify in case they change a rule since then) and one of the guys wanted to play a monk (a modern version of one, it was a french term that it escape me now) that spend years in a tower only with his book studying (he was like a &amp;quot;living&amp;quot; library for his sire). The character idea was a highly moral vampire who study morality and other subjects in his Library sequestered from the world and decided to go outside to finally make his tesis after 70+ years studying as a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a cool concept. He'll occasionally need to roll some Humanity Breaking Points, since the isolation will make it difficult to relate with humans, but that doesn't seem like something that would particularly bother such a character anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe concept was shot down by the ST. The rules said that that character cannot had a high morality (or even function, i dont remember exactly which of the two it was 2+ years ago) because he lacked human connections (touch stones, i think) and/or because of his age (again. 2+ years ago).</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, Humanity is not Morality. Second of all, the long-term isolation would cause him to roll Humanity Breaking Points, and the lack of Touchstones would cause him to suffer a penalty on those rolls, but that should by no means make the character unplayable. Sounds like the problem here is the ST being too restrictive, not the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe ST wasnt being an asshole he felt bad but as we were trying to test the new system we didnt wanna start tweaking them from the get go. That was his Character concept, it wasnt a trenchcoat katana pc but actually a pretty interesting concept but as the game is so focused on the human conections and fighting the beast playing something else is kinda difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to make judgments about the ST's character (I wouldn't call him a dick or anything), but there is absolutely no reason that character couldn't have worked within the rules exactly as-written. Granted, he would have faced some complications due to his lack of human connections, but in a game of personal horror, that's a good thing. Humanity and Touchstones are <i>supposed</i> to cause complications, whether because you don't have any human contact and end up losing Humanity, or because you do maintain deep personal connections and they get in the way of your other obligations. that's the whole point, those complications are <i>where the drama comes from</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYou can? I honestly ask im entering the mage city chapter and from what i understood from obsesions they have to be magical? Other example of NPCs/PCs that i dont think they work in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsessions are related to Mysteries, and Mysteries are usually (though not always) magical. But Mages don't have to spend every waking moment pursuing their Obsessions. They can do other things; hell, technically there aren't even any mechanics forcing them to pursue their Obsessions at all, beyond the player's own desire to earn the Arcane Beats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bA teenager slacker indy musician who just wanna life confortably with his &amp;quot;pay the bills spell&amp;quot; and gets dragged to &amp;quot;adventures&amp;quot; by the rest of his cabal (Cant work because he has to have obsessions, and always care about mysteries)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't that character have Obsessions? Sounds like a perfectly valid start to a character concept that hasn't been fully developed yet. Figure out what does spark this character's curiosity and give him an Obsession related to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bA reaper who has a proxy family that he is breeding to make his own special line (like the one of the paetorians) and he knows that this specific pairing will get him a child that would not age (Is magic in nature the obsesion but there is no mystery to it, said NPC knows the secret and just need to arrange it. So he has to choose another mystery to be obsessed with?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're describing an Obsession a character might have. It doesn't necessarily matter that he knows what he needs to do, there's still more he needs to do to fulfill it, and can still continue to pursue it. Or, you could make that an Aspiration and pick an Obsession that's more related to solving a mystery of some kind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThere is ton of example that other people have posted.<br /> <br /> From people that wanna play changeling downplaying the abuse theme. Playing mage as more Fireball throwing and less astral and symbolism. A game where there is less/no harshness to the sleeping curse. And that just quoting the first page of posters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there are a lot of people that want to alter the themes and aesthetics of those games. There are a also lot of people who would have liked Lord of the Rings better if it had been in space, a lot of people who would have liked Star Wars better if it had been high fantasy, and a lot of people who would have liked the Chronicles of Narnia better if it hadn't had Christian undertones. That doesn't make those works oppressive, it just means they have strong themes and aesthetics, and people have different taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bEven the new concilium setup apparently is revolving around a public mystery. It assumes all concilium forms around a mystery that everyone cares about and knows about when for example boston mystery (the secret concord) i doubt mage come to the nemean and say &amp;quot;yeah we wanna, solve the mystery that will declare us enemies of your administrations&amp;quot; even then if i wanna make concilium base of defending a territory from seers it seems i cant because there is no mistery there. Obviously to me is not a problem i read enough material to just ignore that and go on my own but if i were new and i read 2ed explanation of concilium them it would be very terminant.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* I'm new to Mage and it doesn't bother me. There are some great example Concilia in chapter 7.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAgain not attacking the game because when i wanna play &amp;quot;The Hunt story &amp; the pack vs the world&amp;quot; I go with Forsaken. When i wanna play Magic investigating mysteries, I go with mage Awakening. But if i wanna play Werewolf with protectorate politics then i try some other game because forsaken gives you enough setting info to limit you (Pack mentality, territories, etc) but not enough to help you. Same if i wanted to play a slice of life mage game with little to no focus on the mysteries or the matrix analogy. And thats why i think so many people hack the game with other settings as they want more structure than 2ed offers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if you want to interpret the text narrowly and hack the rules to fix things that aren't broken in the first place, that's your prerogative. But don't be suprised when people point out that werewolf already worked for political games before you hacked it or that the similarities between The Matrix and Demon are superficial at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:54:56-07:00","id":910564,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> <br /> I get where you're coming from Raven. And in some ways I can agree with you. I find Mage frustrating to the extreme because I found character creation too limiting while giving no direction of play, much like you feel with many of the Lines. I find Atlantis/Hermetic Magic/and ancient Mystery dull and uninspiring personally, but admit they can be intriguing for others.<br /> <br /> But, here's the hard part, the books are rather casual and some STs are okay with that and some aren't. I know WW best so your comment on Uratha/ Spirits I can answer and hopefully give you some insight that this has more to do with intuition than facts.<br /> <br /> <b>How does a Spirit react to a spirit with Uratha agents?</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It matters. Are they the same Ilthium or even Brood and the Spirit is using the Uratha to keep them inline? Rebellious most likely, but depends on that spirit's power and how much that group of Uratha have helped produce their essence in the past. If the spirit was forced and intimidated? It makes them look weak and very likely the uratha will be dealing with someone else who took control soon. If the Spirit is weaker but is bullying a tougher Spirit with Uratha aid? Probably view above their station and seen as cowardly, like someone might think of a fink to the police. This of course ignores if the Uratha agents are not Pure who are respected by the Spirits more, especially Fire Touched who serve the Shadow and may be viewed as just a clever play unless personal treachery between the two spirits are at play.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Is there a difference between a spirit part of the pack or owing favours?</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yes Absolutely. It's the difference between Family and someone you bribed. A totem especially defines a Pack, makes it a family. Who it is has to be adopted by the pack and incorporated into who they are, and the spirit gives part of itself and ability to give the Pack power. How much the pack invests in their totem and its goals determines how much the spirit can give itself in return. The bond is near religious, making the ban something the spirit literally cannot do and thus part of the Pack as well. It is the most beneficial relationship many Uratha have with their spirit halves. Even normal spirit packmates are treated the same as other packmates; family, closer even than blood. Favours are favours, I did something for you so you agree you owe me, or because you did this I owe you, no sincere relationship need apply.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>How much does a court affect the other side?</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">That's complex and interwoven. Drug spirits are born because someone used drugs, maybe because depression spirits fostered that action or not, but once they exist they will influence the world around them using their, well influences. They try to get as much essence to stay awake and get more to increase their power or to defeat their rivals. Each spirit has a bent who encourages that influence and the reaction is based on power. If a weak spirit is taken out not much difference in the human world unless that spirit was closely attached to the individual that birthed it, likely the human will have a decrease of that influence IF the catalyst that birthed it in the first place didn't exist. If The Coup of drug spirits have a drug spirit representing the exhilaration of a stimulant be replaced by a drug spirit representing obsession and the push of addiction, you better believe that will change in the real world. None of the users are new or young, perhaps the addiction spirits pushed it in that direction. Also realize spirits are very much local creatures so can't adapt quickly to changes come from outside their influence. A city evolves and change as the people inside it, but the new suburbs are ruins in the Hisil because out of nowhere old nature spirits were deprived of essence. The new people are creating spirits in a vacuum without strong ties until history allows the spirits to grow. Never mind the gauntlet can show how easily each place can be affected with it's thickness. The old cemetery? Each political coup has a huge effect, the new modern hospital? The spirits are just trying to figure out what the place is barely intelligent enough to have any politics rather than bare survival.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Is Court a Pyramid structure? is it a council?</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yes, or both or neither. They order how suits them best. Sometimes there is a top dog, but greed and money spirits might do it like a board meeting with essence treated like stocks and there being a Chairman but the board able to overturn if they can agree. Of course they grumble about paying &quot;taxes&quot; to a more powerful Spirit which could be a River, the spirit of the City, a bigger greed Spirit (Think Wall Street), or none at all. They view the Uratha as police to be bribed, or as nosy federal agents taking away their right to their own work. Another is a group of powerful Alley Cat spirits, they don't agree on anything and don't make decisions as a group. Their politics are more petty and personal, Yowling Queen stole essence from Alley Mange and he wants to get her back. They hate the dog spirits though and enjoy rats spirits they feed on, making their own enemies as a group even if not united. Sometimes a large emotion of deed/tragedy on the private scale produces one large spirit who fosters the others who are born after it. Because of one woman's malice she goes on a large serial killer spree. The spirit born of her malice (it's source) would lord supreme over the lesser Murder and Fear spirits that were produced from that Malice because that's the source. It's so subjective and takes into account history...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>What a lord spirit could ask a uratha to do? Is simply provoking a spike of fear any valuable to a higher member of a court? Or its barely a blip in his radar and not worth his notice?</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Well depends on the Spirit and what the favour being asked, ask a large favour from a powerful Spirit and you could owe years of your life helping the spirit whenever it asks. You ask a small favour and something else will react. A spike of fear would be a small favour, much more likely the large Spirit of fear would ask them to get rid of a human, or group of them, inspiring Courage or deal with a bunch of spirits forming that are encouraging apathy as the residents get used to fear. Maybe even take out it's second so its lessers know (or believe) the spirit has The People to call on if they ever resist. Lots of things.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Why do they fight for territory? How if the humans move more the shadows than the spirit can then why would they want a territory thats not favors them? Why spirit fight each other when they essence is incompatible if eating each other makes them abominations?</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The spirits don't often vie for territory so much as influence. A spirit of Joy doesn't want the West side, it want to spread joy so it can have more joy to consume and more power. It does NOT become Magath if it consumes things natural to it. An owl spirit can consume rat spirits all day and might represent the hunting aspect more as it does so. It does what owls do. Magaths form when the source of what they are disappear and the spirit out of desperation eats essence completely unaligned to what it is. All the owls in the area are killed off by say a plague, but the owl spirit survives by eating a bear spirit and continues doing so. Owls don't hunt bears, have different natures and ideals, having both changes what it is and drives it mad, because the opposite pulls. Magaths are a terrible abomination to Spirits. Spread of territory doesn't do that. Owl spirits might fight a bear if the Bear spirit was worried they were too many and might overtake his position as head spirit in the area, but in this case they wouldn't consume each other's essence, just use each other's influence against the other or bring in other Choir allies. Unless the spirit of an actual location, area and land isn't the issue so much as spreading control. No data spirit wants to take over the back yard, but would love to have more information, electricity and power to give it more influence.</div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> TLDR: I wrote all that up so you can understand how I got all of this from reading the book and how you seem to want cut and dry answers from something that cannot be summed up neatly. They explained this in the book, but I don't think it is how you want. And I get that. Honestly for me Mage is often that way for me too. There's nothing wrong with it, and being frustrated with it I think just means you need/desire a different mode of play or themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T03:22:14-07:00","id":910667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910492#post910492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It went like this, a few years ago, we test the then called, Strix Chronicle (i clarify in case they change a rule since then) and one of the guys wanted to play a monk (a modern version of one, it was a french term that it escape me now) that spend years in a tower only with his book studying (he was like a &quot;living&quot; library for his sire). The character idea was a highly moral vampire who study morality and other subjects in his Library sequestered from the world and decided to go outside to finally make his tesis after 70+ years studying as a vampire.<br /> <br /> The concept was shot down by the ST. The rules said that that character cannot had a high morality (or even function, i dont remember exactly which of the two it was 2+ years ago) because he lacked human connections (touch stones, i think) and/or because of his age (again. 2+ years ago).<br /> <br /> The ST wasnt being an asshole he felt bad but as we were trying to test the new system we didnt wanna start tweaking them from the get go. That was his Character concept, it wasnt a trenchcoat katana pc but actually a pretty interesting concept but as the game is so focused on the human conections and fighting the beast playing something else is kinda difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh.<br /> <br /> See, I hate the Vampire gameline, but I can immediately see that the obvious touchstones are to look in on descendants of old friends, or places where they used to hang out. I mean, that's before I even seriously engage with the idea. Just mark him at Humanity 7 like any other starting character, but peg it to when he comes out of his tower. And, at a glance, I don't see any rules in B&amp;S that say an old vampire is not allowed. Just don't give him any XP for being old. Was that a problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T03:34:06-07:00","id":910673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910357#post910357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Thats the same problem with protectorates. Its says spirits have ranks, it tells you they form courts but not how that courts works and how their politics function. Which is even worse because we are talking about Alien entities so their motivations and what they want is even more obscure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try this topic and take some templates for your game:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2\"> A grab-bag of Shadow - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/902501-a-grab-bag-of-shadow/page2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A lot of people have trouble visualising the Hisil, or coming up with ideas for how the Shadow representation of an area could appear. This is a thread to help fix that. (I don't recall a thread dealing with this before. If we have one, please point me towards it.) Here's the game - pick any place that you think is likely to be part of a territory and describe how it appears in the Hisil. Describe what it looks like, what spirits you find there, how they interact, and how they're likely to react to Uratha intruders. (This can be as broad or narrow as you like. A spirit ecology may respond well to </div> </div> </div><br /> Here we create spiritual places and how all the spirits work within. Probably it will make your life easier to imagine because i know its hard to understand due the lack of examples in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:13:38-07:00","id":910725,"title":"","content":"I've never been a thematic purist. If anything, I love the CofD/nWoD setting but I hate the themes of personal horror because I find that particular thematic to be extremely boring. So, when I am the Storyteller, I remove Humanity/Morality/Clarity/Touchstones, etc., and remove personal horror. I prefer action-horror and political intrigue over personal horror. But that's just me. My opinion and nothing more. Just because I prefer what some would call &quot;Superheroes with fangs&quot; (although in all honesty, my games are more like &quot;Mobsters with fangs&quot; than anything else) doesn't make my games any less valid than an angsty personal horror game.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I never understood the &quot;One True Way&quot; mentality of the WoD/CofD fandom. Quite frankly, I am sick of people telling me I should play &quot;Some Other Game&quot; just because I don't make my games into angsty personal horror. Again, there is nothing wrong with personal horror, but it doesn't work for me. So, when I am the ST, I chuck it out the window and substitute my own themes. Remember the Golden Rule.<br /> <br /> There is nothing in the 1e mechanics that enforces personal horror except Morality and the related systems such as Humanity or Clarity. Remove that and the rest is just fluff you can easily change if you are the ST.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:34:52-07:00","id":910733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910725#post910725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a thematic purist. If anything, I love the CofD/nWoD setting but I hate the themes of personal horror because I find that particular thematic to be extremely boring. So, when I am the Storyteller, I remove Humanity/Morality/Clarity/Touchstones, etc., and remove personal horror. I prefer action-horror and political intrigue over personal horror. But that's just me. My opinion and nothing more. Just because I prefer what some would call &quot;Superheroes with fangs&quot; (although in all honesty, my games are more like &quot;Mobsters with fangs&quot; than anything else) doesn't make my games any less valid than an angsty personal horror game.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I never understood the &quot;One True Way&quot; mentality of the WoD/CofD fandom. Quite frankly, I am sick of people telling me I should play &quot;Some Other Game&quot; just because I don't make my games into angsty personal horror. Again, there is nothing wrong with personal horror, but it doesn't work for me. So, when I am the ST, I chuck it out the window and substitute my own themes. Remember the Golden Rule.<br /> <br /> There is nothing in the 1e mechanics that enforces personal horror except Morality and the related systems such as Humanity or Clarity. Remove that and the rest is just fluff you can easily change if you are the ST.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually there are many mechanics that enforces personal horror. The whole rule set in 1e referred to your own characters temptations is considered personal horror.<br /> The werewolf kuruth, the frenzy and thirst of a vampire, the paranoia of a changeling, the geist tempting sin-eaters are all personal horror elements.<br /> <br /> Virtue / Vices / Touchstones / Blood &amp; Bone etc in my opinion are made to prevent players to create characters based only in functions and not personalities. To make you think about the weaknesses of yourself and give proper weight to the story<br /> The humanity / morality / wisdom They are made to measure the alignment of the character and how their actions reflects. Many of these mechanics are connected directly to how the player cares about his actions.<br /> .<br /> We have all seen that player of D&amp;D, when you ask:<br /> GM: What's your backstory<br /> Player: Im the soldier<br /> GM: Yes but ... whats your motivations?<br /> Player: I protect things .. yea whatever lets kill some goblins<br /> <br /> There is no right way to play, but there are reasons for certain things exist based on past problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","user":"magisanctum","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:51:36-07:00","id":910742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910153#post910153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Inferno is also heavily set on the Catholic mindset of Vice / sin. Several books in 2e are already known for describing the Inferno as the Christian themed Hell. You can't get away from that here. Even if we're not dealing with fallen angels (the whole point of the Demon game lines), Inferno is still heavily Catholic inspired and tied into that religion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Inferno has infernal gods in it, it has the flexiblity.<br /> <br /> Personally for Dominions I'd just have them be Larvas and other Demon types be that choice to purify themselves of none Infernal Essence, an attempt to prefect themselves.<br /> <br /> I'll give you on the 7 sins, but for 2e you have more wiggle room to add in some grey area or change the vices up.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Sins Demons represent are regional and cultural based.<br /> <br /> And the Court of Indulgence is based onthe same 7 sins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:12:26-07:00","id":910753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910725#post910725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a thematic purist. If anything, I love the CofD/nWoD setting but I hate the themes of personal horror because I find that particular thematic to be extremely boring. So, when I am the Storyteller, I remove Humanity/Morality/Clarity/Touchstones, etc., and remove personal horror. I prefer action-horror and political intrigue over personal horror. But that's just me. My opinion and nothing more. Just because I prefer what some would call &quot;Superheroes with fangs&quot; (although in all honesty, my games are more like &quot;Mobsters with fangs&quot; than anything else) doesn't make my games any less valid than an angsty personal horror game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, you're perfectly welcome to play the game that way if that's what your group prefers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910725#post910725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I never understood the &quot;One True Way&quot; mentality of the WoD/CofD fandom. Quite frankly, I am sick of people telling me I should play &quot;Some Other Game&quot; just because I don't make my games into angsty personal horror. Again, there is nothing wrong with personal horror, but it doesn't work for me. So, when I am the ST, I chuck it out the window and substitute my own themes. Remember the Golden Rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your particular case there is more of an issue of you historically having gone out of your way to preface every post you made with an announcement that you don't want anything to do with personal horror or anything gothic. Naturally, a lot of folks' reaction was to suggest that maybe you look for a game whose core themes you didn't find quite so revolting. Like, if you don't mind putting in the work to remove the elements you don't like from the game, more power to you. But when your vocal distaste for those elements reach near-flamebait levels, you should expect people to offer alternatives.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> hacks the crap out of every gameline, but he doesn't harp on about how much he hates Y-Splats and finds antagonist factions boring in every other post. He just presents his homebrew and says &quot;here's how I do it in my games&quot; and a lot of people love it.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I think that's the real reason behind some hacks being labeled &quot;missing the point&quot; and others not. If the hack is connected to a contentious element that people have had to continually defend about the game, you're going to get people saying it's missing the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910725#post910725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing in the 1e mechanics that enforces personal horror except Morality and the related systems such as Humanity or Clarity. Remove that and the rest is just fluff you can easily change if you are the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably Virtue and Vice as well. Also Frenzy/Kiruth and other such loss-of-control states. But yeah, if you don't like the personal horror themes it's really not that hard to play without them. I would argue you don't even need to hack out the rules elements that tie into those themes to do so (unless you want to, obviously). They're in there by default, and some folks seem to get very frustrated that the games fight them in their attempts to play action/adventure games instead of horror games, and to those folks I think it's reasonable to point out that personal horror is a core theme and if they want to play without it it's going to take an effort on their parts. You don't seem to find it takes you much effort, and that's cool. You enjoy playing the games the way you like to play them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:22:13-07:00","id":910760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910725#post910725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a thematic purist. If anything, I love the CofD/nWoD setting but I hate the themes of personal horror because I find that particular thematic to be extremely boring. So, when I am the Storyteller, I remove Humanity/Morality/Clarity/Touchstones, etc., and remove personal horror. I prefer action-horror and political intrigue over personal horror. But that's just me. My opinion and nothing more. Just because I prefer what some would call &quot;Superheroes with fangs&quot; (although in all honesty, my games are more like &quot;Mobsters with fangs&quot; than anything else) doesn't make my games any less valid than an angsty personal horror game.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I never understood the &quot;One True Way&quot; mentality of the WoD/CofD fandom. Quite frankly, I am sick of people telling me I should play &quot;Some Other Game&quot; just because I don't make my games into angsty personal horror. Again, there is nothing wrong with personal horror, but it doesn't work for me. So, when I am the ST, I chuck it out the window and substitute my own themes. Remember the Golden Rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed for the most part. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is nothing in the 1e mechanics that enforces personal horror except Morality and the related systems such as Humanity or Clarity. Remove that and the rest is just fluff you can easily change if you are the ST. </div> </div> </div> And here I disagree. I don't think that the Morality-equivalents really qualify as personal horror, nor are they the only example of p.h. in the game. To use Vampire as an example - use of Disciplines as coercion is far more horrific to me than Frenzy or Humanity. I can be a moral person by avoiding frenzy temptations and maintaining a code of ethics even with low Humanity. I can't avoid the fact that Disciplines are designed to strip people of their free will. And that's not &quot;just fluff.&quot; Its entwined into the very numbers of the game. <br /> <br /> As well, I really dislike the idea that you can easily ignore &quot;fluff.&quot; Story flows from mechanics, and in turn gives shape to those same mechanics. The two are intertwined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910733#post910733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have all seen that player of D&amp;D, when you ask:<br /> GM: What's your backstory<br /> Player: Im the soldier<br /> GM: Yes but ... whats your motivations?<br /> Player: I protect things .. yea whatever lets kill some goblins</div> </div> </div> </div> You know, I get that you're trying to showcase a player that only cares about combat here, but let me have a moment here. I detest histories. As far as I'm concerned, they're glorified bluebooking, and I hate blue books. I don't care what you did in your past - I care about how you are sitting down, at the table now, and acting. I care about how we're introducing you to the others, and the game going on right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910742#post910742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inferno has infernal gods in it, it has the flexiblity.</div> </div> </div> </div> The problem is that the books and writers themselves have a pretty strongly assoiation. I don't think we can deny that connection. The Inferno is Catholic-hell. This doesn't mean that a game can't still come of it, but the association is there and undeniable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:22:21-07:00","id":910761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910166#post910166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is The Matrix the scifi story you think it looks like? Because that was a Gnostic Messiah story with The Machine as an allegory for the Demiurge.<br /> <br /> Besides that, all of the Fallen Angel aspects of DtD are inseparable from the game - falling from service to a higher power, gaining autonomy as a result, fighting or fleeing its remaining servants, bargaining for the souls of mortals, striving to create your own space free from the influence of the higher power, a false human visage and a true angelic form that becomes more and more demonic as your power grows, miracles that draw upon your memories of being an angel to access the rules that God put into place for its Angels to use, blasphemies that exploit those rules to produce greater and more powerful results at a cost... On the other hand, all of the scifi stuff can be changed without impacting the game. Drop the &amp;quot;Machine&amp;quot; from God-Machine, re-name the demonic form abilities, etc. there's a whole thread over on the DtD forums brainstorming more biblical names for everything, and they could all be used without impacting how the game is actually played.<br /> <br /> That's how you can tell what's the core of the story and what's the paint.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, it definitely leaves room for Inferno. Descent is about Fallen Angels, Inferno is about Demons. As much as Milton may have popularized the trend of conflating the two, there's still a significant divide between how a lot of people conceptualize each. Not only that, Descent is distinctly Gnostic, while Inferno is pretty much Agnostic. That also makes a huge difference.</div> </div> </div> </div> I never thought of the Matrix that way. Cool.<br /> <br /> I think Inferno is more complex then Agnostic. It Agnostic on the level omnisent deity level, but it has beings that ARE basically Gods on a Polytheistic level of subomnisence, for example Set.<br /> <br /> So its Agnostic in regards to monothiestic religions, but Gnostic in reguards to Polytheism, the Demons know there are Gods of terrible power in the Inferno, Shadow, Underworld, possibly by now they know its true of Arcadia and the Hedge too, and that doesn't include stuff like Archmages and weirder stuff, like Alien Gods and other asorted Lovecraftian Horrors, the Godmachine, ect...<br /> <br /> I think the big difference between Inferno and DtD, is polytheism vs. monotheism vibe, the Demons in DtD only really care about the Godmachine, I don't think they usually care about other Gods, the Inferno includes demons from various different realms, who are aware of various species of Gods, andcthe Inferno even has its own species of Demon Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:42:34-07:00","id":910775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910760#post910760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know, I get that you're trying to showcase a player that only cares about combat here, but let me have a moment here. I detest histories. As far as I'm concerned, they're glorified bluebooking, and I hate blue books. I don't care what you did in your past - I care about how you are sitting down, at the table now, and acting. I care about how we're introducing you to the others, and the game going on right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I was pointing out is that a player may well be interested in his own history with the help of mechanics. The personal history of a player makes the GM create stories involving personal interests. This can greatly help motivated the players continue to play any game because they have something they created being used and receiving appropriate attention..<br /> The backstory reflects the interest of the players to the table and I think it's a big plot generator.<br /> As for mechanics I was also trying to say that they are directly linked to interpretation.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut if you and your players are happy playing the way you describe I think you still you can have fantastic experiences anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:47:53-07:00","id":910779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910761#post910761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never thought of the Matrix that way. Cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. The sequels kind of muck up the metaphor but they kind of have to be looked at as their own separate thing. They were clearly a two-part unplanned sequel to a film that stood on its own, and they really broke away from the philosophy of the original.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910761#post910761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Inferno is more complex then Agnostic. It Agnostic on the level omnisent deity level, but it has beings that ARE basically Gods on a Polytheistic level of subomnisence, for example Set.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quick Wikipedia definition says Agnosticism is the view that the truth values of certain claims \u2013 especially metaphysical and religious claims such as whether God, the divine, or the supernatural exist \u2013 are unknown and perhaps unknowable. Inferno definitely fits that bill in my reading. It doesn't really make claims one way or the other in regards to the truth of any religion or the existence of any divine being or beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910761#post910761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So its Agnostic in regards to monothiestic religions, but Gnostic in reguards to Polytheism, the Demons know there are Gods of terrible power in the Inferno, Shadow, Underworld, possibly by now they know its true of Arcadia and the Hedge too, and that doesn't include stuff like Archmages and weirder stuff, like Alien Gods and other asorted Lovecraftian Horrors, the Godmachine, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any of those entities can accurately be described as Gods in the theistic sense of the word (mono or poly). Also, you're using Gnostic incorrectly here. Gnosticism is a specific religion, or to be more precise, a collection of religions sharing some foundational beliefs such as the immateriality of the physical world, the existence of a truer reality beyond the material, and the existance of a Demiurge keeping humanity believing in the false material reality. You can't be &quot;Gnostic in regards to polytheism&quot;. You can be a polytheist Gnostic, but Inferno is not that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910761#post910761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the big difference between Inferno and DtD, is polytheism vs. monotheism vibe, the Demons in DtD only really care about the Godmachine, I don't think they usually care about other Gods, the Inferno includes demons from various different realms, who are aware of various species of Gods, andcthe Inferno even has its own species of Demon Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really describe either as theistic at all. The &quot;Gods&quot; of the settings barely resemble theistic deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:57:01-07:00","id":910901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910761#post910761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never thought of the Matrix that way. Cool.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest reading <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Taking-Red-Pill-Philosophy-Religion/dp/1932100024\" target=\"_blank\">Taking the Red Pill</a> and <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Matrix-Philosophy-Welcome-Popular-Culture/dp/081269502X/ref=pd_bxgy_14_img_2?ie=UTF8&amp;refRID=14SMH5159QR0E7CQF3JN\" target=\"_blank\">The Matrix and Philosophy</a>. They delve into the idea quite a bit. As, Charly says though, the sequels kinda break it but it is still there to some degree.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:30:17-07:00","id":910933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910901#post910901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggest reading <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Taking-Red-Pill-Philosophy-Religion/dp/1932100024&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Taking the Red Pill</a> and <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Matrix-Philosophy-Welcome-Popular-Culture/dp/081269502X/ref=pd_bxgy_14_img_2?ie=UTF8&amp;refRID=14SMH5159QR0E7CQF3JN&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">The Matrix and Philosophy</a>. They delve into the idea quite a bit. As, Charly says though, the sequels kinda break it but it is still there to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both great books. They were my first introduction to Gnosticism in a formal sense.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the sequels, I can appreciate what they were trying to do. By showing Neo's powers working in the real world, allowing Smith to exist outside the Matrix in a human host, introducing a higher layer of complexity to The Machines' plans in which the existance of Zion and a resistance were a part. It was all pointing to the idea that even what the characters see as &quot;the real world&quot; isn't real. They were trying to bring the Gnostic message beyond the limits of the cyberpunk metaphor. The problem was, unless you already had a working understanding of Gnosticism, it wasn't at all clear that was the intent, and it just looked like they were breaking their own rules. That's where you get fan theories like &quot;the real world is actually another layer of the simulation&quot; that try to put the events of the sequels back into the context of the metaphor. The real point (in my interpretation) was that while the &quot;real world&quot; isn't literally a computer simulation, that doesn't actually make it any more real than the Matrix. But it was handled too clumsily to come across that way to most of the audience. Besides that, if you don't buy into the philosophy it strains suspension of disbelief way more than the metaphor does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-09-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:48:36-07:00","id":910950,"title":"","content":"I just didn't like the long ass dance cave, the orgasm cake, or other references like that. Felt... unnecessary and put in just for cheap titilation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:12:11-07:00","id":910970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910950#post910950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just didn't like the long ass dance cave, the orgasm cake, or other references like that. Felt... unnecessary and put in just for cheap titilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. It was more than that. All three movies had dance sequences, if you note. The first one, where Neo meets Trinity. The second one, which is what you reference and is a hedonistic &quot;we're not machines&quot; thing. And the third one, which takes places in Hell, er, the Merovingian's club.<br /> <br /> In other words, I think your read on that sequence is slightly unfair. Um. That's all I should say to avoid derail, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:18:28-07:00","id":911135,"title":"","content":"My personal preferences and impressions are unfair? No, they're <i>personal opinions</i>. You can't say how I feel about something is unfair. Its <i>how I feel</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:38:47-07:00","id":911152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910950#post910950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just didn't like the long ass dance cave, the orgasm cake, or other references like that. Felt... unnecessary and put in just for cheap titilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the dance cave was pretty cool, though I could have done without the simultaneous sex scene. The orgasm cake was probably the biggest &quot;what the fuck?&quot; moment in the series to me. Like, on a lot of levels. I liked the Merovingian's monologue about causality, and it served as a cool counterpoint to the protagonists' emphasis on the importance of choice, but... Seriously, what the fuck was up with the cake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:46:56-07:00","id":911162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911152#post911152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, what the fuck was up with the cake?</div> </div> </div> </div>Orgasms. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.sunnation.co.uk/s3/sunnation-prod/uploads/2015/07/ba-dum-tish.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:49:08-07:00","id":911165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911135#post911135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal preferences and impressions are unfair? No, they're <i>personal opinions</i>. You can't say how I feel about something is unfair. Its <i>how I feel</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errol can, in fact, say that he thinks your read on a given sequence is unfair. It is entirely within reason to, <i>as an explicit statement of opinion</i>, describe someone's interpretation of a thing as uncharitable, as this compels no action and makes no claims of authoritativeness or objectivity. That's how statements of opinion work. That's what &quot;I think&quot; tends to mean when placed at the beginning of a clause.<br /> <br /> Having opinions about opinions is kind of a thing people do all the time in a public forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:13:18-07:00","id":911185,"title":"","content":"&quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Having opinions about opinions is kind of a thing people do all the time in a public forum.</span>&quot; -- And telling someone that their impression of a movie is wrong is something people do a lot as well. That doesn't mystically it right.<br /> <br /> &quot;I thought the dance cave was pretty cool, though I could have done without the simultaneous sex scene.&quot; -- well, the sex is kind of what I meant by feeling cheap. Same with the cake. Felt like they were trying to push a sex-theme too hard during the movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-09-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:16:01-07:00","id":911189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911185#post911185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And telling someone that their opinion is wrong is something people do a lot as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing that's not what actually happened, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:50:15-07:00","id":911204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911185#post911185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;[FONT=inherit]<br /> &quot;I thought the dance cave was pretty cool, though I could have done without the simultaneous sex scene.&quot; -- well, the sex is kind of what I meant by feeling cheap. Same with the cake. Felt like they were trying to push a sex-theme too hard during the movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta get that R rating somehow. Otherwise, Mom might bring the younger kids and then the Matrix won't be cool because it's edgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-d