tegrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":2758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","user":"Errol216","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:42:09-07:00","id":911476,"title":"","content":"Point of order: the thread is only partially about how people frequently misread gamelines; it's <i>also</i> about how people frequently take exception to game hacks that violate what they consider to be the spirit of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:45:11-07:00","id":911478,"title":"","content":"That, and analysis of the Matrix sequels <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:02:29-07:00","id":911480,"title":"","content":"I've gotten into a couple incredibly heated discussions about the merits of Changeling as a metaphor for being an abuse survivor, and how deemphasizing that is incredibly unfortunate. It shares a space with Wraith (which I view as an incredibly astute metaphor for the struggle with depression and other mental illness) and possibly Promethean as well (which I'm increasingly viewing in a transgender or more generally queer light) as some of the most emotionally weighty games out there, and while I understand that many people want to have lighter fun (or rather, don't want/need a coping mechanism and avenue for telling stories that resonate with their struggles) it always feels like a shame to try and undercut that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T03:18:52-07:00","id":911552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911476#post911476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order: the thread is only partially about how people frequently misread gamelines; it's <i>also</i> about how people frequently take exception to game hacks that violate what they consider to be the spirit of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If there are plenty of people misreading you are right the thread is going the wrong way, but probably there is a reason for it and we should anylise it.<br /> Currently we have a more organized book than 1e, but the games of the new lines have so much information thrown at specific phrases in specific corners in the book that is almost impossible to record all information without confusing the head or miss something. In 2e some concepts are more clear but some are more vague like the Shadow that is a crucial thing for werewolf. The lack of exemplification in abstract things is a plus Difficulty to run the game.<br /> I already ran Mage the Awakening/changeling for a long time and just as many lines there was always that little rule we found that existed in some hidden corner of the book after the game had already started.<br /> Primarily this is a design error, lack of focus on the book's organization. The games of darkness mix too much the lore and the rule simultaneously spreading information all over the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T04:38:10-07:00","id":911574,"title":"","content":"I'm probably constantly missing the point of Vampire, because I was never interested in the lust and sex metaphor. Or lust and sex in general.<br /> You can probably imagnie how many times I rolled my eyes while reading CofD books with it's tendency to put as much of the above in fluff sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-10-2016, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:20:58-07:00","id":911607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911391#post911391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh.<br /> <br /> I said your <i>read</i> was unfair. &quot;Read&quot;. As in &quot;interpretation&quot;, not &quot;impression&quot;. Not that you didn't feel what you felt.<br /> <br /> Seriously, in a thread about how people frequently misread gamelines completely and possibly intentionally, <i>this</i> is the hill you're choosing to die on?</div> </div> </div> </div> My &quot;read?&quot; My interpretation? And here I was thinking that saying how I felt about something was still just an impression. Silly me.<br /> <br /> Seriously, people do this all the time one these forums. &quot;I don't like the Seers - help me change them. Please don't comment if you don't want to offer suggestions!&quot; What happens? People come in to the threads and argue up and down that, no, you should like the Seers as is. No changing. They say its unfair, that you're reading things wrong. Knee jerk reactions against people not liking what you like. I've even seen people admit that - they felt like, because what they liked wasn't liked by others, it was somehow an &quot;attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you're going to make this about a hill to die on, then actually identify the hill first, Errol. I did nothing more than state my feelings on the matter. I even made sure to use the word &quot;felt&quot; to highlight that it was nothing more than my subjective feelings on the matter. And then, you said my feelings were &quot;unfair.&quot; As if these feelings were unreasonable or wrong somehow. That might not have been your intent, but that is what happened. People should be allowed to not like something, for any reason, without it being 'splained to why they are wrong.<br /> <br /> I think that's the heart of these &quot;you're missing the point!&quot; threads. These are subjective genres, but if someone doesn't like the same thing another person did, then that latter person reads into it negatively. Then, there has to be a post that says, no! wrong! Or unfair, or something like that. Somehow, invariably, the opposing opinion needs to be undermined. &quot;If you don't agree with me, then you must be missing the point.&quot; Things might get lost when people get insulting or patronizing towards one another, but I think that's the heart of the matter. One person doesn't like an aspect, and wants to change it. Other people like the original, feel threatened, and have to &quot;fight back.&quot;<br /> <br /> You see it all the time, but that doesn't make it right. Its nothing more than a knee jerk &quot;Us Versus Them&quot; mentality that doesn't really work in a society. There are a wide variety of opinions, and none of them should be dismissed out of hand. I don't like something, because feelings. You like something, because feelings. Great. Both are fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:35:12-07:00","id":911613,"title":"","content":"It'd be more constructive if people that go around excising out the things they don't enjoy about games if they filled the design vacuum with something, but that's just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:14:18-07:00","id":911631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911574#post911574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably constantly missing the point of Vampire, because I was never interested in the lust and sex metaphor. Or lust and sex in general.<br /> You can probably imagnie how many times I rolled my eyes while reading CofD books with it's tendency to put as much of the above in fluff sections.</div> </div> </div> </div>One is of course always free to ignore things, but ignoring something isn't the same as making it not exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:20:12-07:00","id":911632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911613#post911613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be more constructive if people that go around excising out the things they don't enjoy about games if they filled the design vacuum with something, but that's just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>People complain because they dont have any solution, I believe that answering people giving ideas to solve their stuff will be way more helpful such as myself that have been answered in this topic.<br /> <br /> I will try to collaborate.<br /> Wod books have always been books that should be read literally from page 1 to the last. Not that I would not do that, but when you have so many rules mixed with lore through all the book,. You cant read with a clear direction and it makes even more difficult to search for information in the book. As I said up there: <i>there was always these little rules we found that existed in some hidden corner of the book after the game had already started.</i><br /> <br /> The use charts with summary of rules can help considerably in consultation and with memorizing the most subtle funcionabilidades that the game has to offer.<br /> Of course I'm not anyone to give a solution out of my pocket, but I suggest to take a look at the book A song of Ice and Fire from Green Ronin and notice how everything is crystal clear and easy in terms of book design / organization / guidance however you wish to call. <br /> Clearly there was a huge improvement in the second edition but I believe it can improve even more in the books to come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:32:09-07:00","id":911641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=911574#post911574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably constantly missing the point of Vampire, because I was never interested in the lust and sex metaphor. Or lust and sex in general.<br /> You can probably imagnie how many times I rolled my eyes while reading CofD books with it's tendency to put as much of the above in fluff sections.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see that as an essential part of vampire though, like the trauma metaphor is for Changeling. Like, it's there because vampires have been bound with sex at least since Carmilla. But nothing about the game really relies on that metaphor to function. IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T00:05:40-07:00","id":912131,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> <br /> <br /> I really did try to give myself some space about it and thought, and I admit it is very possible I don't fully understand the social maneuver rules. I'd be glad to learn if you would give examples because it does confuse me.<br /> <br /> I don't see how much someone likes you has anything to do with the length of time to pursue something. I mean obviously disliking hinders, and liking benefits, but that just changes it within the scope of how generally an act takes. By these new rules, any long term persuasion would take seconds if they like you enough, and I just see relationship better represented by modifiers. I mean it can take me weeks to convince my wife to get a real Christmas tree this year, but a cool charismatic person could probably sell it to her in about a week. My +3 for a close relationship doesn't make up for their much higher persuasion and presence. I just feel like relationships don't change the nature of time limits except within it's usual time limits. Nevermind it saps all the drama from a long term persuasion roll with those close to you. Who cares if you are breaking doors with someone you don't like? If all the important people in your character's life can be convinced in seconds, where is the drama?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T05:52:28-07:00","id":912200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907495#post907495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtR - At least during the first few years of the NWoD, the biggest complaints i can remember was that it wasn't Masquerade.No Malkavians,No Tzimisce, and other familiar VtM elementswere left out of the new version and quite a few people were rather salty about it.<br /> <br /> MtC - The tightly focused settings and themes were both a blessing and a curse. Some enjoyed the history and mythology of Irem. Others would have preferred something more global, where they could play a mummy from one of the many other cultures that practiced mummification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding Vampire, more than anything, I would cite people who want Paths back (though there's been less of that lately). Today, and more purely Requiem-related, it might be the subject of new covenants, and the attendant disputes over what constitutes a new covenant.<br /> <br /> Regarding Mummy, there are also those of us who sort of want both. To keep Irem central (and singular in the magnitude of what it achieved), but think there's also room - including within the setting as described - for analogous things to have been achieved elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=909505#post909505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The largest &quot;changing what you don't like things&quot; thing I've heard for Geist are &quot;Make it more like Wraith&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sort of on this train. I like the Geist mythos as it is, but would be overjoyed to see a sort of &quot;W&quot; axis in 2nd Ed, where Sineaters live alongside Revenants, Wraiths (as distinct from ghosts), and Mediums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910760#post910760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the books and writers themselves have a pretty strongly assoiation. I don't think we can deny that connection. The Inferno is Catholic-hell. This doesn't mean that a game can't still come of it, but the association is there and undeniable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second edition has expanded virtues and vices a lot, and Inferno can follow suit. Not every vice is suitable for use as something flat-out evil, but we can go a long way past the magnificent seven (no reason Hunter should get all the Supernatural references). It does mean the powers can't be broken up by Vice any more - too many and too DIY - but there must be another way to do that.<br /> <br /> Inferno works well for some of Demon the Fallen's aspects. The place itself might be a hell, but it's a hell to which humans aren't sentenced, only the demons themselves. Inferno demons are spiritually weak, which makes it little of a stretch to picture one being transformed by possession of a human into something not-quite-a-demon any more. Even more than Fallen, Inferno demons have no grand past to take direction from, so &quot;What will I be now?&quot; can be even more of a theme for those that are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:45:17-07:00","id":912490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=912131#post912131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a><br /> <br /> I really did try to give myself some space about it and thought, and I admit it is very possible I don't fully understand the social maneuver rules. I'd be glad to learn if you would give examples because it does confuse me.<br /> <br /> I don't see how much someone likes you has anything to do with the length of time to pursue something. I mean obviously disliking hinders, and liking benefits, but that just changes it within the scope of how generally an act takes. By these new rules, any long term persuasion would take seconds if they like you enough, and I just see relationship better represented by modifiers. I mean it can take me weeks to convince my wife to get a real Christmas tree this year, but a cool charismatic person could probably sell it to her in about a week. My +3 for a close relationship doesn't make up for their much higher persuasion and presence. I just feel like relationships don't change the nature of time limits except within it's usual time limits. Nevermind it saps all the drama from a long term persuasion roll with those close to you. Who cares if you are breaking doors with someone you don't like? If all the important people in your character's life can be convinced in seconds, where is the drama?</div> </div> </div> </div>I might have some time tomorrow. I'll see how much I can write up and how coherent I can make it, then. Can't promise to deliver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T19:15:14-07:00","id":912573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=912200#post912200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sort of on this train. I like the Geist mythos as it is, but would be overjoyed to see a sort of &quot;W&quot; axis in 2nd Ed, where Sineaters live alongside Revenants, Wraiths (as distinct from ghosts), and Mediums.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there are already playable ghost things in Chronicles of Darkness (in Mummy iirc), that is seperate to Sin-Eaters, revenants are just ghosts who possess/claim their own bodies/use a numina from mummy, and mediums are a supernatural merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T19:43:01-07:00","id":912589,"title":"","content":"The Lucid Dead Numina from Mummy is largely incompatible with ChroD Ephemeral Entities rules, and was a patch job anyway. I'd like Geist 2e to provide a more robust, 2e-compatible approach, treating lucid ghosts the way Werewolf treats wolf-bloods or the way Mage treats Sleepwalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T03:24:31-07:00","id":912716,"title":"","content":"I'm a weird one. I frankly love the animism of Werewolf and the weirdness of the Shadow Realm, but I couldn't care less about the furries themselves. <br /> May have been up to me, I would have chosen mortal shamans as the main protagonists, and the way humans influence and are influenced by their environment as the main theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T04:04:43-07:00","id":912728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=912716#post912716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a weird one. I frankly love the animism of Werewolf and the weirdness of the Shadow Realm, but I couldn't care less about the furries themselves.<br /> May have been up to me, I would have chosen mortal shamans as the main protagonists, and the way humans influence and are influenced by their environment as the main theme.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but Shamans aren't Horror Monsters. Nearest fit for that is Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T08:15:15-07:00","id":912804,"title":"","content":"That said, it's possible to play WtF through the eyes of the wolf-blooded, with a Pack that's devoid of Uratha; and there are some wolf-blooded who are effectively shamans. (And there are others that are essentially werewolves \u2014 just not Uratha; good for those who prefer a <i>less</i> spiritual take on werewolves.) Indeed, the one hack I'd make to WtF for those who'd prefer to play it as shamans and spirits would be to introduce a Tell \u2014 or enhance an existing Tell \u2014 that grants the spirit-oriented wolf-blood full access to Rites. <br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm very impressed at how accommodating WtF is of \u201cnon-standard\u201d styles of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T17:22:37-07:00","id":913101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point#post907459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been noticing a trend on the various ChroD Forums: it seems that just about every gameline has developed an alternate fanbase that dislikes some core aspect of the gameline and proposes hacks to change the gameline in question. Meanwhile, there are fans of the game as written who consider such hacks to be missing the point of the game. This is an attempt to catalog this phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Note: I'm trying not to pass judgment. Some of these, I like; others, I don't. That's not the point of the catalog. If you want to advocate for one side or the other on any of these points, I won't try to stop you. But let's at least complete the catalog first, OK?<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Vampire:</b> I'm not familiar enough with the gameline to know, nor do I visit the forum frequently enough to have picked up on anything here. Anyone want to help me out?<br /> \u2022 <b>Werewolf:</b> There are those who dislike the animism baked into the gameline, and have explored ways to strip it out.<br /> \u2022 <b>Mage:</b> I'm not as familiar with this gameline's dissidents; but I know that there are some who try to stretch Mage to handle magic user concepts that it isn't designed to handle.<br /> \u2022 <b>Promethean:</b> This is an easy one: there's a vocal faction that doesn't like the game's focus on becoming human.<br /> \u2022 <b>Changeling:</b> There are some who want a more traditional concept of \u201cchangeling\u201d: a fae thrust into mortal society and trying to fit in.<br /> \u2022 <b>Hunter:</b> some would like to see Hunter support Heroic Mortals: not people with access to Endowments, but hunters who are nevertheless a cut above your average mortal. This ranges from traits designed to mitigate the uneven playing field regular mortals have to deal with all the way to giving hunters a power stat.<br /> \u2022 <b>Geist:</b> I don't know if this qualifies, but I've seen a general misperception of this gameline as \u201cZombie: the Walking Dead\u201d.<br /> \u2022 <b>Mummy:</b> non-Iremite Arisen.<br /> \u2022 <b>Demon:</b> scrapping the tech- overtones.<br /> \u2022 <b>Beast:</b> I don't know. If there's one gameline with which I'm less familiar than Vampire, it's this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's perhaps hypocritucal, but I tend to both remove/ignore portions of the games I don't like, and be deeply perturbed by some people doing it:<br /> -I find the Shadow, Father Wolf and the Werewolves' backkstory awful, and tend to ignore W:tF's fluff altogether.<br /> -I find the obsession of some players and storytellers with non-Iremite mummies <u><i>very</i></u> disturbing.<br /> -I find Beast focus on feeding on humans too vampiric, so I tend to dance around it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:15:05-07:00","id":913161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=912804#post912804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it's possible to play WtF through the eyes of the wolf-blooded, with a Pack that's devoid of Uratha; and there are some wolf-blooded who are effectively shamans. (And there are others that are essentially werewolves \u2014 just not Uratha; good for those who prefer a <i>less</i> spiritual take on werewolves.) Indeed, the one hack I'd make to WtF for those who'd prefer to play it as shamans and spirits would be to<b> introduce a Tell \u2014 or enhance an existing Tell \u2014 that grants the spirit-oriented wolf-blood full access to Rites</b>.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm very impressed at how accommodating WtF is of \u201cnon-standard\u201d styles of play.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Pack</i>, p.31 has you covered.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:36:22-07:00","id":913166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=913161#post913161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Pack</i>, p.31 has you covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it does. I had been thinking in terms of granting such benefits on an individual basis; but it makes sense for it to be a Pack thing \u2014 though I'd remove the \u201cyou can't have any Uratha\u201d clause from Moon's Grace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:49:39-07:00","id":913170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=913166#post913166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed it does. I had been thinking in terms of granting such benefits on an individual basis; but it makes sense for it to be a Pack thing \u2014 though I'd remove the \u201cyou can't have any Uratha\u201d clause from Moon's Grace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it, it won't break the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T22:03:05-07:00","id":913231,"title":"","content":"I've joked before that my ideal Werewolf chronicle is one where all the players are freshly-Embraced Gangrel, frenzying all the time and terrified of eating people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T06:47:24-07:00","id":914062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=912804#post912804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I'm very impressed at how accommodating WtF is of \u201cnon-standard\u201d styles of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still wish Lupus were a thing. The idea of playing a pet that now gets to do all those people things was something I really wanted to do in Apocalypse. Like the <i>only</i> thing. I wanted to be a wolfdog who had her Change and absolutely loved being a person. The concept was a Lupus Glasswalker Galliard (although due to Rage, that doesn't exactly work out in oWoD either). But the chances of me finding a Werewolf game where I'm not the one running it, and also I get the okay to play a wolfwere and <i>also</i> that's not a one time amazing unique thing but something that just happens and people don't find it weird...<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=913101#post913101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's perhaps hypocritucal, but I tend to both remove/ignore portions of the games I don't like, and be deeply perturbed by some people doing it:<br /> -I find the Shadow, Father Wolf and the Werewolves' backkstory awful, and tend to ignore W:tF's fluff altogether.<br /> -I find the obsession of some players and storytellers with non-Iremite mummies <u><i>very</i></u> disturbing.<br /> -I find Beast focus on feeding on humans too vampiric, so I tend to dance around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you find it so disturbing? Or perturbing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:40:29-07:00","id":914198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914062#post914062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still wish Lupus were a thing. The idea of playing a pet that now gets to do all those people things was something I really wanted to do in Apocalypse. Like the <i>only</i> thing. I wanted to be a wolfdog who had her Change and absolutely loved being a person. The concept was a Lupus Glasswalker Galliard (although due to Rage, that doesn't exactly work out in oWoD either). But the chances of me finding a Werewolf game where I'm not the one running it, and also I get the okay to play a wolfwere and <i>also</i> that's not a one time amazing unique thing but something that just happens and people don't find it weird...</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about that one, which is very much on point for this topic. In fact, I even worked up a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken\">hack for that</a>, with generous advice from the WtF community. Which reminds me, I should get back to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T13:03:50-07:00","id":914300,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I think someone showed me Stew's Urhanu and my reply was to come up with my own hack for lupus:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>My hack</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your original form is a wolf :V</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T13:11:46-07:00","id":914311,"title":"","content":"That's the basic idea, yes; but there are implications that need to be considered. I've just released <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914222-forsaken-youths\">my latest iteration of the concept</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:10:56-07:00","id":914511,"title":"","content":"Replying to the topic and at risk of opening the old scab wound:<br /> <br /> The design choice of hard coding mortals to forget everything about the supernatural rather than the idea that they know about it but simply don't want to admit to it and would rather just drop it in the core game.<br /> <br /> One invites mystery, wonder, and the agency to encounter worlds beyond this if one only has the courage to pursue. Other simply closes the door on these things.<br /> <br /> I've already said my piece on this many a time and won't get into it but figured it was relevant to mention here. <br /> <br /> That being said, my other opinion comes as follows:<br /> <br /> WoD markets it's self as first and foremost, a horror game. The problem is a sizeable camp of players don't play it as such. They play it as either Urban Fantasy or Dark Urban Fantasy. Which is fine for the most part but leads to such things as downplaying the Abuse and Trauma themes of Changeling or the pains of Alienation of Promethean which isn't what the game is designed for. But in the end, the game is in the players, not the developer's hands when it comes to these things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:36:05-07:00","id":914532,"title":"","content":"Yes, I'm not a fan of the turn towards Urban Fantasy over Horror either. I don't think it's solely a thing players are doing, either. Sometimes it's in the books and can make the writing seem disjointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:45:37-07:00","id":914545,"title":"","content":"It's a tough disconnect because games like Vampire or Promethean really nail the horror themes while it takes some work to bring theme to the forefront in Werewolf or Mage. And all that's before you get the players who care more about the novelty of a supernatural modern world or getting to play as the monsters than any of the major themes and metaphors behind these games.<br /> <br /> I've been accused one one-true-wayism before, but it feels like a disservice to come at a game like Changeling and run it as &quot;wow, it's so much fun to be a magical knight in my home city!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:58:24-07:00","id":914555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914545#post914545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a tough disconnect because games like Vampire or Promethean really nail the horror themes while it takes some work to bring theme to the forefront in Werewolf or Mage. And all that's before you get the players who care more about the novelty of a supernatural modern world or getting to play as the monsters than any of the major themes and metaphors behind these games.<br /> <br /> I've been accused one one-true-wayism before, but it feels like a disservice to come at a game like Changeling and run it as &quot;wow, it's so much fun to be a magical knight in my home city!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I think that novelty is a big draw for a lot of players. It's what got me into CofD, honestly. I wasn't really interested in playing out deep, tragic horror stories that examine what it means to be human, I just wanted to dress up all goth and hang out pretending to be a vampire with other people in cool costumes, and setting it in my college town added an appealing semi-ARG element to it. I fell in love with the games because of the compelling stories that I realized could be told with them, but it certainly wasn't the reason I started playing. So, I'm at least sympathetic to those who want to downplay the personal horror, even if I think they're missing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:01:43-07:00","id":914558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914555#post914555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. I think that novelty is a big draw for a lot of players. It's what got me into CofD, honestly. I wasn't really interested in playing out deep, tragic horror stories that examine what it means to be human, I just wanted to dress up all goth and hang out pretending to be a vampire with other people in cool costumes, and setting it in my college town added an appealing semi-ARG element to it. I fell in love with the games because of the compelling stories that I realized could be told with them, but it certainly wasn't the reason I started playing. So, I'm at least sympathetic to those who want to downplay the personal horror, even if I think they're missing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>A part of me has to wonder if the CofD couldn't benefit from stealing the &quot;modes of play&quot; idea that several GUMSHOE games have been busting out recently. Trail of Cthulhu has the Pulp/Purist dichotomy, with the former being two-fisted action where the heroes shoot and dynamite dozens of Deep Ones while the latter is all about your sanity shattering because you saw a pack of ghouls. <br /> <br /> There's a little bit of this in the Demon Storyteller's Guide, but I honestly feel like that's a section that belongs in the corebook more than anything else; being able to approach your group before the chronicle even starts and saying &quot;what level of grit and horror do we want from this?&quot; with mechanics to back it up would be a godsend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:07:16-07:00","id":914565,"title":"","content":"I'm a major personal horror advocate too (despite having a fondness for pulp, action, and fantasy stories), which is exactly why the elements of ChroD that I don't like rub me the wrong way- I actually don't think Werewolf has much of a problem with it, since ChroD's sort of horror is about BEING a monster, and Forsaken (esp 2e) hammers in that being Good Werewolf Spirit Cop Human Defender is a hard fucking thing to be, and even if you pull it off you're gonna have be leaving bodies in your wake. <br /> <br /> Mage and Promethean have the most problems with being personal horror games to me- Mages are too shiny and enlightened and Prometheans have their handy little escape hatch (and they're Playing Wrong if they don't pursue it). Beast has this problem in a lesser way- Beasts are undeniably monstrous, but the game makes constant excuses for them and treats them like 3edgy5u coolkids who are just misunderstood, maaaaaaan. One of the reasons I like Leviathan more (in addition to the more coherent themes and setting) is that it really goes into how being an ancient primordial monster who fucks with people's minds without even meaning to would fucking suck if you actually want to live a stable life with meaningful relationships. <br /> <br /> Leviathan is a near perfect example of how to do personal &quot;you are the monster&quot; horror- you're an ancient and incredibly powerful being who could probably bench a tank, but at the end of the day you have to face the very real possibility that the world would be better off without you, and the guys with ray guns chasing you might be right after all. That's a hell of a lot scarier than &quot;you're totally helping humanity by terrorizing them and the people who want to stop you are just dorks&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Atamajakki, you hit the nail right on the head with that one. If there's ever a New New World of Darkness or a Chronicles of Darkness 3e that deserves to be in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:10:35-07:00","id":914566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914062#post914062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you find it so disturbing? Or perturbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a lot of the time it merely comes down to people not wanting to play mummies from the Middle East or Africa. Not all the time mind you, but still often enough for me to feel uncomfortable around those discussions when they pop up, and around hose who press for playing non-Iremite mummies again and again.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:30:57-07:00","id":914579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914566#post914566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because a lot of the time it merely comes down to people not wanting to play mummies from the Middle East or Africa. Not all the time mind you, but still often enough for me to feel uncomfortable around those discussions when they pop up, and around hose who press for playing non-Iremite mummies again and again.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this. A lot of the time &quot;I don't want to play someone from Irem&quot; is followed by &quot;I want to play someone white instead,&quot; and that's just a bad time for everyone involved in the conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:35:10-07:00","id":914619,"title":"","content":"Also, Mummy is a game that's limited in a lot of ways, but the limits are because it's designed to be much less of a &quot;sandbox&quot; and more of a weird experimental game about playing through the tragedy of Irem and its children, and limiting it to Iremites is kind of necessary with that in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:52:04-07:00","id":914634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914579#post914579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seconding this. A lot of the time &amp;quot;I don't want to play someone from Irem&amp;quot; is followed by &amp;quot;I want to play someone white instead,&amp;quot; and that's just a bad time for everyone involved in the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? I've never noticed that. Usually, I see it followed by requests for South American or Asian mummies. Not that there's anything wrong with being Caucasian, mind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:59:22-07:00","id":914641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914579#post914579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seconding this. A lot of the time &quot;I don't want to play someone from Irem&quot; is followed by &quot;I want to play someone white instead,&quot; and that's just a bad time for everyone involved in the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This first time the conversation ever came up, it was done because the OP wanted to play a white character instead of a black/brown person. True Story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T21:02:31-07:00","id":914643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914641#post914641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This first time the conversation ever came up, it was done because the OP wanted to play a white character instead of a black/brown person. True Story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'd totally play Mesopotamian mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T21:06:40-07:00","id":914646,"title":"","content":"Not that I doubt it, I've only heard people asking for Chinese and South American mummies. But they may have been Chinese or South American.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T23:11:27-07:00","id":914694,"title":"","content":"If I were asking for non-Iremite Mummies, it would be because Irem is lame and &quot;Mummies from Egypt&quot; is done to death. Then again, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mummy:_Tomb_of_the_Dragon_Emperor\" target=\"_blank\">Chinese Mummies are kind of dumb</a>. <span style=\"font-size:9px\">I'm pretty sure I still enjoyed that movie, even if I can't remember anything about it</span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar604_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"604\" data-vbnamecard=\"604\">Shock</a> Urban Fantasy <i>is</i> horror. I wish I could remember the quote, but paraphrasing something from an UrbFan anthology: &quot;Urban fantasy is the love child of gothic horror and noir&quot;. I mean, sure, it often ends up being a horror that you can show on daytime TV (Vampire Diaries, Twilight, Mortal Instruments, The Magicians, both versions of Being Human, Teen Wolf, even Buffy) but it's still <i>horror</i>, even if every moment isn't dripping with guts and gore. It's important to keep in mind that horror isn't limited to TV-14+. Although if you mean the kind of people who ignore the Morality system and don't care about any sort of consequences, then yeah, I definitely hate that. I just think it's wrong to say that's &quot;urban fantasy and not horror&quot;. I mean, Dresden Files is the <i>Ur</i>-example these days, and half of Dresden's friends are dead, he's had to make hard choices, and I'm like 90% sure he was either raped or basically raped. And that's on top of the actual spooky Halloween horror of ghosts and monsters.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914545#post914545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been accused one one-true-wayism before, but it feels like a disservice to come at a game like Changeling and run it as &quot;wow, it's so much fun to be a magical knight in my home city!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's the Spring Court's whole outlook. I also <i>do</i> think there's a bit of room for a non-abusive Keeper story. I mean, a relationship doesn't really have to have been abusive to change you. Although admittedly I like the idea of &quot;he was always so nice to me...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T23:56:25-07:00","id":914701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914694#post914694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar604_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"604\" data-vbnamecard=\"604\">Shock</a> Urban Fantasy <i>is</i> horror. I wish I could remember the quote, but paraphrasing something from an UrbFan anthology: &quot;Urban fantasy is the love child of gothic horror and noir&quot;. I mean, sure, it often ends up being a horror that you can show on daytime TV (Vampire Diaries, Twilight, Mortal Instruments, The Magicians, both versions of Being Human, Teen Wolf, even Buffy) but it's still <i>horror</i>, even if every moment isn't dripping with guts and gore. It's important to keep in mind that horror isn't limited to TV-14+. Although if you mean the kind of people who ignore the Morality system and don't care about any sort of consequences, then yeah, I definitely hate that. I just think it's wrong to say that's &quot;urban fantasy and not horror&quot;. I mean, Dresden Files is the <i>Ur</i>-example these days, and half of Dresden's friends are dead, he's had to make hard choices, and I'm like 90% sure he was either raped or basically raped. And that's on top of the actual spooky Halloween horror of ghosts and monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Urban Fantasy is a broader genre than that, but &quot;horror&quot; is a reasonable genre descriptor of a lot of urban fantasy media, definitely.<br /> <br /> There's a Venn diagram or something here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T02:16:14-07:00","id":914723,"title":"","content":"I disagree 100% with the notion that Urban Fantasy is some off-shot of the Horror genre. The Horror genre, much as the implicit themes of the games produced by White-Wolf, focus on the immersion on a supernatural creature to explore it's metaphors out of the dramatics of such an existence, and while you can have an Urban Fantasy work feature elements of it, just like High Fantasy can, it's intended purpose is considerably more light-hearted.<br /> <br /> In fact, the need to actually amend the elements of aversion within the different games is what strips the work of it's patina of Horror.<br /> <br /> The difference between an element such as rape as presented in a work of fantasy, compared to one of horror is that in the work of fantasy, it's used to elicit a sympathetic response for the character(s) involved, while in horror it is to add repugnance to the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-15-2016, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T02:51:47-07:00","id":914728,"title":"","content":"Horror doesn't require the supernatural at all. I also don't think I've ever seen an urban fantasy series that wasn't in what I'd consider the horror genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T02:57:10-07:00","id":914729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914728#post914728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horror doesn't require the supernatural at all. I also don't think I've ever seen an urban fantasy series that wasn't in what I'd consider the horror genre.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying supernatural elements are required for horror.<br /> <br /> Fantasy is grounded in the otherworldly elements of romance. Gothic Horror is a combination of such elements and the Gothic atmosphere, plus tragedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T04:45:53-07:00","id":914747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914694#post914694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar604_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"604\" data-vbnamecard=\"604\">Shock</a> Urban Fantasy <i>is</i> horror. I wish I could remember the quote, but paraphrasing something from an UrbFan anthology: &quot;Urban fantasy is the love child of gothic horror and noir&quot;. I mean, sure, it often ends up being a horror that you can show on daytime TV (Vampire Diaries, Twilight, Mortal Instruments, The Magicians, both versions of Being Human, Teen Wolf, even Buffy) but it's still <i>horror</i>, even if every moment isn't dripping with guts and gore. It's important to keep in mind that horror isn't limited to TV-14+.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't. Urban fantasy often but not always has the trappings of horror, otherwise not much beyond it.<br /> <br /> And no one said horror was limited to some age or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2016, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T09:45:05-07:00","id":914880,"title":"","content":"None of those shows are horror. A quick Wikipedia definition tells us that &quot;Horror is a film genre seeking to elicit a negative emotional reaction from viewers by playing on the audience's primal fears.&quot; The shows you listed all feature monsters and/or the supernatural, but they're played for drama, romance, and even comedy in the case of Buffy, not for fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T09:52:48-07:00","id":914884,"title":"","content":"This opinion may help? <a href=\"http://io9.gizmodo.com/the-key-difference-between-urban-fantasy-and-horror-1749628499\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.gizmodo.com/the-key-diffe...ror-1749628499</a> I was going to use the protagonist's response as an explanation for the difference in my comment, but I wasn't feeling terribly coherent last night.<br /> <br /> I've also used the term &quot;dark fantasy&quot; to describe stuff in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:08:42-07:00","id":914893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914884#post914884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This opinion may help? <a href=\"http://io9.gizmodo.com/the-key-difference-between-urban-fantasy-and-horror-1749628499\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.gizmodo.com/the-key-diffe...ror-1749628499</a> I was going to use the protagonist's response as an explanation for the difference in my comment, but I wasn't feeling terribly coherent last night.<br /> <br /> I've also used the term &quot;dark fantasy&quot; to describe stuff in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I agree with that either. I would say Supernatural is an example of a popular TV show that, while it certainly fits the definition of Urban Fantasy, does straddle the line into horror. The Winchesters are supremely capable protagonists, regularly killing demons, Angels, gods, and in the post-season 5, stranger things like progenitor monsters and what ever the heck Leviathins were supposed to be. However, the show regularly plays on the audience's primal fears to evoke negative emotional responses. It disempowers the protagonists to the point where &quot;why don't the Winchesters just attach their weapons to their arms with bungie chords?&quot; was something actually brought up in the show. They display horrific and gruesome death scenes at the beginning of most episodes. They constantly escalate the stakes so that no matter how competent the Winchesters are, they are somehow still always in over their heads (which, to be fair, is a big part of why I stopped watching). Eliciting fear responses is clearly a significant part of the intent of the show, even if it also contains elements of drama, comedy, and urban fantasy. That's why I loved it for the first five seasons, it was a complex and multi-layered show, and evoked a lot of what I love about Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:24:06-07:00","id":914902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914884#post914884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This opinion may help? <a href=\"http://io9.gizmodo.com/the-key-difference-between-urban-fantasy-and-horror-1749628499\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.gizmodo.com/the-key-diffe...ror-1749628499</a> I was going to use the protagonist's response as an explanation for the difference in my comment, but I wasn't feeling terribly coherent last night.<br /> <br /> I've also used the term &quot;dark fantasy&quot; to describe stuff in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>The counterpoint is that a character in the horror genre can be competent if the author displays him struggling with the ramifications of how to deal with the conflict, before, during or after the fact.<br /> <br /> Specially if logic and rationality is ultimately not the answer to end said conflict. This is why I love spirits so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-15-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:56:37-07:00","id":914916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914893#post914893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eliciting fear responses is clearly a significant part of the intent of the show, even if it also contains elements of drama, comedy, and urban fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to highlight this: dropping any single piece of media into a definitive genre bucket is frequently really hard. That a lot of media that's primarily urban fantasy will overlap with horror, or vice versa, is really not that unusual. It doesn't necessarily mean they're the same thing, but overlaps can definitely make it seem that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:00:23-07:00","id":914920,"title":"","content":"Boy, this thread has taken a long, strange path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:07:15-07:00","id":914925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914916#post914916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to highlight this: dropping any single piece of media into a definitive genre bucket is frequently really hard. That a lot of media that's primarily urban fantasy will overlap with horror, or vice versa, is really not that unusual. It doesn't necessarily mean they're the same thing, but overlaps can definitely make it seem that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue here is that endeavoring to strip the games from their editorially unpleasant themes works directly towards a genre shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:22:58-07:00","id":914933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914920#post914920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boy, this thread has taken a long, strange path.</div> </div> </div> </div>The urban fantasy and horror division was actually brought up in the first few posts, it just didn't explicitly call out the genre shift.<br /> <br /> As a vampire one is on the road to the complete loss of Humanity, the becoming of an uncontrollable monster. Requiem, the game, is about dealing with that fact and attempting to find a place where you are alright with what you are, but this will often come at the sacrifice of others, or doing profoundly monstrous things in a way the vampire can deal with. Once you take the loss of Humanity aspect from the game, you are dealing with a human who has superpowers fueled in a certain way and weaknesses they must deal with.<br /> <br /> A lot of the other things people wanted to change about games, not counting making them more like old World of Darkness, shift them from monsters with a horrific theme to the more supernatural superhero-type characters you see in urban fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2016, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T12:50:13-07:00","id":914999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914933#post914933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the other things people wanted to change about games, not counting making them more like old World of Darkness, shift them from monsters with a horrific theme to the more supernatural superhero-type characters you see in urban fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that why I balk at so many of the same changes that pop up all the time.<br /> <br /> Vampires out in the sunlight. Vampires with less risks to their Humanity.<br /> Werewolves that can wander around in War Form without a second thought.<br /> Werewolves and Mages that don't lose control of themselves.<br /> Mages who get to practice magic without any consequences.<br /> Prometheans who either don't want to be human or don't have to deal with the downside of being Created.<br /> Changelings who were never taken/kept under unpleasant circumstances. Changelings who get to just &quot;let it all hang out&quot; and don't have to hide.<br /> Hunters who aren't fighting a losing battle. Hunters who can always come out on top against the supernatural. Hunters who just wanna be friends with the creatures.<br /> Sin-Eaters who want to be in total sync with their Geists so there's no conflict. Sin-Eaters who don't feel compelled by their Geists, but get to do what they want.<br /> <br /> Of course, some of the God-Machine/X Chronicles/2nd Edition changes seem to be drifting away from that, so maybe the Chronicles are aiming for dark/urban fantasy rather than horror. To me, the line is drawn where the monster begins/ends. Dark/urban fantasy has monsters <b>in it</b> and the characters have to deal with that. Horror has the characters <b>as </b>the monsters and they have to deal with that. Dark/urban fantasy has the characters fight against the monsters and <b>win</b>. Horror has the characters fight the monsters and <b>lose</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T13:00:29-07:00","id":915009,"title":"","content":"Have you been reading the same second edition I have? Because from what I've been reading, every second edition like has re-emphasized and doubled down on the horror themes of the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T13:42:30-07:00","id":915052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915009#post915009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you been reading the same second edition I have? Because from what I've been reading, every second edition like has re-emphasized and doubled down on the horror themes of the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding that notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:15:01-07:00","id":915068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914999#post914999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires out in the sunlight. Vampires with less risks to their Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet the very act of being slowly baked by the sun reminds you that you're fundamentally not human. Less risks to humanity, you say? When the mere act of joining a Covenant is one?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914999#post914999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves that can wander around in War Form without a second thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Risking breaking points for not using said form for it's sacred purpose is hardly what I'd call &quot;without a second thought&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914999#post914999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves and Mages that don't lose control of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox. Kuruth. Enough said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914999#post914999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages who get to practice magic without any consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't even being to imagine from where you've coined this notion. Magic always has a consequence. <i>Always</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914999#post914999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans who either don't want to be human or don't have to deal with the downside of being Created.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans off the path to the Great Work were always a thing. Wasteland and Disquiet were always a thing.<br /> <br /> I won't comment on the other lines because I haven't read anything of the sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:17:48-07:00","id":915069,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely sure but I believe Papa Bear had two separate points, the first list being changes people want to games and that they have in their own, but aren't official. The second, in paragraph form, was more directed at official works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:32:24-07:00","id":915083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915069#post915069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely sure but I believe Papa Bear had two separate points, the first list being changes people want to games and that they have in their own, but aren't official. The second, in paragraph form, was more directed at official works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, clearly I was not clear. I'll just bow out. As Charlaquin and Arc have pointed out, I'm hardly up to speed on the latest texts and tomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:55:38-07:00","id":915109,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> But by this definition...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greg Cox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sometimes seems to me that the main difference between urban fantasy and horror is simply a matter of competency. Urban fantasy characters generally take vampires and zombies in stride and react as competently as the reader would like to think they would do in similar straits.<br /> Horror characters, on the hand, tend to freak out, panic, doubt their sanity, make unwise decisions,, or even descend into gibbering madness\u2014which is probably the more realistic approach!<br /> I know people who simply don\u2019t get or can\u2019t tolerate horror because they expect the protagonists to be as matter-of-fact as, say, Buffy when dealing with weird paranormal threats.<br /> THEY: \u201cWell, why don\u2019t they just go out and buy some silver bullets instead of freaking out over their werewolf issue?\u201d<br /> ME: \u201cBecause horror is not about problem-solving. It\u2019s about fear and guilt and madness and darkness, not competence. And, honestly, most normal people would not behave rationally when confronted with an actual ghost or succubi.\u201d<br /> Yes, this is a debate I\u2019ve had many times.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>None</i> of the <s>World</s>Chronicles of Darkness games are about horror by that definition. When was the last time your splat character freaked out about the monsters they face? Which is why I once again bring up the slew of Urban Fantasy shows. Yeah, they're not eliciting negative emotions primarily, but I feel that's not really an accurate summation of what Horror is. After all, an anime about high school girls has elicited fear and revulsion from me, but it was a romance drama, not &quot;Horror&quot;. Worth noting is that most of those shows <i>are</i> listed as Horror on Wikipedia, except for <i>Shadowhunters</i> (which is what the <i>Mortal Instruments</i> show is called) and <i>The Magicians</i>, though since <a href=\"https://youtu.be/3qXpTOWyshg\" target=\"_blank\">this is the only thing I've seen of <i>The Magicians</i></a>, I'm going to say that at least that scene is pretty horror. (Twilight didn't get thrown a bone). I disagree that Horror is about competency, though, just as I disagree that Horror is solely about negative emotions, because in that case, Drama <i>is</i> horror. My heart hurts more and I feel worse when watching a romance anime than when I watch <i>Halloween 18: Michael Myers is Pretty Mean</i>, even if one conjures images of unstoppable serial murderers lurking in the unlit hallways and the other doesn't. So clearly the trappings matter.<br /> Every urban fantasy setting I've seen has had the same kinds of horror that the CofD games do. You're rarely afraid of the Thing, you're afraid of what the Thing can do. More than that, you're afraid of what <i>you</i> might do in pursuit of your goals. One of the constant plots of the UK <i>Being Human</i> (and maybe the US one) is how the bad vampires are trying to get Mitchell to fall off the wagon. George is worried about flipping out and murdering everyone. In Buffy, yeah, it's got comedy, but she's also worried about how Slaying will effect her future, how it'll effect her family, and yeah, how it will effect her love life. Hell, every commercial I've seen for <i>The Vampire Diaries</i> is &quot;oh no, they're going to find out about The Thing!&quot; and worrying about what the fallout might be. <i>Supernatural</i> is all about Sam and Dean's relationship, and later Castiel, and later apparently Crowley or something but I lost track at that point. Sure, the fate of the world is at stake, but who cares about losing the world if you lose your family?<br /> All of those things? Those are the kind of horror that shows up in my games. You're a teenage Hunter. What do the teachers think when they see their bruises? What will your parents say when they see your report card (or will they even care)? What are you going to do when you get caught trespassing at 2am? Or maybe you're a Mage who's given up on having a mortal life. The Acamoth doesn't scare you because it's a horrible abomination from outside reality. It scares you because it wants to break you. Because it gives you an offer that, maybe, is just too good to refuse. As a Vampire, what scares you more: The thought of your rivals breaking your limbs and seeing if you can survive the morning on the roof, or your rivals finding out about the prostitute that you take to Denny's every Sunday, and doing the same to him? What makes that scenario less Horror when you change from a vampire to a crime boss who has a platonic affection for a rentboy? Why is it Horror if <i>Supernatural</i> shows a grisly death at the beginning of every episode, but not when CSI or Law &amp; Order does it? And at this point, the only Law &amp; Order on the air is the one about sex crimes, which most people would consider pretty horrible.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915009#post915009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you been reading the same second edition I have? Because from what I've been reading, every second edition like has re-emphasized and doubled down on the horror themes of the line.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915052#post915052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding that notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are no longer the ones in <i>From Dusk Til Dawn</i> or <i>John Carpenters: </i><i>Vampires</i>, where they explode into gouts of flame when they walk into the sun. Werewolves are actually worth a damn in combat. Paradox is more easily managed without the existence of Vulgar magic. Disquiet is no longer because you're a horrible abomination and everything about you is wrong and disgusting. There's also the fact that overall the second edition gamelines are much <i>stronger</i>, both mechanically and narratively. Demons can do things right out of the gate that are sequence breakingly powerful. Werewolves can cripple or outright flatten anything they come across. Beasts powers are one long list of ways to ruin someone's day. Even vampires no longer have to fear a gang of lucky thugs, and Mages, well, Mages can create earthquakes and invert gravity as starting characters.<br /> Like I said above, I don't consider strong or competent characters to be antithetical to horror, but I can see why some people feel that way. But, also like I said above, I don't see the horror of these games to be about bodily harm or really even sanity. It's the horror of what you'll have to do, and the horror of what might be done to you in an existential or social way. Honestly, in that regard, <i>Werewolf</i>, the game where you're the biggest badass motherfucker (to the point that its even codified as a power!) is the one with the strongest Horror elements. The horror isn't the spirits or the Hosts, the Horror is <i>you</i>, and the potential loss of control you have to manage to keep those spirits and hosts and other werewolves and humans and claimed and stranger things besides from hurting you and yours. Every time you go into battle, there's the chance that you might murder everyone you know and love, but that's the only way to keep them safe.<br /> <br /> Although, really, if we're going to talk about how some people want to play the games as <i>not</i> being Horror, we'd really have to agree on what <i>is</i> Horror, and I don't really think that's likely to happen. Charlaquin called <i>Supernatural</i> Horror, but Buffy not Horror. I'm sure for at least someone out there, the opposite is true. Neither of them seem entirely fitting with the simple definition of &quot;designed to elicit negative emotions such as fear, shock, or revulsion&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-15-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T15:21:11-07:00","id":915128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When was the last time your splat character freaked out about the monsters they face? </div> </div> </div>Fairly often. In the last game I ran, the coterie of vampires routinely ran from such threats. Strix, idigam, angels of the God Machine are not there so players can wonder at their beauty. They're threats the players don't have good ways to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being Human...Vampire Diaries...Supernatural... </div> </div> </div>This is drama. It's an important element in storytelling. It does not make horror or fantasy. The way you play is not the same way everyone else does. That's fine, but it doesn't speak for the genre as a whole, or even the books as written. Which is the entire point of this thread. It's okay to admit that, many people play their games differently.<br /> <br /> As someone points out in every 'what would you be' thread, you don't really want to be in the Chronicles of Darkness. If you're playing the game as a form of wish-fulfillment, you're likely verging into fantasy territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:03:35-07:00","id":915157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915128#post915128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone points out in every 'what would you be' thread, you don't really want to be in the Chronicles of Darkness. If you're playing the game as a form of wish-fulfillment, you're likely verging into fantasy territory.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think this is the broadest pitfall. I can totally sympathize with focusing on aspects other than the horror and providing more hopeful moments for contrast. I've even been considering a <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Noblebright\" target=\"_blank\"><b>noblebright</b></a> (NSFW ads) feel for my next game. But I agree that you shouldn't play CoD mainly for wish-fulfillment.<br /> <br /> Another change that I often see proposed for Mage is the removal of the Gnostic and Platonic parts. This encompasses everything from taking away Quiescence/Dissonance/Paradox to inserting pieces from Ascension that clash with Awakening's lore. The latter can be done well (see Pendragon's homebrew), but the underlying assumptions about the workings of magic and the cosmos itself are very different in each game. You have to think it through, or you'll probably run into plot holes and conflicting rules. As always, the Translation Guide is your friend.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:22:25-07:00","id":915173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915109#post915109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> But by this definition...<br /> <i>None</i> of the <s>World</s>Chronicles of Darkness games are about horror by that definition. When was the last time your splat character freaked out about the monsters they face?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Points at the stupidly high number of conditions that merely facing a monster's aura, be it predatory, hunter aspect, or nimbus is capable of inflicting. Monster or no monster.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:27:01-07:00","id":915174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915109#post915109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> But by this definition...<br /> <i>None</i> of the <s>World</s>Chronicles of Darkness games are about horror by that definition. When was the last time your splat character freaked out about the monsters they face? Which is why I once again bring up the slew of Urban Fantasy shows. Yeah, they're not eliciting negative emotions primarily, but I feel that's not really an accurate summation of what Horror is. After all, an anime about high school girls has elicited fear and revulsion from me, but it was a romance drama, not &quot;Horror&quot;. Worth noting is that most of those shows <i>are</i> listed as Horror on Wikipedia, except for <i>Shadowhunters</i> (which is what the <i>Mortal Instruments</i> show is called) and <i>The Magicians</i>, though since <a href=\"https://youtu.be/3qXpTOWyshg\" target=\"_blank\">this is the only thing I've seen of <i>The Magicians</i></a>, I'm going to say that at least that scene is pretty horror. (Twilight didn't get thrown a bone). I disagree that Horror is about competency, though, just as I disagree that Horror is solely about negative emotions, because in that case, Drama <i>is</i> horror. My heart hurts more and I feel worse when watching a romance anime than when I watch <i>Halloween 18: Michael Myers is Pretty Mean</i>, even if one conjures images of unstoppable serial murderers lurking in the unlit hallways and the other doesn't. So clearly the trappings matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that protagonist competency is not a good yardstick for horror. As for drama being horror because it elicits negative emotions, I think you latched onto the wrong part of &quot;seeking to elicit a negative emotional reaction from viewers by playing on the audience's primal fears.&quot; In horror, fear is the tool used to elicit negative emotions. In drama, tragedy is. There is often overlap between the two genres, but to me it's not monsters that make a work horror, it's the intent to frighten.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915109#post915109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every urban fantasy setting I've seen has had the same kinds of horror that the CofD games do. You're rarely afraid of the Thing, you're afraid of what the Thing can do. More than that, you're afraid of what <i>you</i> might do in pursuit of your goals. One of the constant plots of the UK <i>Being Human</i> (and maybe the US one) is how the bad vampires are trying to get Mitchell to fall off the wagon. George is worried about flipping out and murdering everyone. In Buffy, yeah, it's got comedy, but she's also worried about how Slaying will effect her future, how it'll effect her family, and yeah, how it will effect her love life. Hell, every commercial I've seen for <i>The Vampire Diaries</i> is &quot;oh no, they're going to find out about The Thing!&quot; and worrying about what the fallout might be. <i>Supernatural</i> is all about Sam and Dean's relationship, and later Castiel, and later apparently Crowley or something but I lost track at that point. Sure, the fate of the world is at stake, but who cares about losing the world if you lose your family?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would call all of that drama. The catharsis here comes from tragedy, from friction in interpersonal relationships. It doesn't come from playing on primal fears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915109#post915109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of those things? Those are the kind of horror that shows up in my games. You're a teenage Hunter. What do the teachers think when they see their bruises? What will your parents say when they see your report card (or will they even care)? What are you going to do when you get caught trespassing at 2am? Or maybe you're a Mage who's given up on having a mortal life. The Acamoth doesn't scare you because it's a horrible abomination from outside reality. It scares you because it wants to break you. Because it gives you an offer that, maybe, is just too good to refuse. As a Vampire, what scares you more: The thought of your rivals breaking your limbs and seeing if you can survive the morning on the roof, or your rivals finding out about the prostitute that you take to Denny's every Sunday, and doing the same to him? What makes that scenario less Horror when you change from a vampire to a crime boss who has a platonic affection for a rentboy? Why is it Horror if <i>Supernatural</i> shows a grisly death at the beginning of every episode, but not when CSI or Law &amp; Order does it? And at this point, the only Law &amp; Order on the air is the one about sex crimes, which most people would consider pretty horrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>My whole point is that a work doesn't have to feature spooky halloween monsters to be horror, it has to play on fear. Frankly, CSI and Law &amp; Order <i>do</i> fit the definition of horror far, far better than Buffy the Vampire Slayer (and that's not a knock against Buffy - as a lot of folks probably know, I am a huge fan of the show). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915109#post915109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are no longer the ones in <i>From Dusk Til Dawn</i> or <i>John Carpenters: </i><i>Vampires</i>, where they explode into gouts of flame when they walk into the sun. Werewolves are actually worth a damn in combat. Paradox is more easily managed without the existence of Vulgar magic. Disquiet is no longer because you're a horrible abomination and everything about you is wrong and disgusting. There's also the fact that overall the second edition gamelines are much <i>stronger</i>, both mechanically and narratively. Demons can do things right out of the gate that are sequence breakingly powerful. Werewolves can cripple or outright flatten anything they come across. Beasts powers are one long list of ways to ruin someone's day. Even vampires no longer have to fear a gang of lucky thugs, and Mages, well, Mages can create earthquakes and invert gravity as starting characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elders absolutely still explode into flame as soon as they walk into the sun, it's only new vampires that can stand short-term exposure to sunlight. That makes the horror all the more compelling because you can actually watch yourself gradually losing your ability to walk in the sunlight as your Humanity slips away. Werewolves <i>should</i> be worth a damn in combat, because part of the horror of Werewolf comes from taking a step back and looking at what you're capable of and what might happen if you lose yourself to Kuruth at the wrong time (or actually doing so). Paradox is considerably more insidious without the distinction between Vulgar and Covert magic because you can no longer just avoid casting Vulgar spells. <i>Any</i> spell can cause Paradox if you let your reach exceed your grasp, and the fact that it's relatively easy for new mages to manage and gets more and more difficult as their Gnosis increases is far more compelling, for similar reasons to why it's better for vampires to lose the ability to walk in the sun gradually. Disquiet being a thing because you're a Thing That Should Not Be never really made any sense, because it implied that there was some objective standard by which to judge whether or not things Should Be. The change to Disquiet is just giving an actual reason to why they &quot;Should Not Be&quot; - the Divine Fire within them is too hot for the rest of the living world to handle. There's an actual reason that everything about them is wrong and disgusting, instead of it just being something we are informed of with no satisfactory explanation. And yes, supernatural creatures are stronger mechanically and narratively. That strengthens the feeling of external horror in mortal games because the monsters can do more horrible things to you than ever, and it strengthens the feeling of personal horror for supernatural games because you can do more horrible things to innocent people than ever. For someone who claims to prefer horror to come from within, I would expect you to appreciate that playing a character that is capable of such things is intensely horrifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915109#post915109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said above, I don't consider strong or competent characters to be antithetical to horror, but I can see why some people feel that way. But, also like I said above, I don't see the horror of these games to be about bodily harm or really even sanity. It's the horror of what you'll have to do, and the horror of what might be done to you in an existential or social way. Honestly, in that regard, <i>Werewolf</i>, the game where you're the biggest badass motherfucker (to the point that its even codified as a power!) is the one with the strongest Horror elements. The horror isn't the spirits or the Hosts, the Horror is <i>you</i>, and the potential loss of control you have to manage to keep those spirits and hosts and other werewolves and humans and claimed and stranger things besides from hurting you and yours. Every time you go into battle, there's the chance that you might murder everyone you know and love, but that's the only way to keep them safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... agree with all of this? It also seems completely inconsistent with everything else you have said in this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915109#post915109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, really, if we're going to talk about how some people want to play the games as <i>not</i> being Horror, we'd really have to agree on what <i>is</i> Horror, and I don't really think that's likely to happen. Charlaquin called <i>Supernatural</i> Horror, but Buffy not Horror. I'm sure for at least someone out there, the opposite is true. Neither of them seem entirely fitting with the simple definition of &quot;designed to elicit negative emotions such as fear, shock, or revulsion&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure for some people Buffy is horrifying and Supernatural is not. But Supernatural should be classified under the horror genre because it is written with the intent to cause fear, and Buffy shouldn't because it is not. People react to different things in different ways, which is why genre should be defined by the reactions it is <i>intended</i> to elicit, not by how a given audience member individually reacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T17:07:18-07:00","id":915196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915174#post915174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure for some people Buffy is horrifying and Supernatural is not. But Supernatural should be classified under the horror genre because it is written with the intent to cause fear, and Buffy shouldn't because it is not. People react to different things in different ways, which is why genre should be defined by the reactions it is <i>intended</i> to elicit, not by how a given audience member individually reacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Example.<br /> <br /> In high school, there was always a small portion of people who, after reading Poe, would exclaim &quot;That's not scary!&quot;<br /> <br /> And yet, Poe remains a horror icon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T17:45:34-07:00","id":915216,"title":"","content":"About &quot;how often do your characters fear the things they face&quot;... <br /> <br /> First of all, there's stuff even in the blue books that would freak out Mummies and Demons, and second, that's not the only kind of horror. What about making the players afraid of what they are? That's something that ChroD can really push, and it's why I like Genius and Leviathan so much more than Mage and Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:06:08-07:00","id":915224,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> They're categorized as Horror, according to Wikipedia. In fact, both Supernatural and Being Human are referenced in the Inspiration section of World of Darkness books. At least, I'm pretty sure Being Human is, I can't find it. I also don't really see how the things I listed are wish fulfillment. I mean, the one I keep going back to is Dresden Files. Dresden is a competent protagonist who keeps gaining power, but he's also facing horrible, terrible things that are outside his weight class. People who <i>do</i> like the Horror themes of CofD point to Mage as &quot;not fitting&quot;. I point to <i>Summoners.</i>\u200b What makes the themes from those &quot;Urban fantasy, not horror&quot; shows any less horror than what you get from these games? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> being afraid doesn't mean running and hiding in terror. Not only that, the <i>players</i> are often the ones with Lunacy and Auras. In fact, that would be one of the arguments people make when they say that the game <i>isn't</i> Horror, or does Horror badly. Admittedly I made him with his Resistance Attributes all at 4, but my Mage never ran from fear. If anything, it was fear that kept him pushing on. If he wasn't afraid of what would happen to the people he cared about, he certainly wouldn't have done half the stupid shit he did.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> In standard Horror, I fear for the character's health and safety. In drama, I care for the character's social standing and emotional wellbeing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For someone who claims to prefer horror to come from within, I would expect you to appreciate that playing a character that is capable of such things is intensely horrifying.<br /> I... agree with all of this? It also seems completely inconsistent with everything else you have said in this post. </div> </div> </div>I said I don't agree with those complaints I listed, I was just providing reasons other people do. I don't think any of them take away from the Horror.<br /> <br /> I don't think that those <i>other</i> things <i>aren't</i> horror. I mean, I don't even think <i>Supernatural</i> is trying to make you afraid. Not of the monsters, at least, but afraid in the same way that drama elicits fear: Fear of emotional wellbeing, not bodily harm. I mean, it's been shown repeatedly that death means little to the Winchester brothers. Even in the first five seasons, <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/Supernatural/comments/2h3im8/i_rewatched_supernatural_a_few_weeks_ago_these/\" target=\"_blank\">which I don't agree were the best</a>. I mean, why does Law &amp; Order <i>not</i> get classified as Horror but all these urban fantasy shows do? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> doesn't that also apply to the argument that urban fantasy isn't horror? Just because it doesn't elicit fear from <i>you</i> doesn't mean it doesn't elicit fear period. I mean, I definitely won't say I'm a super fan or anything, and I haven't watched it since I was a teen, but Buffy was still about as intended as horror as some B grade movies. The make up on vampires is hideous, the monsters are gruesome even as the Scoobies crack jokes, and the plots are dire. It's even listed on Wikipedia as Supernatural Drama, Fantasy, Action, and Horror.<br /> <br /> And if it wasn't clear, I'm not really arguing that <s>World</s>Chronicles of Darkness <i>isn't</i> Horror. Demon and Mage with their reality warping are Horror. Vampire with it's inhumanly strong starting characters is horror. Even Beast and Werewolf with their lack of human morality and emphasis on destroying and crushing and defeating things is still Horror. I'm arguing that all of the things that people might draw inspiration from <i>are also Horror</i>. There's more than one way to skin a cat-demon. The reason that people who play Vampions and other styles are &quot;missing the point&quot; isn't because they're playing urban fantasy instead of horror, because that genre <i>has Horror</i>. It's because they're ignoring the horror. They're ignoring the questions of Morality, and Humanity. They're ignoring the fear of losing control, or the fear of exposure, or the fear of losing yourself, or the fear of betrayal, or loss of status or face. Those are themes urban fantasy has as well. They're horrifying themes that even crime fiction and drama have. I mean, look at Demon. It's part of the World of Darkness, but it doesn't look to Horror for it's themes. It looks to <i>Thrillers.</i> It looks to spy fiction. <br /> <br /> I just think that it's doing a disservice to miscategorize why people are missing the point. It's not because they're playing urban fantasy. It's because they're ignoring or getting rid of the consequences and concerns that the setting inherently wants to focus on. The game <i>is</i> urban fantasy after all, but your life is not your biggest concern, the fallout is. Whether you can punch out that guy before he punches you out, but if you can't it's no biggy, is not your concern. The concern is &quot;what's going to happen if I can't?&quot; or even &quot;what are the consequences if I do?&quot;. To quote a <i>Silent Hill</i> soundtrack, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YdCRHwhA_EY\" target=\"_blank\"><i>dying is the least of fears</i></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:12:23-07:00","id":915227,"title":"","content":"I just spent all day writing a comment and it's gone now :T<br /> <br /> But anyway, my point is that urban fantasy isn't the problem, and CofD is urban fantasy. Urban fantasy is plenty horror-ible. The problem is people taking out or ignoring the consequences of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:39:00-07:00","id":915246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915227#post915227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just spent all day writing a comment and it's gone now :T<br /> <br /> But anyway, my point is that urban fantasy isn't the problem, and CofD is urban fantasy. Urban fantasy is plenty horror-ible. The problem is people taking out or ignoring the consequences of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem was you included a link to Reddit in the post. Ever since the great spambot deluge, posts that include links to Reddit are automatically flagged as spam and require moderator approval before they show up publicly. I went ahead and approved your post so it should be visible now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:44:37-07:00","id":915252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915227#post915227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just spent all day writing a comment and it's gone now :T<br /> <br /> But anyway, my point is that urban fantasy isn't the problem, and CofD is urban fantasy. Urban fantasy is plenty horror-ible. The problem is people taking out or ignoring the consequences of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> My previous comment may have given the impression that I'm against urban fantasy. What I am against is taking out the consequences, as you said.<br /> <br /> For example: it's totally valid to use the Hedge for a picnic scene with no monsters hiding behind the trees or what have you. The city outside the Hedge gate doesn't always have to look all grim and filthy to make you want to stay in the Thorns. Should you choose to stay there, it's not guaranteed to bite you in the rear. What happens there depends on your choices, but with more dream logic, of course. You can even find a cool Token or befriend a friendly hobgoblin.<br /> <br /> In other words, I don't feel the need to reinforce the idea that &quot;life sucks, and you're probably gonna get eaten by T\u0336y\u0336r\u0336a\u0336n\u0336i\u0336d\u0336s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/884923-gisilu-the-ant-host\"><b>Gisilu</b></a>&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-16-2016, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:03:51-07:00","id":915266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're categorized as Horror, according to Wikipedia. In fact, both Supernatural and Being Human are referenced in the Inspiration section of World of Darkness books. At least, I'm pretty sure Being Human is, I can't find it. </div> </div> </div>In another thread you expressed a problem you had reading people's posts when they quoted everything someone said. In order to ameliorate the issue I only mentioned the key points. I was not saying they were drama and not horror, I was saying the situations you explained were dramatic ones, not representative of horror. Bad people getting Mitchell to fall off the wagon. George being worried about flipping out. Buffy worrying about her future. These are not aspects of horror, they are aspects of drama within a genre. These three examples are the same issues characters have dealt with in General Hospital.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't really see how the things I listed are wish fulfillment. I mean, the one I keep going back to is Dresden Files. Dresden is a competent protagonist who keeps gaining power, but he's also facing horrible, terrible things that are outside his weight class. </div> </div> </div>He is also a wizard who is well-liked by nearly everyone and can do very little wrong. I'll skip over the weird grooming of an underage girl and other issues with women but they are just as much wish-fulfillment. I was referring to a key difference between urban fantasy and horror as genres. Urban fantasy is fantasy, it depicts something you fantasize about being, like a wizard or a superhero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People who do like the Horror themes of CofD point to Mage as &quot;not fitting&quot;. I point to Summoners.\u200b What makes the themes from those &quot;Urban fantasy, not horror&quot; shows any less horror than what you get from these games? </div> </div> </div>Primarily the depiction of the fantastic as something wonderful and amazing, also the concept that there is always good to defeat bad. The setting in the Chronicles of Darkness has undergone many apocalypses already, each one stored away by an alien entity that only does so for its own equally alien desires.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I think a large flaw in Mage's second edition was not emphasizing the horrible nature of its antagonists. One can look through it and think outside of the Seers the things one should be most worried about is accidentally taking a wrong turn in London, or running into an egomaniac in LA. But when you take out these antagonists and all you have is politicking, mage is very susceptible to Dresden-like urban fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:08:23-07:00","id":915270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> being afraid doesn't mean running and hiding in terror.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep putting words in other people's mouth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only that, the <i>players</i> are often the ones with Lunacy and Auras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't means they're immune to other shit inflicting their conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, that would be one of the arguments people make when they say that the game <i>isn't</i> Horror, or does Horror badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your arguments, as usual are invalid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mittedly I made him with his Resistance Attributes all at 4, but my Mage never ran from fear. If anything, it was fear that kept him pushing on. If he wasn't afraid of what would happen to the people he cared about, he certainly wouldn't have done half the stupid shit he did.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's in fact, another fashion of horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, why does Law &amp; Order <i>not</i> get classified as Horror but all these urban fantasy shows do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because horrible shit may happen, but the premise of the show is how to deal with it. In Horror, unlike in urban fantasy, the premise is &quot;how do you deal with this horrible thing, personally?&quot;. Not &quot;How do you solve this so everything turns out ok in the end?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Want to make a horror show without supernatural trappings and in the police-procedural atmosphere? make the victims the protagonists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> doesn't that also apply to the argument that urban fantasy isn't horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not, because as explained above, it depends on vantage point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because it doesn't elicit fear from <i>you</i> doesn't mean it doesn't elicit fear period. I mean, I definitely won't say I'm a super fan or anything, and I haven't watched it since I was a teen, but Buffy was still about as intended as horror as some B grade movies. The make up on vampires is hideous, the monsters are gruesome even as the Scoobies crack jokes, and the plots are dire. It's even listed on Wikipedia as Supernatural Drama, Fantasy, Action, and Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone is agoraphobic, that doesn't makes a documentary on historic, public, open spaces a work of horror. It may be horrible to this demographic, but it's not intended to be a work of horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason that people who play Vampions and other styles are &quot;missing the point&quot; isn't because they're playing urban fantasy instead of horror, because that genre <i>has Horror</i>. It's because they're ignoring the horror. They're ignoring the questions of Morality, and Humanity. They're ignoring the fear of losing control, or the fear of exposure, or the fear of losing yourself, or the fear of betrayal, or loss of status or face. Those are themes urban fantasy has as well. They're horrifying themes that even crime fiction and drama have. I mean, look at Demon. It's part of the World of Darkness, but it doesn't look to Horror for it's themes. It looks to <i>Thrillers.</i> It looks to spy fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, horror is internal, urban fantasy is external.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think that it's doing a disservice to miscategorize why people are missing the point. It's not because they're playing urban fantasy. It's because they're ignoring or getting rid of the consequences and concerns that the setting inherently wants to focus on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Internal consequences. <b>Personal Horror</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game <i>is</i> urban fantasy after all,</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You can play it as such, but it's branded and marketed as games of personal horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but your life is not your biggest concern, the fallout is. Whether you can punch out that guy before he punches you out, but if you can't it's no biggy, is not your concern. The concern is &quot;what's going to happen if I can't?&quot; or even &quot;what are the consequences if I do?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a game of horror, it doesn't matters if you win the day or not at the end. unlike in fantasy. In the end you have to live with the consequences. With the knowledge that do as you might, you're fucked anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-15-2016, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:10:59-07:00","id":915272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> In standard Horror, I fear for the character's health and safety. In drama, I care for the character's social standing and emotional wellbeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may have been a little freudian, but notice how you say in horror you <i>fear</i> for the character's health and safety and in drama you <i>care</i> for the character's social standing and emotional wellbeing. My argument is that the difference between horror and drama is not health and safety vs. social standing and emotional wellbeing. It's fear vs. care. If the intent is to make the audience <i>fear</i> for the character's social standing and emotional wellbeing, that's still horror. If the intent is to make the audience <i>care</i> for the character's health and safety, that's still drama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said I don't agree with those complaints I listed, I was just providing reasons other people do. I don't think any of them take away from the Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I must have missed that part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that those <i>other</i> things <i>aren't</i> horror. I mean, I don't even think <i>Supernatural</i> is trying to make you afraid. Not of the monsters, at least, but afraid in the same way that drama elicits fear: Fear of emotional wellbeing, not bodily harm. I mean, it's been shown repeatedly that death means little to the Winchester brothers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, first of all, as I've said I think Supernatural fits both under horror and drama. These aren't mutually exclusive categories. Second of all, notice how you're now describing your concern for the characters' emotional wellbeing as fear. Third of all, just because you're not meant to fear for the protagonists being physically harmed (which I don't agree is the case in Supernatural, but that's tangential to the point anyway) doesn't necessarily mean you aren't meant to fear the things that pose potential harm to the protagonists. Many of the monsters in the show are frightening, or at least meant to be so, even if the Winchesters are at no real risk of being harmed by them. And finally, I agree with you that the primary driving force of fear in Supernatural is internal and interpersonal rather than external and physical. I don't agree that that in any way makes it not horror. That's the difference between personal horror and external horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in the first five seasons, <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/Supernatural/comments/2h3im8/i_rewatched_supernatural_a_few_weeks_ago_these/\" target=\"_blank\">which I don't agree were the best</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I read this comment, and true to form for Reddit, it's completely missing the point of why many people enjoyed the first 5 seasons and didn't enjoy the later seasons. Of course it's riddled with plot holes. Of course it's silly and at times downright cheesy. Of course the writers were making shit up as they went. All the same is true of the later seasons just as much as the first 5, and none of it has anything to do with why I stopped watching the show. On the contrary, that's all a huge part of the show's charm and why I continued watching up through... I dunno, what season was it that Dean had a vampire friend he met in Purgatory? That one. The problem is that the story ended in Season 5. Whether or not that ending was planned in advance doesn't matter, they wrote a satisfying conclusion to the story that tied up all the loose ends, and then they crammed some loose ends in to keep it going. That's fine, I don't blame them for wanting to keep the show going, and I tried hard to stick with it but at the end of the day I just like stories to stop when they reach a satisfying conclusion. Same reason I love the first Matrix and the first Pirates of the Caribbean and tolerate the sequels. It's not that the sequels were objectively worse, it's just that I didn't feel the need for more. If you enjoy and even prefer the post-Kripke Supernatural or the sequels to the above-mentioned films, that's fine. I've got no beef with that. It's just not for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, why does Law &amp; Order <i>not</i> get classified as Horror but all these urban fantasy shows do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the people classifying them are out of touch with what horror fans like about horror and categorize things as horror based on superficial trappings instead of the actual qualities fans look for in the genre. As I mentioned before, I think Law &amp; Order would be more appropriately called horror than Buffy, and this is coming from someone who loves Buffy and is bored to tears by Law &amp; Order. I mean, really I don't think either should be considered horror, because neither is written with the intent to elicit negative emotions through playing on primal fears, but Law &amp; Order is at least closer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> doesn't that also apply to the argument that urban fantasy isn't horror? Just because it doesn't elicit fear from <i>you</i> doesn't mean it doesn't elicit fear period. I mean, I definitely won't say I'm a super fan or anything, and I haven't watched it since I was a teen, but Buffy was still about as intended as horror as some B grade movies. The make up on vampires is hideous, the monsters are gruesome even as the Scoobies crack jokes, and the plots are dire. It's even listed on Wikipedia as Supernatural Drama, Fantasy, Action, and Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point was that intent should be the deciding factor here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915224#post915224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if it wasn't clear, I'm not really arguing that <s>World</s>Chronicles of Darkness <i>isn't</i> Horror. Demon and Mage with their reality warping are Horror. Vampire with it's inhumanly strong starting characters is horror. Even Beast and Werewolf with their lack of human morality and emphasis on destroying and crushing and defeating things is still Horror. I'm arguing that all of the things that people might draw inspiration from <i>are also Horror</i>. There's more than one way to skin a cat-demon. The reason that people who play Vampions and other styles are &quot;missing the point&quot; isn't because they're playing urban fantasy instead of horror, because that genre <i>has Horror</i>. It's because they're ignoring the horror. They're ignoring the questions of Morality, and Humanity. They're ignoring the fear of losing control, or the fear of exposure, or the fear of losing yourself, or the fear of betrayal, or loss of status or face. Those are themes urban fantasy has as well. They're horrifying themes that even crime fiction and drama have. I mean, look at Demon. It's part of the World of Darkness, but it doesn't look to Horror for it's themes. It looks to <i>Thrillers.</i> It looks to spy fiction.<br /> <br /> I just think that it's doing a disservice to miscategorize why people are missing the point. It's not because they're playing urban fantasy. It's because they're ignoring or getting rid of the consequences and concerns that the setting inherently wants to focus on. The game <i>is</i> urban fantasy after all, but your life is not your biggest concern, the fallout is. Whether you can punch out that guy before he punches you out, but if you can't it's no biggy, is not your concern. The concern is &quot;what's going to happen if I can't?&quot; or even &quot;what are the consequences if I do?&quot;. To quote a <i>Silent Hill</i> soundtrack, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YdCRHwhA_EY\" target=\"_blank\"><i>dying is the least of fears</i></a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is where it becomes clear that we are arguing past each other, because I agree with every word of these two paragraphs and disagree with everything else in your post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-15-2016, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:20:38-07:00","id":915281,"title":"","content":"My point is not that something can't be multiple genres, because they clearly can be. Genres are an illusion anyways.<br /> <br /> My point is-wait, Ephsy and Charly explained this already. I don't have to be here. I can go play Kingdom Hearts.I'ma go play Kingdom Hearts.<br /> <br /> (I don't have much interest in being in this conversation beyond supporting what I think are good arguments and occasionally illuminating on points I think I can illuminate on, as an aside. I have opinions, but they are mine.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:25:59-07:00","id":915287,"title":"","content":"I'd really say Law &amp; Order was more like fantasy. They solve a ridiculous amount of crimes, and while there's always more criminals, they are most often criminals with very discernible reasons, usually basic and understandable ones, like greed, shame and anger. In horror there's a certain, I don't want to say hopelessness exactly, but perhaps some nihilism, that would point out that sometimes people do bad things for no reason at all and never get caught, or all evidence could point towards a criminal and they could get away with it completely due to some technicality or get a lot of leniency, for example, six months out of what would normally demand a larger sentence. In Law &amp; Order, if it happened, the victim or another victim or someone else would likely kill the person or the police would find evidence of some other crime.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which and since we're linking to things, I passed by <a href=\"https://www.vice.com/read/law-order-special-victims-unit-offers-women-justice-and-thats-why-i-love-it\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> the other day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T20:40:45-07:00","id":915338,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915246#post915246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem was you included a link to Reddit in the post. Ever since the great spambot deluge, posts that include links to Reddit are automatically flagged as spam and require moderator approval before they show up publicly. I went ahead and approved your post so it should be visible now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I saw a &quot;Unapproved&quot; message and worried I did something wrong, but when I refreshed, it was gone, so I figured it was eaten.<br /> <br /> Also, iunno. I'd definitely say that I feel an empathy based fear when I watch a good drama. I worry about them. I feel that for characters in a drama more than I do for the characters in a typical horror movie. When I think of horrifying moments, I think of things like the first season finale of <i>Orange is the New Black</i>, or... wow, I haven't really watched many things lately. Also, for the record, I'm not saying <i>Supernatural</i> isn't Horror, just that the horror is the same sort of internal horror that you could get from, say, <i>The Departed</i>. That movie is emotionally agonizing to watch, but it's not what people would classify as Horror. (<span style=\"font-size:9px\">Also, that was <i>my</i> Reddit thread. I was pointing out that the argument that the Kripke seasons were <i>better quality </i>is flawed</span>). I mean, when we get to the intent argument, I just... disagree. I feel that aspects of Buffy are clearly meant to be horror. They're scary. They unsettle. I mean, there's an entire episode about how the meat might be people. It wasn't, but that's still pretty gruesome for prime time. It's not meant to keep you up at night, though the creatures from Hush (and by extension DaveB's avatar) do tend to show up on those kind of lists.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915246#post915246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is where it becomes clear that we are arguing past each other, because I agree with every word of these two paragraphs and disagree with everything else in your post.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably an apt description. It seems like we agree in a general sense what Horror is, just not which specific things fit that criteria.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> on the other hand, I feel like you just aren't grasping what I'm saying at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915287#post915287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really say Law &amp; Order was more like fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I mean it does have as much to do with the New York Criminal Justice System as Golarion or Eberron do...<br /> <br /> But this really gets to the heart of the problem: Genre is always arbitrary. Law &amp; Order uses the vaguest trappings of the Criminal Justice system, and so it's a crime procedural. When you throw fantastical creatures into drama, it becomes urban fantasy. Horror is generally not going to have the some kind of supernatural elements, even though there are many real life situations that are horrifying without the supernatural. <i>Scream</i> is horror, <i>Zodiac</i> is thriller.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> I rarely have a problem with that. Sometimes I think people take things a little <i>too</i> far, and act like because &quot;it's the world of darkness, not the world of happiness&quot; that everything is always terrible and bad and shitty and whoops, you got stabbed by a junky. I think that might be an even bigger way to miss the point (though there's also the argument that &quot;darkness&quot; means secrecy, but I do think that fits oWoD with its Vampire Illuminati more). I think <i>consequence</i> is the biggest way to miss the point, but that does go both ways. I mean, after all, having a nice picnic space in the Hedge is even a Merit. Like you say, not everywhere is Crapsville. If it's always raining, there's never any reason to appreciate the sun.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> I missed your first comment (<span style=\"font-size:9px\">every time I say something I seem to get five people telling me I'm wrong</span>). I'm <i>maaaaaybe</i> getting the impression that you're not a big Dresden Files fan, but I have to ask, if those things I listed are the same issues people have to deal with on <i>General Hospital</i> (and, I mean, I guess <i>maybe</i> med students can worry about their future like someone who fights crime, and vampirism is a good metaphor for drugs, but I don't think any doctors are going to flip out and start eating people...) and not the kind of things you face in Horror... what is? I mean, George wolfing out and killing everyone is basically the core element of Horror in Forsaken. Mitchell giving in to his urge for blood and Frenzying is straight out of Requiem. Buffy worrying about her supernatural vigilantism getting in the way of her life is so straight out of Hunter that the only reason I can think for not putting it in the Intro chapter is because that would be too on the nose. Dresden constantly worries about what he's becoming, and the things he's done to keep from getting killed, which fits any gameline, though Dave has used him as an example of a Low Wisdom Mage (I don't actually agree)<br /> <br /> If those aren't the issues that your characters face, what are?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Also it's less that I can't handle when people break a post up, and more that I find it tedious and somewhat condescending.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-15-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T20:55:43-07:00","id":915352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915338#post915338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this really gets to the heart of the problem: Genre is always arbitrary. Law &amp; Order uses the vaguest trappings of the Criminal Justice system, and so it's a crime procedural. When you throw fantastical creatures into drama, it becomes urban fantasy. Horror is generally not going to have the some kind of supernatural elements, even though there are many real life situations that are horrifying without the supernatural. <i>Scream</i> is horror, <i>Zodiac</i> is thriller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Urban fantasy is fantasy trappings in an urban setting. Chicago with wizards, New York with fairies, Baton Rouge with vampires, and so forth.<br /> <br /> A point that has been made here is that you can play with the horror in the game, or you can kick it out and have it be, if urban fantasy is too confusing a term, something more equivalent to Dungeons &amp; Dragons Modern or tabletop General Hospital with 'monster' races. And that's what many of these changes attempt to do, sometimes inadvertently.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with playing these other ways, but it isn't what the books generally plot for the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to ask, if those things I listed are the same issues people have to deal with on General Hospital (and, I mean, I guess maybe med students can worry about their future like someone who fights crime, and vampirism is a good metaphor for drugs, but I don't think any doctors are going to flip out and start eating people...) </div> </div> </div>General Hospital does not solely focus on the hospital, and involves the environs around Port Charles. AJ Quartermain had a debilitating drinking disorder that people were constantly trying to make him fall back into. Sonny Corinthos is a mob boss with bipolar disorder and who has, in certain extreme moments, seriously harmed people he didn't mean to. Worrying about one's future due to things one is doing at the moment is common to almost every character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and not the kind of things you face in Horror... what is? </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that. I said the incidents you referred to were dramatic. They are not unique to horror. I didn't say that they couldn't happen in horror. You used them as examples of horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915109#post915109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are the kind of horror that shows up in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, George wolfing out and killing everyone is basically the core element of Horror in Forsaken. Mitchell giving in to his urge for blood and Frenzying is straight out of Requiem. Buffy worrying about her supernatural vigilantism getting in the way of her life is so straight out of Hunter that the only reason I can think for not putting it in the Intro chapter is because that would be too on the nose. Dresden constantly worries about what he's becoming, and the things he's done to keep from getting killed, which fits any gameline, though Dave has used him as an example of a Low Wisdom Mage (I don't actually agree)<br /> <br /> If those aren't the issues that your characters face, what are? </div> </div> </div>All these games offer more than that. Werewolves have to deal with internecine warfare against an enemy that outnumbers them and outmatches them in savagery and spiritual power. They have to deal with the fact that killing a man does not just have physical consequences, but spiritual ones that can result in more bloodshed. A vampire who frenzies for blood has to worry about hunters and every other vampire that knows they've broken the Masquerade, with the fact that that dead human means they are likely to take a hit to their Humanity, putting them 1/10th closer to being lost forever. Buffy's superhumanly resilient, effective and knowledgeable in a way that most hunters would never be. It took my werewolf three rounds to stake a vampire, with enhanced strength. She and her buddies do it without breaking a sweat, at a certain point. She worries about her future because she's likely to be alive to have one, but she doesn't have to worry about the police busting into her place for leaving headless bodies all over town with her fingerprints on the stakes in their chests. Dresden doesn't face the Seers, ochemata and other threats, and his survival isn't dependent upon the roll of dice, his magic doesn't actively work to bring the Abyss into the world and corrupt everything and he's not driven to obsession by merit of being touched with magic.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness games can have drama, that's a part of storytelling. But there is more to it than that, with themes of personal horror and nail-biting paranoia, dominance and violence, power and hubris. They're worlds where your name is not on the cover of the book, and you may be the protagonist but you aren't the hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-16-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:00:10-07:00","id":915361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915352#post915352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urban fantasy is fantasy trappings in an urban setting. Chicago with wizards, New York with fairies, Baton Rouge with vampires, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>We must be talking about the World of Darkness <i>without</i> vampires and wizards and faeries, then. My mistake.<br /> <br /> I'll acknowledge that despite it's roots in Gothic Horror that Urban Fantasy is not <i>necessarily</i> Horror, but I'm going to strongly disagree that the setting with wizards, faeries, robot angels, vampires, werewolves, spirits, and other fantastical beings in urban settings isn't Urban Fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-16-2016, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:06:18-07:00","id":915366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915338#post915338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> on the other hand, I feel like you just aren't grasping what I'm saying at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>We might fare better at understanding your arguments if your every post didn't include a half a dozen new diatribes, tangents and off-topic clunk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915361#post915361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll acknowledge that despite it's roots in Gothic Horror that Urban Fantasy is not <i>necessarily</i> Horror, but I'm going to strongly disagree that the setting with wizards, faeries, robot angels, vampires, werewolves, spirits, and other fantastical beings in urban settings isn't Urban Fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be, but again, this is not the expressed purpose for the games, as it was editorially expressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:12:11-07:00","id":915370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915338#post915338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, iunno. I'd definitely say that I feel an empathy based fear when I watch a good drama. I worry about them. I feel that for characters in a drama more than I do for the characters in a typical horror movie. When I think of horrifying moments, I think of things like the first season finale of <i>Orange is the New Black</i>, or... wow, I haven't really watched many things lately. Also, for the record, I'm not saying <i>Supernatural</i> isn't Horror, just that the horror is the same sort of internal horror that you could get from, say, <i>The Departed</i>. That movie is emotionally agonizing to watch, but it's not what people would classify as Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with you. I've been saying this whole time that horror comes from the fear the work elicits, not from the presence of spooky scary skeletons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915338#post915338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(<span style=\"font-size:9px\">Also, that was <i>my</i> Reddit thread. I was pointing out that the argument that the Kripke seasons were <i>better quality </i>is flawed</span>). I mean, when we get to the intent argument, I just... disagree. I feel that aspects of Buffy are clearly meant to be horror. They're scary. They unsettle. I mean, there's an entire episode about how the meat might be people. It wasn't, but that's still pretty gruesome for prime time. It's not meant to keep you up at night, though the creatures from Hush (and by extension DaveB's avatar) do tend to show up on those kind of lists.That's probably an apt description. It seems like we agree in a general sense what Horror is, just not which specific things fit that criteria.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, you've got me there. I'll agree that Buffy did cross into horror territory at times, even if I still think the overall vibe is one of comedy. That Doublemeat Palace episode was admittedly creepy as fuck. That said, what made it horrifying for me personally was how uncharacteristically (for that show) <i>real </i>it got. The existential horror of being trapped in a dead-end food service job and the uncomfortably realistic portrayal of the toxicity of Buffy and Spike's relationship was far scarier to me than the body horror of &quot;the meat might be people&quot; and the Cronenberg-esque monster. That episode and The Body are tied for the two most genuinely horrific episodes of that show for me, and neither of them because of anything to do with monsters. Another good moment was when (spoilers for a 13-year-old show) Giles smothered Ben behind Buffy's back. Again, nothing really supernatrual about what made that moment scary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915338#post915338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> on the other hand, I feel like you just aren't grasping what I'm saying at all.<br /> <br /> Well I mean it does have as much to do with the New York Criminal Justice System as Golarion or Eberron do...<br /> <br /> But this really gets to the heart of the problem: Genre is always arbitrary. Law &amp; Order uses the vaguest trappings of the Criminal Justice system, and so it's a crime procedural. When you throw fantastical creatures into drama, it becomes urban fantasy. Horror is generally not going to have the some kind of supernatural elements, even though there are many real life situations that are horrifying without the supernatural. <i>Scream</i> is horror, <i>Zodiac</i> is thriller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this whole time you've been arguing this point at people who already agree with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-16-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:29:40-07:00","id":915380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915361#post915361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We must be talking about the World of Darkness <i>without</i> vampires and wizards and faeries, then. My mistake.<br /> <br /> I'll acknowledge that despite it's roots in Gothic Horror that Urban Fantasy is not <i>necessarily</i> Horror, but I'm going to strongly disagree that the setting with wizards, faeries, robot angels, vampires, werewolves, spirits, and other fantastical beings in urban settings isn't Urban Fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fantasy, including urban fantasy, these are things of wonder. In horror, they are things of terror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T22:39:42-07:00","id":915409,"title":"","content":"Firstly let me mention something about <b>Mummy</b> (of course). I think a lot of people are slightly disappointed that the game wasn't second edition especially since the game afterwards we knew would be, but that there's one thing that's the root of a few issues (like non-Iremite Mummies): <i>people mistaking backstory for metaplot</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=914634#post914634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? I've never noticed that. Usually, I see it followed by requests for South American or Asian mummies. Not that there's anything wrong with being Caucasian, mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in the game's early days the issue was more about its approach to racial phenotype rather than cultural variations of a supernatural condition.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way there's a couple things I wanted to chime in on:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=907494#post907494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal beef is primarily with Mage, which I've always argued has something of a thematic disconnect with the rest of the CofD; in a world about horror and mystery, having godlike power and focusing on finding answers seems to somewhat miss the point. They're the line with the least drawbacks, and while one can warn about the dangers of hubris or point to all the scary Abyssal beasties they, it stands to reason that Awakening is gonna be a straight upgrade from mortal life for most people. Look at the &quot;Who are you in the CofD?&quot; thread and see all the people excited to have magic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that is why I never even <i>looked</i> inside that thread. I think second edition, at least, put <b>Mage</b> back in a personal horror spot but it is (for better or worse) still very much, in my eyes, a game of wish-fulfillment. Someone else in the thread talked about how <b>Mage</b> exists in its own secluded world that no other splat can interact with (which is interesting because that's the second biggest jumped-to-conclusion people make regarding <b>Mummy</b>), but isn't that the point? That <i>being a Mage</i> gives you secret occult knowledge that drives you mad and isolates you from friends and family because they don't get it? Simultaneously and ironically, <b>Mage</b> is probably the best game for crossover despite <b>Beast</b> being designed for it, which, incidentally, explains that Beasts are native to a realm described in <b>Mage</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=909505#post909505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The largest &quot;changing what you don't like things&quot; thing I've heard for Geist are &quot;Make it more like Wraith&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I've accepted that my preferred 'ghost game' is <b>Wraith</b> and my preferred 'faerie game' is <b>Changeling the Dreaming</b>. I know when to fold 'em.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=910534#post910534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obsessions are related to Mysteries, and Mysteries are usually (though not always) magical. But Mages don't have to spend every waking moment pursuing their Obsessions. They can do other things; hell, technically there aren't even any mechanics forcing them to pursue their Obsessions at all, beyond the player's own desire to earn the Arcane Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Appropriately enough, the only Mages who <i>are </i>compelled to indulge their Obsessions are those who have reached Wisdom 0 and become Mad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T00:09:21-07:00","id":915439,"title":"","content":"I always saw the cWoD s a horror setting where all sorts of scary things are coming to get you, specifically (the Sabbat, the Technocracy, the Wyrm, etc) while the nWoD was more a Urban Fantasy where the scary things where there, but not specifically after you as long as you didn't get in their way, or else they were reasonable challenges, like hunters, bale hounds or banishers.<br /> <br /> The cWoD also made things worse (or better!) by making the protagonist very distant from the normal human experience, fostering horror by the callousness that resulted, while in the nWoD protagonists felt more like freaks and pariahs angsting over their damaged links to humanity (I often felt a bit of Anne Rice in those titles).<br /> <br /> The CoD feels like a mix of both, with protagonists being monstrous rather than being supernatural misfits, but also having deeper and more complex (and thus complicated) links than ever to mundane people. Once again, the scary things are after you, from Angels to Strix and Huntsmen, but they are not the quasi omnipotent and omnipresent threats the cWoD had to deal with. Often things will start like Urban Fantasy with the protagonists juggling with the mundane and supernatural aspects of their lives, and then turn to horror as one aspect intrudes on the other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:51:08-07:00","id":915466,"title":"","content":"Huh, I've always thought kind of the opposite, that ChroD was much more horror-y. Well, not so much more horror-y as trying for straight horror as closer to a primary goal. oWoD is absolutely drenched in horror aesthetics, but that's the thing- it's drenched. It's gothic, it's gory, it's nineties as fuck, and so on. It's hard to run Werewolf as something other than &quot;splatterpunk Captain Planet&quot; or Ascension as something other than &quot;Prog Rock Concept Album: The Game&quot;. And while there's nothing wrong with any of that and I love oWoD dearly, whereas nWoD and ChroD in particular seem like they're out to spoop you good, and they've made their focus more local and personal for that purpose. <br /> <br /> See, to me, the Strix, the Gentry, and the GM pretty much scream &quot;terrifying omnipresent threat&quot;- all of them have the central concept of &quot;they could be anywhere, they could be anyone, they're hard to fight, they can't be reasoned with, oh shit&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-07-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T03:55:50-07:00","id":915499,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1405_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1405\" data-vbnamecard=\"1405\">Anteros</a> I'm going to have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a>. It always felt more to me that nWoD does Horror more than oWoD, which wasn't so much more or less urban fantasy as it was &quot;Horrorpunk&quot;. It used the trappings of Horror, and had horrifying things, but they were more the kind of horror of a metal album cover. It was very Fight The Power. Everyone was under the thumb of some faceless The Man and you fight back or do his bidding. When you do face some big terrifying threat, it's really just the face of The Man, whether it be your Elders or the Wyrm/Pentex or even the Technocracy. oWoD was very intentionally Anne Rice, as well, but only when it wasn't busy being Shadowrun with fangs.<br /> <br /> nWoD--Chronicles especially--feels like there's a lot of bad shit out there that'll eat your face off if you look tasty and alone. You'll generally be safe if you're part of an established group, but there's something in the sewers eating hobos, so try not to look like no one knows where you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:42:19-07:00","id":915629,"title":"","content":"Generally ChroD is my go to if I want to run or play horror. There are still horror elements in WoD certainly, but by and large I feel that ChroD manages it better because it deliberately maintains much more mystery and ambiguity. Also the overall aesthetic of the ChroD books evokes horror moreso than most of the WoD books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:13:14-07:00","id":915646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915466#post915466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I've always thought kind of the opposite, that ChroD was much more horror-y. Well, not so much more horror-y as trying for straight horror as closer to a primary town. oWoD is absolutely drenched in horror aesthetics, but that's the thing- it's drenched. It's gothic, it's gory, it's nineties as fuck, and so on. It's hard to run Werewolf as something other than &quot;splatterpunk Captain Planet&quot; or Ascension as something other than &quot;Prog Rock Concept Album: The Game&quot;. And while there's nothing wrong with any of that and I love oWoD dearly, whereas nWoD and ChroD in particular seem like they're out to spoop you good, and they've made their focus more local and personal for that purpose.<br /> <br /> See, to me, the Strix, the Gentry, and the GM pretty much scream &quot;terrifying omnipresent threat&quot;- all of them have the central concept of &quot;they could be anywhere, they could be anyone, they're hard to fight, they can't be reasoned with, oh shit&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard a lot of people mention Captain Planet in relation to W:tA, as if the ecologist theme of the game somehow made it silly or goofy. I don't get how taking seriously a very real and very deadly issue is supposed to lessen the horror of the game.<br /> Still, apart from this, it seems to come down to aesthetics? Like the punk athmosphere is seen as 'diluting' the horror?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915499#post915499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1405_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1405\" data-vbnamecard=\"1405\">Anteros</a> I'm going to have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a>. It always felt more to me that nWoD does Horror more than oWoD, which wasn't so much more or less urban fantasy as it was &quot;Horrorpunk&quot;. It used the trappings of Horror, and had horrifying things, but they were more the kind of horror of a metal album cover. It was very Fight The Power. Everyone was under the thumb of some faceless The Man and you fight back or do his bidding. When you do face some big terrifying threat, it's really just the face of The Man, whether it be your Elders or the Wyrm/Pentex or even the Technocracy. oWoD was very intentionally Anne Rice, as well, but only when it wasn't busy being Shadowrun with fangs.<br /> <br /> nWoD--Chronicles especially--feels like there's a lot of bad shit out there that'll eat your face off if you look tasty and alone. You'll generally be safe if you're part of an established group, but there's something in the sewers eating hobos, so try not to look like no one knows where you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Shadowrun isn't a horror game, if it doesn't feel scary, you're missing something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The cWoD was nightmare of hopelessness and parano\u00efa, where fighting despair was as integral as fighting the howling packs of the Sabbat and the Black Spiral Dancers. It was watching the world die around you while knowing than your hard won victories most likely merely delayed the ineluctable defeat. It was constantly facing who you are in the dark, because the enemy was as much after your soul than after your blood. It was going home to find your furniture replaced by your mortal family fleshcrafted into chairs by the Tzimisce who learned your true name, or your Kinfolk turned into fomors because you let a innocent witness alive after attacking that Pentex power plant.<br /> <br /> The nWoD left more breathing room. The True Fae aren't trying to eat the world, the Exarchs couldn't care less about you personally as long as you aren't pocking your nose in their business. The scale is smaller, you can go it alone or with a few friends and not have to live in constant fear. Unless you're a hunter or a changeling, in which case you should be afraid, because sooner or later there will be things coming after you specifically.<br /> They're probably coming right now, in fact.<br /> ...Why aren't you running already, fool?!<br /> <br /> Seriously though, Hunter and Changeling are the only nWoD that I can see as horror, wih perhaps Prometheans when Pandorans wake up. Otherwise things are too impersonal and random to set a horror mood.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T10:30:10-07:00","id":915701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915646#post915646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously though, Hunter and Changeling are the only nWoD that I can see as horror, wih perhaps Prometheans when Pandorans wake up. Otherwise things are too impersonal and random to set a horror mood.</div> </div> </div> </div>How impersonal or random would it be if your own sense of inferiority literally possessed you in a climax of bloody retribution, leaving the mauled and half-eaten corpses of you abusive family behind? Your weakness literally gave birth to the thing that triggered the event, you just needed a little nudge. Now life as you know it is undone, and you can't but recall the sweet, essence-ridden taste of your parents and sister before you attempt to sleep. So much that you wake up drenched in blood and guts. You can't help it anymore.<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random would it be that your obsession with altering the event that forever changed your life never happened, so much that you shattered the timeline in such a fashion that the person you loved the most in the entire world is but a figment of your oneiros? And you have nobody else to blame but yourself? And your new obsession is now to stop yourself from ever attempting such.<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random is it that, despite your otherworldly birth, after attaining a taste of what being human is, you cannot condone the sight of your fellow fallen angels ripping people's souls apart for a cheap fa\u00e7ade at life, instead of carefully building the perfect lie to move under God's radar? And when you, yourself are forced to cash in your last chance soul pact, because that's better than being ripped to shreds and recycled, like a common piece of glass?<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random is it to watch your mother witter slowly with the years, see dementia sweep in to the point she doesn't even recognizes you when you visit her at night, because she recalls a funeral for her son with an empty casket that your Sire arranged for? How do you keep your humanity after you bow to yourself to spare her the indignity of a rotting brain and a broken life without notion for her own identity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T11:09:52-07:00","id":915726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915646#post915646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard a lot of people mention Captain Planet in relation to W:tA, as if the ecologist theme of the game somehow made it silly or goofy. I don't get how taking seriously a very real and very deadly issue is supposed to lessen the horror of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't actually played or read Apocalypse, but from what I understand, the &quot;Captain Planet&quot; criticism isn't about the environmentalist themes, it's about the way they're handled. Presenting climate change as a problem you can punch in the face and pollution as something perpetrated by evil corporations actually hurt the environmentalist message. I have no idea if those complaints are accurate, and I would be willing to bet they're founded on shallow reading of the material and exaggerated for the purpose of argument, just like most recurring complaints about WoD and CofD are. But that's my understanding of where those complaints are coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915646#post915646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, apart from this, it seems to come down to aesthetics? Like the punk athmosphere is seen as 'diluting' the horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so much about aesthetics as it is about mood. Punk is founded on righteous indignation, fighting back against the systems that oppress you. For a lot of people, fighting back is the antithesis of horror. I don't really agree with that perspective, but I certainly understand it, as helplessness is often an important element of horror.<br /> <br /> I think another part of the issue is that WoD is more externally-focused horror, while CofD is more personally focused. In WoD, the fear is of the monsters that are out there, walking unseen among us. In CofD, the fear is of the self, of what you're capable of, of the things you've forgotten or ignored because it's easier to pretend nothing is wrong than to face the truth that the momsters out there are nothing compared to the monsters in here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915646#post915646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cWoD was nightmare of hopelessness and parano\u00efa, where fighting despair was as integral as fighting the howling packs of the Sabbat and the Black Spiral Dancers. It was watching the world die around you while knowing than your hard won victories most likely merely delayed the ineluctable defeat. It was constantly facing who you are in the dark, because the enemy was as much after your soul than after your blood. It was going home to find your furniture replaced by your mortal family fleshcrafted into chairs by the Tzimisce who learned your true name, or your Kinfolk turned into fomors because you let a innocent witness alive after attacking that Pentex power plant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a very Punk-informed, externally-focused take on horror. It's definitely horror, but a lot of folks, myself included, don't find that type of horror particularly scary. What's scary for me is the subtler, more internally focused kind of horror that CofD focuses on. YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915646#post915646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nWoD left more breathing room. The True Fae aren't trying to eat the world, the Exarchs couldn't care less about you personally as long as you aren't pocking your nose in their business. The scale is smaller, you can go it alone or with a few friends and not have to live in constant fear. Unless you're a hunter or a changeling, in which case you should be afraid, because sooner or later there will be things coming after you specifically.<br /> They're probably coming right now, in fact.<br /> ...Why aren't you running already, fool?!<br /> <br /> Seriously though, Hunter and Changeling are the only nWoD that I can see as horror, wih perhaps Prometheans when Pandorans wake up. Otherwise things are too impersonal and random to set a horror mood.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's that shallow reading exaggerated for the sake of argument again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T11:31:08-07:00","id":915732,"title":"","content":"Something i've noticed, in regards to change i make, is that often times they come from an inaccurate interpretation of the fluff. But what happens is when i figure my mistake sometimes i still end up preferring the inaccurate interpretation, either because it highlights well elements that i want to present a game or simply because i've internalized my first interpretation better. <br /> <br /> As an example. <br /> When i first read mage i thought that the seers of the throne were sleepers who in exchange for obediance are given power by the exarch. I liked that it would highlight a difference between understanding power and being given power.<br /> <br /> Now i've been told (and i agree) that its not how the seers are presented in the books. But i cant help it, i still prefer my (wrongful) interpretation nonetheless. And it can be said that i'm 'missing the point' in regards to the seers and what they represent in the setting, but i still things that this alternate interpretation is well within the themes of mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T11:54:01-07:00","id":915744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915726#post915726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't actually played or read Apocalypse, but from what I understand, the &quot;Captain Planet&quot; criticism isn't about the environmentalist themes, it's about the way they're handled. Presenting climate change as a problem you can punch in the face and pollution as something perpetrated by evil corporations actually hurt the environmentalist message. I have no idea if those complaints are accurate, and I would be willing to bet they're founded on shallow reading of the material and exaggerated for the purpose of argument, just like most recurring complaints about WoD and CofD are. But that's my understanding of where those complaints are coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little of both. You wouldn't wipe out all pollution and racism, but you would severely diminish it. The Wyrm is a corrupting influence, but it and its agents corrupt what already exists, for the most part.<br /> <br /> The Maeljin Incarna are primarily human and humanoid-oriented influences, like madness and fear, but also encompass things like Entropy and Disease, though primarily seems to urge a sort of apathy towards the things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book of the Wyrm</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Destroying one of the Maeljin Incarna is a world-shaking feat that should be a major part of a chronicle. It will also have obvious and wide-ranging consequences. For example, killing Lord Steel would lower the level of hatred in the world.<br /> Hatred would still dwell in human and shapeshifter hearts without help from any aspect of the Wyrm, but the Wyrm inflames it, and the destruction of Lord Steel would significantly weaken the Urge Wyrm Abhorra. As a result, the level of racially based violence, gay-bashing and similar crimes would decrease, and social tensions and ethnic hostilities around the world would decline. To the bulk of humanity, all of these changes would seem perfectly natural, if somewhat puzzling, but most of the Changing Breeds would know what had actually occurred.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Elemental Wyrms represent more of a twisting of the four elements. Smog, Sludge, Toxin, and Balefire, which involves radiation as well as actual balefire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Destroying one of the elemental Maeljin Incarna would increase the difficulty of summoning that type of elemental by at least +4 (difficulties over 10 make the summoning impossible) everywhere and would noticeably decrease the amount and virulence of the actual physical element everywhere on Earth. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T12:41:06-07:00","id":915765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915701#post915701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How impersonal or random would it be if your own sense of inferiority literally possessed you in a climax of bloody retribution, leaving the mauled and half-eaten corpses of you abusive family behind? Your weakness literally gave birth to the thing that triggered the event, you just needed a little nudge. Now life as you know it is undone, and you can't but recall the sweet, essence-ridden taste of your parents and sister before you attempt to sleep. So much that you wake up drenched in blood and guts. You can't help it anymore.<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random would it be that your obsession with altering the event that forever changed your life never happened, so much that you shattered the timeline in such a fashion that the person you loved the most in the entire world is but a figment of your oneiros? And you have nobody else to blame but yourself? And your new obsession is now to stop yourself from ever attempting such.<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random is it that, despite your otherworldly birth, after attaining a taste of what being human is, you cannot condone the sight of your fellow fallen angels ripping people's souls apart for a cheap fa\u00e7ade at life, instead of carefully building the perfect lie to move under God's radar? And when you, yourself are forced to cash in your last chance soul pact, because that's better than being ripped to shreds and recycled, like a common piece of glass?<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random is it to watch your mother witter slowly with the years, see dementia sweep in to the point she doesn't even recognizes you when you visit her at night, because she recalls a funeral for her son with an empty casket that your Sire arranged for? How do you keep your humanity after you bow to yourself to spare her the indignity of a rotting brain and a broken life without notion for her own identity?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Definitely not impersonal or random...but a bit melodramatic?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I enjoy personal horror, it too easily becomes tragedy porn if you let it. One of the worst games I was ever in became almost a contest to see whose character was the most miserable. Each character was supposed to be miserable and a tortured soul in one way or another, and didn't become fun until we all started laughing about it. You can only do so many iterations of I lost people I love, or I can't be near those I love because of what I am before it becomes funny rather than meaningful.<br /> <br /> Take your 4th point, while the sire, and being dead aren't in my repertoire, that wasn't the focus of the horror. I had a father who was losing himself to dementia and the idea of losing my humanity was never in question. Maybe because we talked a lot about assisted suicide when he was well, but the stress of dealing with red tape and my family's anger was much more the issue and burden. That's the problem. The horrific themes sometimes feel forced to the point of incredulity. Two years ago we played Innocents and we still make jokes about how all children are psychopaths until puberty slowly cleanses their souls. I'm sorry, but when my 8 year old niece smooshes an ant my first thought isn't she's going to have depression for years over her guilt.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I find personal horror only good when used in small doses, and with much of their core elements seem to be based on it, WoD seems to overuse it and can make it seem trite. Horror as a genre does not lend itself well to rpgs because once they are concluded, few horror stories have a reason to continue. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd argue the only real horrific game in the lineup is Vanilla mortal. Even as a hunter you have knowledge and the strength of belief you can defeat what is coming, the very antithesis of horror. What all the line ups have are dark themes and Creepiness. The idea of the dangerous bizarre isn't horrifying, but creepiness is easier to sustain and still makes the players on edge while having power when they are confronted.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:58:20-07:00","id":915827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915701#post915701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How impersonal or random would it be if your own sense of inferiority literally possessed you in a climax of bloody retribution, leaving the mauled and half-eaten corpses of you abusive family behind? Your weakness literally gave birth to the thing that triggered the event, you just needed a little nudge. Now life as you know it is undone, and you can't but recall the sweet, essence-ridden taste of your parents and sister before you attempt to sleep. So much that you wake up drenched in blood and guts. You can't help it anymore.<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random would it be that your obsession with altering the event that forever changed your life never happened, so much that you shattered the timeline in such a fashion that the person you loved the most in the entire world is but a figment of your oneiros? And you have nobody else to blame but yourself? And your new obsession is now to stop yourself from ever attempting such.<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random is it that, despite your otherworldly birth, after attaining a taste of what being human is, you cannot condone the sight of your fellow fallen angels ripping people's souls apart for a cheap fa\u00e7ade at life, instead of carefully building the perfect lie to move under God's radar? And when you, yourself are forced to cash in your last chance soul pact, because that's better than being ripped to shreds and recycled, like a common piece of glass?<br /> <br /> How impersonal or random is it to watch your mother witter slowly with the years, see dementia sweep in to the point she doesn't even recognizes you when you visit her at night, because she recalls a funeral for her son with an empty casket that your Sire arranged for? How do you keep your humanity after you bow to yourself to spare her the indignity of a rotting brain and a broken life without notion for her own identity?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does feel rather random to me? I mean, what are the chances for those things to happen? Do people live in dread of those things happening to them?<br /> Yes, when it does happen you have some very personal horror, but there's no real feeling of anticipation of those particular fates, isn't it? Who live their lives in fear of being Claimed? or breaking time? Those are freak events or personal tragedies, that do not really define the game's mood, unless that's what the ST is going for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915726#post915726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't actually played or read Apocalypse, but from what I understand, the &quot;Captain Planet&quot; criticism isn't about the environmentalist themes, it's about the way they're handled. Presenting climate change as a problem you can punch in the face and pollution as something perpetrated by evil corporations actually hurt the environmentalist message. I have no idea if those complaints are accurate, and I would be willing to bet they're founded on shallow reading of the material and exaggerated for the purpose of argument, just like most recurring complaints about WoD and CofD are. But that's my understanding of where those complaints are coming from.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think it's so much about aesthetics as it is about mood. Punk is founded on righteous indignation, fighting back against the systems that oppress you. For a lot of people, fighting back is the antithesis of horror. I don't really agree with that perspective, but I certainly understand it, as helplessness is often an important element of horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree aabout helplessness. I just find that a futile effort is worse than no effort. Might just be me, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915726#post915726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think another part of the issue is that WoD is more externally-focused horror, while CofD is more personally focused. In WoD, the fear is of the monsters that are out there, walking unseen among us. In CofD, the fear is of the self, of what you're capable of, of the things you've forgotten or ignored because it's easier to pretend nothing is wrong than to face the truth that the momsters out there are nothing compared to the monsters in here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also agree, though I was focused more on the cWoD and the nWoD, than the CofD which as I mentioned, seems to use the tropes of both previous games. I just think that the kind of horror used in the nWoD is not the game's defining feature. It feels more like a sandbox whith all kind of cool and scary shit lying about, which you can use to play however you want. Which to me seems to fit Urban Fantasy more than just Horror.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915726#post915726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's that shallow reading exaggerated for the sake of argument again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll need you to be more explicit, there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:01:53-07:00","id":915828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915827#post915827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does feel rather random to me? I mean, what are the chances for those things to happen? Do people live in dread of those things happening to them?<br /> Yes, when it does happen you have some very personal horror, but there's no real feeling of anticipation of those particular fates, isn't it? Who live their lives in fear of being Claimed? or breaking time? Those are freak events or personal tragedies, that do not really define the game's mood, unless that's what the ST is going for.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that was a Werewolf, a Mage, a Demon, and a Vampire in that order. So that literally is the theme and mood of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:47:12-07:00","id":915855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915409#post915409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly let me mention something about <b>Mummy</b> (of course). I think a lot of people are slightly disappointed that the game wasn't second edition especially since the game afterwards we knew would be, but that there's one thing that's the root of a few issues (like non-Iremite Mummies): <i>people mistaking backstory for metaplot</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a big part of this has to do with people having different notions of what metaplot <i>is</i>. For many, it's some aspect of the setting that tends to intrude on the story you're trying to tell \u2014 that is, the game tends to push you to tell (some variant of) the story that the game's designers had in mind rather than the story <i>you</i> have in mind. In this regard, it's related to the question of how \u201ctoolboxy\u201d the game is. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915409#post915409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone else in the thread talked about how <b>Mage</b> exists in its own secluded world that no other splat can interact with (which is interesting because that's the second biggest jumped-to-conclusion people make regarding <b>Mummy</b>), but isn't that the point? That <i>being a Mage</i> gives you secret occult knowledge that drives you mad and isolates you from friends and family because they don't get it? Simultaneously and ironically, <b>Mage</b> is probably the best game for crossover despite <b>Beast</b> being designed for it, which, incidentally, explains that Beasts are native to a realm described in <b>Mage</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason why <b>Mage</b> has a reputation for sticking its nose in everyone else's business. I hadn't thought of it that way before, but you're right; conceptually at least, <b>Mage</b> works far better as a crossover-friendly game than any other, <b>Beast</b> included. Even in 2e terms, there's the fact that Mysteries are by no means sequestered in a box that only mages deal with; they spill out and spread over the entire setting, with every other gameline being a potential source of Mysteries for a mage to investigate. Not to mention <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>' \u201cyes, <i>you too</i> can make a vampire!\u201d\u2026<br /> <br /> That said, my pet peeve with respect to <b>Mage</b> is how it's designed with its own themes being paramount and with little to no regard as to how that might affect crossover play. Which is fine in and of itself, but sticks in my craw when the developers then insist that other gamelines should conform to <b>Mage</b>'s way of doing things. In particular, the relationship between mages and mortals, and the relationship between <b>Mage</b> and <b>Hunter</b>: in <b>Mage</b>, mortals who haven't been changed by the supernatural are usually Sleepers, and thus at an <i>overwhelming</i> disadvantage when dealing with mages. Which arguably is very appropriate for the themes of <b>Mage</b>. But then you get into <b>Hunter</b> (incidentally, arguably the main rival to <b>Mage</b> in terms of crossover potential), which has as one major theme the notion that ordinary humans aren't nearly as helpless as they seem, and you get statements from the Mage developer that if he has any say in the matter, hunters <i>aren't</i> going to be able to find any chinks in the \u201cSleeping Curse\u201d glass ceiling that prevents them from having a fair shot at confronting an out-of-control mage. It's <b>Hunter</b>; the whole <i>point</i> of the game is to surprise the supernatural denizens of the ChroD by achieving things that they think are beyond your grasp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:04:09-07:00","id":915928,"title":"","content":"Yeah, corporate greed and pollution and so on are serious problems that are ripe for horror- but Apocalypse presents those problems as &quot;horrible spirit monsters are controlling Puppy Kickers Incoporated so hulk out and start ripping out throats&quot;. I mean, I'm exaggerating, and you don't have to play it that way, but that's the bluntest way to put it. Again, there's nothing wrong with that- 90s-as-hell splatterpunk can be fun as hell, but you can't exactly say that Apocalypse provides a grounded look at the horror of pollution and so on. <br /> <br /> And...I'm really not sure how you can look at Vampire, Promethean, Mummy, and Demon without getting horror vibes. Werewolf, Mage, and Beast are debatable, yeah, but there's a TON of clearly demonstrated horror in the Kindred condition. <br /> <br /> Plus, you can't really just &quot;leave the monsters alone and you'll be safe&quot;- you never know when a Stirge or a Huntsman or a Privateer or your Keeper or so on will take an interest in you, or an angel or stigmatic notices something suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:08:56-07:00","id":915931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915646#post915646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard a lot of people mention Captain Planet in relation to W:tA, as if the ecologist theme of the game somehow made it silly or goofy. I don't get how taking seriously a very real and very deadly issue is supposed to lessen the horror of the game.<br /> Still, apart from this, it seems to come down to aesthetics? Like the punk athmosphere is seen as 'diluting' the horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>The feeling that many have is that it <i>doesn't</i> take the issue seriously. Pentex might as well be run by Hoggus Greedly and Dr Blight, and adding to the comparison is the way that Tribe is handled so ridiculously. It's both an ethnic caricature complete with phenotype <i>and</i> an opt-in socio-political faction. With the fact that everyone is going to want to play a different Tribe, you've got a multi-ethnic band of do-gooders fighting for Gaia (another reason for the comparison) against villains who want to make the world gross and dirty because they worship pollution. That's not taking environmentalism seriously, that's turning it into a Saturday morning cartoon. Much like Hoggus Greedly and Dr Blight, Pentex doesn't want to poison the world because it's cheaper than safely disposing of their industrial waste or finding alternative sources of cleaner energy; they do it because Hexus told them all about <a href=\"https://youtu.be/hr4knvNNgtU\" target=\"_blank\">Toxic Love</a>. <br /> <br /> And presenting that kind of world outlook doesn't really do well to convey a sense of hopelessness or paranoia. I mean, keeping just in Apocalypse, half the reason the world is so garbage is because the Garou Nation is what is clinically known as &quot;pants on head incompetent&quot;. They're like a nation of Batman. Sure, they have the power to fix things and make the world better, but instead of actually approaching problems sensibly, they'd rather just rip and tear like the Doomguy. Punching out Pentex is a lot more <i>fun</i> than actually working to socially or politically undermine them. The few factions that <i>do</i> try an approach outside of CRINOS SMASH are derided for it, or even accused of being Weaver tainted. The fact that Black Spiral Dancers exist isn't surprising, what's surprising is that the whole Nation hasn't caught on to the beat. It's hard to feel like you're fighting despair when OOC it's patently obvious that the &quot;Good Guys&quot; are incompetent at everything they do. And at a certain point it becomes less hopeless and more pointless.<br /> <br /> Contrast this with nWoD, where, yes, the True Fae don't want to eat the world and the Exarchs don't care about you personally. But really, neither did Pentex, or the Sabbat. That Tzimisce? He turned your family into chairs because he hated you. The allies turned Fomor? They were given the Uruk-hai treatment because you screwed up. Events in nWoD actually matter, often to you personally. They're not &quot;this is the way the world has always been&quot;, they're &quot;the world is now effecting <i>you</i>.&quot; You pissed off the Seer, you made someone mad. And even then, just because things are smaller in scope doesn't mean they're less hopeless or paranoid. Once you've dipped your toes in the water of the Supernatural, you know that you're not safe. Walking to your car at night you might get grabbed by some blood sucking corpse, possessed by a Spirit, attacked by a living shadow that eats flesh, be victim to a hellhound, learn that chupacabra are real, get snatched by faeries, or any number of things. You have ever reason to be paranoid. If you don't belong to a faction, you have even more reason to be afraid, as the Firetouched might capture and try to convert you, the Seers might threaten your family if you don't do as they say, a Reaper might think your soul looks tasty, the VII might make you part of their spooky hivemind. Hell, being <i>part</i> of a faction may make it worse, as suddenly you have to deal with politics. Who's to say your rival in the Consilium won't compel the pizza guy to bring you a bomb? You're a thorn in the prince's side, but why does he keep licking his lips whenever he looks at you? This is also ignoring the existentialist threats, which by and large seem to outnumber oWoD and be handled better. The Abyss, the Seers, the Strix, the Idigam, the Host, Spirits, Ghosts, etcetera etcetera. They don't need to directly threaten to destroy the whole world--and even in oWoD no one really wanted to do that--to be meaningful and threatening.<br /> <br /> &quot;Breathing room&quot; from silly Vampire Illuminati vs Vampire Gangbanger conspiracies and Captain Planet villains doesn't mean a world free of paranoia. The Black Spiral or Hand isn't going to go after you personally for no reason, but they might still see you all on your lonesome and feel like you'd make a good snack. That kind of paranoia hasn't really changed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seriously though, Hunter and Changeling are the only nWoD that I can see as horror, wih perhaps Prometheans when Pandorans wake up. Otherwise things are too impersonal and random to set a horror mood. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915827#post915827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does feel rather random to me? I mean, what are the chances for those things to happen? Do people live in dread of those things happening to them?<br /> Yes, when it does happen you have some very personal horror, but there's no real feeling of anticipation of those particular fates, isn't it? Who live their lives in fear of being Claimed? or breaking time? Those are freak events or personal tragedies, that do not really define the game's mood, unless that's what the ST is going for.<br /> I agree about helplessness. I just find that a futile effort is worse than no effort. Might just be me, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who lives in fear of the events you mentioned? Does your vampire really expect to randomly have a Tzimisce turn his family into furniture? Those examples aren't even random, they're often the core theme of the game.<br /> <br /> Since for once <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> and I are on the same page, and because it's the kind of thing that I was talking about just last page, a few examples:<br /> I'm going to brush over it, but in <b>Old World of Darkness</b> your main source of Horror is ostensibly the fact that the world is shitty and you can do nothing about it. Ancient conspiracies and pollution cults and people who... want magic to be available to everyone in the form of technology (how terrible!) rule the world. Lip service is paid to how scary and powerful these groups are, but the attitude is definitely one of PUNK. You're rebelling against the status quo. You're fighting back against the simplistic pastiche of corporations that oppress the world, or telling your elders (literally, Elders) where to stick it. By and large, though, you don't have anything that holds you back from being a Vampion.<br /> In <b>Requiem</b>, you're dealing with your own inner demons. You struggling nightly with the fact that you're a monster, or at the very least a parasite. The more monstrous you become, the harder it is to even interact with normal people. In <b>2e</b>, you have to keep your friends and allies close, because they keep you grounded and closer to the Man than the Beast, but they're in danger because of how close they are to you. Not just danger from your rivals or enemies, but danger from you. You might harm them, whether by snapping at them and Frenzying, drinking them too deeply, or simply hurt them in the same way that an alcoholic hurts those around her. Doing the things you need to survive--murder, destruction, using unnatural abilities, joining the social groups--makes you feel less and less human, which in turn makes it harder to act human. You can harden yourself to the things you do, but each time you do you gain a bane, and in doing so become more of a monster. This isn't even touching on the actual supernatural threats vampires face, in both editions: VII, Belial's Brood, sectarian infighting, the Strix, and every spooky disgusting bloody thing in Wicked Dead.<br /> In <b>Forsaken</b>, you aren't even human anymore and really you never were. You have to find balance between your shifting nature and more to the point you have to keep the balance of the world around you. You know that you did nothing wrong, but that doesn't mean you don't have penance to pay for the crimes of an ancient ancestor. But more than that is the fact that you are a <i>weapon</i>. Not a safe, secure weapon, either. You're not a rifle stored with the safety on and the ammunition separate in a locked case. You're <i>dynamite</i>, left to sweat and break down. Every time you go into battle, you're juggling those sticks. Something--some<i>one</i>--is going to <i>fucking die</i>, or damned near close to it. And if you lose control, everything is going to explode and the people you want to protect are going to die at your hands, and you'll wake from it with your face ear-deep in your little sis' chest with the taste of her heart still on your lips, and you'll have to live with just how <i>good</i> her Essence tastes. <b>2e </b>of course strengthens that theme. Your lack of control may spread. When you snap, everyone you fight with snaps as well. You all become a surge of fur and muscle and death and blood and viscera. More than that, your Pack is more than just nine foot death dealers. It's frail and fragile mortals, who may not even know they're a part of something that puts them in danger. Will you threaten their wellbeing when you go after a rival Pack? Will the Host or the sorcerer or the unkillable corpse think twice about wearing their skin?<br /> In <b>Awakening</b>, it's easy to ignore the horror. Easy even for the characters themselves to ignore the fact that the world is a prison meant to contain the vastness and power of the untempered soul. It's easy for characters to forget that when they impose their will upon the world, they risk becoming convinced that their way is not just the right way, but the only way. Not just their political beliefs, but their personal take on how physics and nature should be wrangled into submission by their will. If becoming a mad scientist isn't horrifying enough for you, there's always the fact that your Magic is inherently inimical to the world. You impart your will, but watching you work it causes the cursed minds of those around you to reel in pain, and threatens to destroy Magic itself one bite at a time as your careless use of power brings taint and ruin into the world. But all that you need is just out of Reach, just a little further... And of course there's the temptation of power. You've had a taste, sure, but the first taste is always free. Are you willing to sell your soul? Sell someone else's soul?<br /> In <b>Lost</b>, well, you already feel there's horror in Changeling, but you seem to think the main source of concern is the Gentry. The truth of the matter is that they aren't a problem. They may not even know you're gone, more or less care about one little broken plaything. No, what you should be worried about as a Changeling is the fact that your life is in tatters. Sexual assault is the go-to metaphor, but this is a metaphor. You weren't just raped, you were raped by a hurricane that not only tore our your heart and made it so you'd never love again, but tore your house apart and threw you into the wilds, except none of the people around you were any the wiser. You're an outcast now. Your life is no longer there, and may even have been taken over. You're constantly given the reminder that you are no longer human, and more than that, there's the worry that the things you know might not even be real.<br /> In <b>Created</b> you're broken. A silly little <i>thing</i> that thinks it might possibly maybe be almost like a human. The world around you burns and boils and flinches at your unwholesome, broken presence. Everyone around you can sense, even if they can't see, that you're flawed. They know the deep dark secret that you harbour, the fact that you're not &quot;real&quot;. They know that you live a half life, missing some integral spark of humanity. It's something that you feel, too, but that yearning need doesn't exactly come with instructions. The only way for you to ever <i>fix</i> the problem is to try whatever you can to overcome your existential angst and ennui.<br /> In <b>Hunter</b> you also seem to consider that horrifying, but what do you find horror about it? Is it the fact that the monsters are stronger, faster, possibly even smarter than you, with supernatural powers that you may not be able to match, much less comprehend? Or is it the fact that you're driven to do horrible things to protect people? You're unable to snuff out the candle and go back to sleep. You're unable to rest when you know the things that lurk in the darkness. What are you willing to do to keep them in the dark--to chase them far away from the firelight? What knowledge will you use, no matter how forbidden? What laws will you break? How far will you go in the name of a supposed greater good? Even if you tell yourself that you did the right thing, will you be able to sleep at night, or will the faces of those all too human monsters stare back at you in fear and surprise and judgemental anger whenever you close your eyes? Putting aside the things you do, what about the things you've <i>seen</i>? That walking corpse last week went down easily, but the grisly scene it left behind will stay with you.<br /> I'm not going to bother doing the rest, this comment is already pretty long, Geist tends to get called out as not being horror, but there's a lot there with the nature of the Geist, I just don't think that it gets enough attention or mechanical weight. I know nothing about Mummy, and I feel Beast has Geist's problems. <b>Demon</b>'s horror is very similar to the horror of oWoD, but it tends to eschew the whole stereotype-as-player-type aspects, and focuses more on the thriller aspects of maintaining cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll need you to be more explicit, there. </div> </div> </div>She's saying that you're intentionally getting the games wrong to make your point, as outlined above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:11:31-07:00","id":915932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915827#post915827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does feel rather random to me? I mean, what are the chances for those things to happen? Do people live in dread of those things happening to them?<br /> Yes, when it does happen you have some very personal horror, but there's no real feeling of anticipation of those particular fates, isn't it? Who live their lives in fear of being Claimed? or breaking time? Those are freak events or personal tragedies, that do not really define the game's mood, unless that's what the ST is going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the world of Chronicles of Darkness? Very common. It's a canon fact that most people have had or know someone who has had some kind of experience with the supernatural. But they keep their heads down for fear of drawing attention, fear of being seen as crazy, fear of admitting to themselves what they know is out there. They live in constant fear, but they work damn hard to convince themselves they don't, and it almost works. At least, it works well enough to maintain a functioning society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915827#post915827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree aabout helplessness. I just find that a futile effort is worse than no effort. Might just be me, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They both have a place in horror. The thing is, that &quot;go down swinging&quot; reaction to the futility of the effort is a very punk attitude. Lots of folks (again, myself included) resonate more with a more goth-informed reaction of existential anxiety and find works that focus on that mood more horrifying. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915827#post915827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also agree, though I was focused more on the cWoD and the nWoD, than the CofD which as I mentioned, seems to use the tropes of both previous games. I just think that the kind of horror used in the nWoD is not the game's defining feature. It feels more like a sandbox whith all kind of cool and scary shit lying about, which you can use to play however you want. Which to me seems to fit Urban Fantasy more than just Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>CofD is nWoD, the only difference is edition and branding. And the toolbox nature of the game does allow it to be played without the horror aspects, but it's not the default assumption or the intended theme, which, to bring this back to the topic, is why folks who find the system fighting them when they try to play it as straight urban fantasy often get told they're missing the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915827#post915827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll need you to be more explicit, there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the reading of the CofD game lines you presented in that post to be founded on a shallow reading of the text and suspect it may have been exaggerated for the sake of supporting your argument. This is quite common for detractors of both CofD and WoD to do, and it's the place glib statements like &quot;Appcalypse is furry Captain Planet&quot; and &quot;Forsaken is furry spirit border patrol&quot; come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:26:29-07:00","id":915935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915855#post915855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">conceptually at least, <b>Mage</b> works far better as a crossover-friendly game than any other, <b>Beast</b> included.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter is best! Not only does it encourage you to play with the other splats, it provides rules for creating them. Sure, 1e's Dread Powers weren't nearly as developed, and it wasn't until supplements that monster creation became more detailed, but it's the <i><b>idea</b></i> presented in Hunter that makes it the best. (Or I guess <b>Hunter</b>, since you're making me look bad with your adherence to formatting). That's why Hunter will likely always be my favourite game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, my pet peeve with respect to <b>Mage</b> is how it's designed with its own themes being paramount and with little to no regard as to how that might affect crossover play. Which is fine in and of itself, but sticks in my craw when the developers then insist that other gamelines should conform to <b>Mage</b>'s way of doing things. In particular, the relationship between mages and mortals, and the relationship between <b>Mage</b> and <b>Hunter</b>: in <b>Mage</b>, mortals who haven't been changed by the supernatural are usually Sleepers, and thus at an <i>overwhelming</i> disadvantage when dealing with mages. Which arguably is very appropriate for the themes of <b>Mage</b>. But then you get into <b>Hunter</b> (incidentally, arguably the main rival to <b>Mage</b> in terms of crossover potential), which has as one major theme the notion that ordinary humans aren't nearly as helpless as they seem, and you get statements from the Mage developer that if he has any say in the matter, hunters <i>aren't</i> going to be able to find any chinks in the \u201cSleeping Curse\u201d glass ceiling that prevents them from having a fair shot at confronting an out-of-control mage. It's <b>Hunter</b>; the whole <i>point</i> of the game is to surprise the supernatural denizens of the ChroD by achieving things that they think are beyond your grasp. </div> </div> </div>I feel that's a little disingenuous but also a benefit, for the most part. Disingenuous because Dave doesn't think anything outside of Mage should conform to Mage. He's said that the Lobotomy Tactic wouldn't work in Mage, it would just produce a Mad One, but that it's a Hunter Tactic. He's also said that Hunters can't get passed the Sleeping Curse because <i>no</i> Sleeper can. (Although I do think that Quiescence is a bit arbitrary when it keeps coming back even after the fact, though if I understand it right that's the Exarch's fault). No mortal, Hunter or not, can avoid Quiescence unless they're a Sleepwalker, which requires at least 1 dot in any inherent supernatural ability, or the one dot Sleepwalker merit.<br /> And if you ask me, wow, &quot;I keep dealing with all this Supernatural shit&quot; sounds like a perfectly valid justification for taking the Sleepwalker merit. Although he's also said (in relation to Sundered World and the Wise) that knowing someone is a wizard is perfectly fine. It's just seeing the Magic they work that's a problem.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;but also a benefit&quot; part, I feel like it makes Mage--or any game, since Hunter does it as well--a better game when it worries primarily about it's own thing. Yeah, keep the big stuff together (it would suck if every game used different Spirit rules, and I <i>do</i> feel it's arbitrary that the Primordial Dream is part of the Temenos but apparently the Skien is not the Oneiros) but there's no reason that Mage should care about other games. Likewise, Hunter is my favourite precisely because it plays fast and loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T18:34:57-07:00","id":915952,"title":"","content":"cWoD to me feels like dark pulp verging on gonzo satire at times to me, with only rare breaths of genuine emotional meat in a handful of Vampire books or tucked away in Wraith; it honestly feels like a bloodier Shadowrun more than anything else.<br /> <br /> nWoD/CofD earn horror points from me largely thanks to how much subtler it is as a universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T20:23:22-07:00","id":915998,"title":"","content":"On the subjective interpretation of the games, you can tell me Masquerade, Oblivion, and Fallen are horror games. Depending on my mood, you can also tell me Dreaming is a horror game.<br /> <br /> But I can't really believe that of Apocalypse, Ascension(particularly Ascension), or Reckoning. I can't comment on Resurrection.<br /> <br /> Try and tell me any of the ChroD games aren't horror and I'll just laugh, say Okay, and proceed to doubt your every statement unless I already have reason to do otherwise.<br /> <br /> I am a judgmental person. This should be well known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T21:00:49-07:00","id":916017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915928#post915928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, you can't really just &quot;leave the monsters alone and you'll be safe&quot;- you never know when a Stirge or a Huntsman or a Privateer or your Keeper or so on will take an interest in you, or an angel or stigmatic notices something suspicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>The odds of going completely untouched by the supernatural within the Chronicles of Darkness are next to nil.<br /> <br /> The odds of having a number of concrete instances of such contact in the single digits (or below the triple digits, if we're to be pessimistic) are dramatically higher if, as the mast majority of adults in the setting implicitly understand, you don't make it a point to get deeply and/or repeatedly involved with the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Sure, nothing's going to stop your life from becoming very interesting and possibly very lethal if something takes a powerful interest in you personally, but a) very few of the qualities monsters fixate on are unique enough that they can't find someone else and 2) much like having a lock on your front door, the aversion defense does a good enough job at deterring casual attempts on the sanctity of your living space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T21:13:04-07:00","id":916023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915935#post915935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that's a little disingenuous but also a benefit, for the most part. Disingenuous because Dave doesn't think anything outside of Mage should conform to Mage. He's said that the Lobotomy Tactic wouldn't work in Mage, it would just produce a Mad One, but that it's a Hunter Tactic. He's also said that Hunters can't get passed the Sleeping Curse because <i>no</i> Sleeper can. (Although I do think that Quiescence is a bit arbitrary when it keeps coming back even after the fact, though if I understand it right that's the Exarch's fault). No mortal, Hunter or not, can avoid Quiescence unless they're a Sleepwalker, which requires at least 1 dot in any inherent supernatural ability, or the one dot Sleepwalker merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing disingenuous about it. The above boils down to accepting that there are things in print for <b>Hunter</b> that are inconsistent with how he'd handle them in <b>Mage</b>, which isn't so much a statement of preference as a statement of fact. The one time I can recall (but unfortunately cannot seem to find) where Dave actually stated his personal preference was during a discussion speculating about Hunter 2e where he came out and said essentially what I mentioned above: that if he had any say in how <b>Hunter</b> 2e turned out, hunters would have no means to cope with the Sleeping Curse other than being Sleepwalkers. Furthermore, he's on record saying that if a cell of hunters confronts an Awakened mage, the hunters <i>will get curbstomped</i> \u2014 and that that's <b>Mage</b> working as intended. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915935#post915935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you ask me, wow, \u201cI keep dealing with all this Supernatural shit\u201d sounds like a perfectly valid justification for taking the Sleepwalker merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, I count it as a small victory; because I recall arguments to the effect that picking up the Sleepwalker Merit after character creation should be exceedingly difficult to do, and impossible without supernatural intervention. Upon review of the \u201cFitful Slumber\u201d Sleepwalker Merit, it does appear that Dave softened his stance:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Fitful Slumber (\u2022)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> The character has suffered three or more breaking points due to exposure to the Supernal or Abyss and is now considered a Sleepwalker, even if he did not start the game that way. <br /> <i>Effect:</i> Because of the regular abuse, your character is able to resist breaking points triggered by all things Abyssal or Supernal with a +2 bonus.</span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915935#post915935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although he's also said (in relation to Sundered World and the Wise) that knowing someone is a wizard is perfectly fine. It's just seeing the Magic they work that's a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915935#post915935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the \u201cbut also a benefit\u201d part, I feel like it makes Mage\u2014or any game, since Hunter does it as well\u2014a better game when it worries primarily about its own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly, yes. Games with a tendency toward crossover encounters (such as <b>Hunter</b> due to its whole premise, arguably <b>Mage</b> due to a mage's tendency to stick his nose into <i>everything</i>, and supposedly <b>Beast</b> due to its \u201cfamily of monsters\u201d concept) need to pay closer attention to the other gamelines than games without that tendency (pretty much every other gameline). <br /> <br /> Heck, <b>Mage</b> has the <i>Tremere</i>, Reaper Liches with a history deeply entangled with the Kindred. Name one other game (besides <b>Hunter</b>) that has anything like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T22:03:09-07:00","id":916034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915998#post915998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subjective interpretation of the games, you can tell me Masquerade, Oblivion, and Fallen are horror games. Depending on my mood, you can also tell me Dreaming is a horror game.<br /> <br /> But I can't really believe that of Apocalypse, Ascension(particularly Ascension), or Reckoning. I can't comment on Resurrection.<br /> <br /> Try and tell me any of the ChroD games aren't horror and I'll just laugh, say Okay, and proceed to doubt your every statement unless I already have reason to do otherwise.<br /> <br /> I am a judgmental person. This should be well known.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could probably argue that Werewolf and Mage aren't horror unless the Storyteller does a whole lot of work to break away from both fandom perceptions and the actual texts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T22:30:18-07:00","id":916038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916034#post916034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could probably argue that Werewolf and Mage aren't horror unless the Storyteller does a whole lot of work to break away from both fandom perceptions and the actual texts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you referring to Awakening and Forsaken here? The horror in Awakening is not overtly apparent in the text, and is completely ignored by a saddeningly large portion of the fandom, but it is present without having to change anything.<br /> <br /> Forsaken has a stronger Dr. Jekyl and Mr. Hyde subtheme than Requiem does, with a far deadlier Hulk mode and the addition of an undeniable urge to hunt and kill just about anything, including humans, that makes your berserker rage even deadlier and harder to resist if you don't indulge it often enough. That's all <i>before</i> taking into account the constant necessity to deal with alien creatures from another plane of existance or the struggle to balance between conflicting human and alien natures that fucks with you if you go too far in either direction. Werewolves are literally forced to keep themselves just human enough to be able to recognize themselves as monsters, or face loss of control that makes them <i>even worse</i> monsters. All the while maintaining ties to their humanity and to their alien heritage just strong enough to make them long for a deeper connection, while simultaneously keeping them at arm's length from the other side. Amd of course let's not forget the body horror aspect, which Forsaken has in spades. Oh, and if cosmic horror is more your thing, there is no shortage of elderitch abominations and alien gods from beyond the stars.<br /> <br /> Yeah, if Forsaken isn't a horror game, I don't know what is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-17-2016, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T22:31:39-07:00","id":916039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916034#post916034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could probably argue that Werewolf and Mage aren't horror unless the Storyteller does a whole lot of work to break away from both fandom perceptions and the actual texts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I actually have to break away from the text. But then again, Mage is the one game that horrifies me the most, and Werewolf sets up its' dominos so easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T02:34:54-07:00","id":916093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915855#post915855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then you get into <b>Hunter</b> (incidentally, arguably the main rival to <b>Mage</b> in terms of crossover potential), which has as one major theme the notion that ordinary humans aren't nearly as helpless as they seem, and you get statements from the Mage developer that if he has any say in the matter, hunters <i>aren't</i> going to be able to find any chinks in the \u201cSleeping Curse\u201d glass ceiling that prevents them from having a fair shot at confronting an out-of-control mage. It's <b>Hunter</b>; the whole <i>point</i> of the game is to surprise the supernatural denizens of the ChroD by achieving things that they think are beyond your grasp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter (1st edition, at least, who knows what 2nd ed will do) is actually the single CofD game that implicitly doesn't crossover with the other major splats. Instead, it occupies a world very closely parallel to the others, but one where the Hunters have a chance. This is seen through various Hunter tactics that work for Hunter: The Vigil, but only by directly ignoring established facts of the other game lines. No, in CofD, Mages can't lose their magic by specific lobotomy, but that's a Hunter tactic. No, Hunters can't stop werewolves from using innate shapeshifting, etc.<br /> <br /> Hunter looks like it crosses over, but only if you apply Hunter's rules to other splats and depower them. Otherwise, the splats... splat... Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 06-17-2016, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T03:08:26-07:00","id":916102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916034#post916034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could probably argue that Werewolf and Mage aren't horror unless the Storyteller does a whole lot of work to break away from both fandom perceptions and the actual texts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you could do that in regards to <b>Werewolf</b> at least, that'd be cool, because I'm having a hard time wrapping my head around it <i>not</i> being horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T05:12:58-07:00","id":916131,"title":"","content":"Isn't Hunter the game that tells you to create supernaturals in simpler versions to fit it's game, using it's own inbuilt system for monsters, so vampires that Hunter fights aren't Vampires-from-vampire-book and so on? I never understood why people find it crossover centric or crossover-fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T05:41:59-07:00","id":916141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915855#post915855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For many, it's some aspect of the setting that tends to intrude on the story you're trying to tell \u2014 that is, the game tends to push you to tell (some variant of) the story that the game's designers had in mind rather than the story <i>you</i> have in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I disagree slightly, I think that's a fair point. On the other hand, if you're going to break it down like that then I'll argue <i>all </i>the games do that. Like, that's what this thread is about, right? Or are we now just talking in circles? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915855#post915855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, my pet peeve with respect to <b>Mage</b> is how it's designed with its own themes being paramount and with little to no regard as to how that might affect crossover play. Which is fine in and of itself, but sticks in my craw when the developers then insist that other gamelines should conform to <b>Mage</b>'s way of doing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>If people can tell me if I want non-Iremite Mummies then I should look at <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Promethean</b> then I can tell people who want to Hunt Mages to look at something other than the Supernal Awakened of <b>Mage</b>. Sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:42:27-07:00","id":916156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916141#post916141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people can tell me if I want non-Iremite Mummies then I should look at <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Promethean</b> then I can tell people who want to Hunt Mages to look at something other than the Supernal Awakened of <b>Mage</b>. Sorry</div> </div> </div> </div>Rephrasing: if Joe tells you to look at <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Promethean</b> if you want non-Iremite mummies, then you can tell Sam to look somewhere other than <b>Mage</b> if he wants mages that hunters stand a chance against. <br /> <br /> Never mind that Joe and Sam are two different people, each with his own opinion on matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:19:46-07:00","id":916219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916131#post916131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Hunter the game that tells you to create supernaturals in simpler versions to fit it's game, using it's own inbuilt system for monsters, so vampires that Hunter fights aren't Vampires-from-vampire-book and so on? I never understood why people find it crossover centric or crossover-fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an option presented so you aren't obligated to buy other game lines for the sole purpose of statting your antagonists. If you want to use the other game lines though that is equally ideal. Most games I've played in have used the other game lines as written (because we're nerds and we buy a lot of RPG supplements) while using Hunter's monster rules to stat up things that don't fit neatly into a box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:22:22-07:00","id":916224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=915998#post915998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subjective interpretation of the games, you can tell me Masquerade, Oblivion, and Fallen are horror games. Depending on my mood, you can also tell me Dreaming is a horror game.<br /> <br /> But I can't really believe that of Apocalypse, Ascension(particularly Ascension), or Reckoning. I can't comment on Resurrection.<br /> <br /> Try and tell me any of the ChroD games aren't horror and I'll just laugh, say Okay, and proceed to doubt your every statement unless I already have reason to do otherwise.<br /> <br /> I am a judgmental person. This should be well known.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to go ahead and disagree on Reckoning at least. Reckoning is all about claustrophobic horror and desperation on a pretty much constant basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:26:34-07:00","id":916228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916224#post916224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go ahead and disagree on Reckoning at least. Reckoning is all about claustrophobic horror and desperation on a pretty much constant basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree, being Imbued is a powerful curse that is guaranteed to drive you insane or to death at the hands of supernatural, and likely both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:17:10-07:00","id":916259,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, lightsaber toothbrush.<br /> <br /> But point taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:23:32-07:00","id":916264,"title":"","content":"Cleave seems really cool right up until you realize its going to be your one and only trick for a very long time and all it really does is make sure the monsters know not to pull any punches with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:33:20-07:00","id":916271,"title":"","content":"This thread's gone in odd places...<br /> <br /> That said, HtR is a weird game regarding its themes and mood. While it aims to be horror, it has a lot of material that doesn't seem to remember that. The horror of the Hunt driving you insane is kind of lost when you've gotten tired of trying to juggle 4+ derangements on one PC and just start glossing over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:47:26-07:00","id":916281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916017#post916017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The odds of going completely untouched by the supernatural within the Chronicles of Darkness are next to nil.<br /> <br /> The odds of having a number of concrete instances of such contact in the single digits (or below the triple digits, if we're to be pessimistic) are dramatically higher if, as the mast majority of adults in the setting implicitly understand, you don't make it a point to get deeply and/or repeatedly involved with the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Sure, nothing's going to stop your life from becoming very interesting and possibly very lethal if something takes a powerful interest in you personally, but a) very few of the qualities monsters fixate on are unique enough that they can't find someone else and 2) much like having a lock on your front door, the aversion defense does a good enough job at deterring casual attempts on the sanctity of your living space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I was mostly talking about supernatural PCs there, as part of a larger sense of &quot;ChroD supernaturals don't have to worry about the apocalypse or the illuminati but will inevitably have to deal with Some Shit even if they're only doing the bare minimum to survive&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:10:45-07:00","id":916294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916271#post916271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread's gone in odd places...<br /> <br /> That said, HtR is a weird game regarding its themes and mood. While it aims to be horror, it has a lot of material that doesn't seem to remember that. The horror of the Hunt driving you insane is kind of lost when you've gotten tired of trying to juggle 4+ derangements on one PC and just start glossing over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As threads are wont to do.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say that H:tR is any more heavy handed with derangements than 1E NWoD core was. At least not in my experience. I never had an Imbued with more than two at any one time, and even that wasn't common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T14:25:09-07:00","id":916427,"title":"","content":"Depends how long you played I guess. The problem is that HtR Derangements weren't bad luck on degeneration rolls, they were hardcoded into having high Virtues. I had a game once with four players that lasted long enough two had 4 derangements, one had 5,and the last racked up 7. And that was technically because they were rolling <i>well</i> regarding things like Conviction gambles and the Edges that helped stave off Conviction dribble (like the Creedbook Visionary Edges). As the ST it was maddening to try to keep that much crazy from derailing everything.<br /> <br /> It also didn't really work well with the fluff side of things. You don't slowly lose yourself into the Hunt like HtV can manage via Morality/Integrity loss. HtR was a cliff. Virtues 0-6 you're fine, then you bump up to 7 and you snap automatically and at full force. If you spread out your Conviction to Virtue to max out at 6/6/6 (ha) you could have a decent collection of Edges without any mental issues, but if you go straight for your primary Virtue to 10 (8 less trade ins as well) so you can grab a level 4 Edge (you don't have to, but if you don't you're making ever getting a 5 that much harder), which leaves you with four Edges and four Derangements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T14:40:25-07:00","id":916438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916156#post916156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never mind that Joe and Sam are two different people, each with his own opinion on matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, man, of course. But the philosophy behind these games has always been &quot;don't let the mechanics prevent you from telling a good story&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T02:22:28-07:00","id":917255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=916438#post916438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, man, of course. But the philosophy behind these games has always been &quot;don't let the mechanics prevent you from telling a good story&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But I mean you don't have to, one of the draws of WoD is that the world is already done and it has long histories and preset ideas of how these things work in the world. If I want to create a vampire that doesn't drink blood, then I guess i could say the game is limiting my story... but it's part of the preset world. I get the frustrations, I do. And that is partly what this whole thread is about, not being pleased that the world is not available to our wishes. <br /> <br /> I feel there are only 3 options.<br /> 1) They make a book that while can't include all these different rules of play, at least offers some as a supplement book.<br /> 2) Onyx path makes a completely new system that is more like universal systems which would allow any idea we have to be a viable way to play, with little or no preset history/culture/cosmology to tie down our stories.<br /> 3) We homebrew/ houserule/ and disregard the parts we don't like since this conversation shows we are very different on how we feel about the world's workings and there is no possibility we will all agree. I don't think there is actually anything wrong with any of the systems even if I personally don't like how some were handled, but I don't think any of them limit the stories we can tell just by providing what they always did before. That is a preset world with it's own rules on how things work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:33:24-07:00","id":917533,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11938\" data-vbnamecard=\"11938\">3Comrades</a>: Option 1 already exists, that's what the Chronicler's Guides are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T16:22:14-07:00","id":917609,"title":"","content":"Eh. To me, part of the point of every individual table/group/session is that you're never going to perfectly render RPG systems into an actual play where every system is relevant and has the exact impact that their designer wanted. So, IMO, you <i>never</i> play RAW; it's just a spectrum of how much you acknowledge that and how much effort/formality you put into your hack. Tweaking the rules as you go feels very much like part of the point of playing a TTRPG rather than, say, Ocarina of Time.<br /> <br /> But I also developed a hatred from rules lawyering very, very early on and that probably informs a lot of my perspective. My general attitude when approaching TTRPGs is that the text is an inspirational piece of art, much like a novel or painting. The first thing to do is to engage with the text itself and figure out what the author <i>wants</i> to say, because to me, that's the part that matters. The second thing to do is to use your appreciation or criticism of the text as a basis for what you do yourself. It's extremely nonsensical to me that feel entitled to systems designed by someone else that help tell a story they want to tell: my response to a reading of Lord of the Rings might be to argue that Sauron shouldn't have been such a vague, amorphous villain, but I'm not entitled to ask Tolkien to change his text to suit my taste when reading it out loud to an audience; I'm only entitled to tell my own story in my own way and take from his text what I want to keep and discard what I'm not interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:49:29-07:00","id":918414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=917609#post917609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. To me, part of the point of every individual table/group/session is that you're never going to perfectly render RPG systems into an actual play where every system is relevant and has the exact impact that their designer wanted. So, IMO, you <i>never</i> play RAW; it's just a spectrum of how much you acknowledge that and how much effort/formality you put into your hack. Tweaking the rules as you go feels very much like part of the point of playing a TTRPG rather than, say, Ocarina of Time.<br /> <br /> But I also developed a hatred from rules lawyering very, very early on and that probably informs a lot of my perspective. My general attitude when approaching TTRPGs is that the text is an inspirational piece of art, much like a novel or painting. The first thing to do is to engage with the text itself and figure out what the author <i>wants</i> to say, because to me, that's the part that matters. The second thing to do is to use your appreciation or criticism of the text as a basis for what you do yourself. It's extremely nonsensical to me that feel entitled to systems designed by someone else that help tell a story they want to tell: my response to a reading of Lord of the Rings might be to argue that Sauron shouldn't have been such a vague, amorphous villain, but I'm not entitled to ask Tolkien to change his text to suit my taste when reading it out loud to an audience; I'm only entitled to tell my own story in my own way and take from his text what I want to keep and discard what I'm not interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I change things, but I feel rules are there to facilitate play and it is fine changing it if your group wants,but rule changes have to be upfront or players can feel duped. To me, a game isn't fun if I'm the only one telling the story, and because of that, the players need to know what I'm changing. If they signed up for a clear Evil Sauron, than I'm kinda cheating their play by taking that away. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Our</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> story doesn't have to be entitled to anyone, but I can't view it as just mine or that can ruin the fun for the others. Been in several groups that when the ST changed something dramatic about the world, players would go out of their way to avoid it if not talked about beforehand, because we didn't sign up for that. It can turn into some of the worst railroading, as even shared conceptions are at risk. One ST for WtF wanted to have lupus in the game, but mentioned the fact they were everywhere after the game started, even telling the Blood Talon they had a hard time being non-lupus. We had been open before about finding Lupus weird and uncomfortable, so the game became our wacky adventures of trying to find out where this mass Uratha delusion came from. It was a fun game.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I feel changing most mechanical rules doesn't have the same effect, but in WoD so much of the mechanics interact with the world. A player may build their character one way to find that their idea is void or other some such. Even something pure mechanics can be frustrating for players. Once made a character who I wanted to be great at classic wrestling, built them in a way that wouldn't give me an advantage. The first time I tried to grapple, the DM told me they didn't like the grappling rules so there wouldn't be any. When I complained, he said I could roll it like a normal attack, but I made the character so I could have a different combat experience and the DM was unfair not to make that clear from the beginning.<br /> <br /> guess what I am saying, is it's important everyone is on board with the rules or there can be disgruntled feelings as the ST forces a story the players may not have signed up forG</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T01:57:35-07:00","id":918505,"title":"","content":"Sorry I wasn't clear about that. Discussion with everyone else is such a basic assumption to me that I forget that it's non-obvious to other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T00:16:52-07:00","id":918969,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">Post deleted by moderator. Did you even read the terms of use before clicking &quot;I agree&quot;? If not then I suggest you do. You have some serious misconceptions about the CoD, you have engaged in edition warring, and what amount to personal attacks against the developers. You blatantly violated the rule about respecting others (in this case the developers) and will have a week off to think about how you word your criticisms in the future, next offense is a permanent ban. It's fine to say you don't care for an idea, it's another to accuse staff writers of supporting or advocating rape culture.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 06-22-2016, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T01:09:46-07:00","id":918993,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2313_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2313\" data-vbnamecard=\"2313\">Knit-I-Fine</a> There are so many things you said that I have a vehement negative reaction to, but this is America and we're not allowed to arrest or murder people for being <i><b>wrong</b></i>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Step 2: Remove the part where a person relationships are considered their property that they can sell off in contracts because that's super rapey, white wolf, what the hell were you thinking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will address this part, though. You do know that Vampire is basically one big rape metaphor, right? I mean, their blood is literally a date rape drug. Even then, I don't see how being able to trade off your own relationships is somehow rapey. It's <i>my</i> relationship. If I don't want to be part of it, that's my choice. It's not even as skeevy as debt trading (which can be done even if you've paid it off), and that's a real life thing that for some reason is legal.<br /> I feel like you're seeing things as &quot;validating rape culture&quot; that really aren't. It's like all those people who see games about fighting demons and say they're encouraging Satanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T01:42:23-07:00","id":919003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=918969#post918969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also if anyone knows how to make a drop down to hide parts of the post till open so they're less obtrusive for people who aren't interested let me know)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">... something like this?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The tag is literally spoiler /spoiler.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's time has come and gone, publishing new compilation content and the like for it as they're currently doing is a source of aggravation for me. </div> </div> </div>Kinda curious... how does its existence cause you any harm (obviously not physically) that's worth being aggravated about? Clearly people like the 20th lines well enough that a lot of people are happy even if you never want to play the games again.<br /> <br /> Also, kinda helps if you read the books yourself sometimes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mummy</b><br /> Disclaimer: I have not actually read the full Mummy book.<br /> It sounds to me like an oWoD splat that was put in nWoD for no reason. To me nWoD is about playing humans who have been changed by the wicked supernatural world they live in (with Promethean being an exception that's still on point because of the quest for humanity and not having 10,000+ ancient conspiracies and apocalypses looming and other hack oWoD writing still hanging around). </div> </div> </div>It has nothing to do with Mummy the Resurrection. Mummy the Curse (not sure why that's not a give away that being a Mummy in this game isn't all its cracked up to be) is very much about playing humans who have been changed by the wicked supernatural world they live in. It was just a very, very, very long time ago. You're basically playing an immortal slave to an empire so old humanity doesn't even know it exists, stuck in an never ending cycle of waking up full of power but massively disoriented, only to have your power drain out of you turning you more human-ish before you go back to sleep. It is very much somewhere between Requiem (your peers are largely ancient bastards and you all belong to groups that are morally dubious at best to try to pass eternity) and Lost (a huge amount of what you do is try to reclaim agency in the face of what you've been turned into by uncaring supernatural forces).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Step 2: Remove the part where a person relationships are considered their property that they can sell off in contracts because that's super rapey, white wolf, what the hell were you thinking? </div> </div> </div>They're... Demons. They buy and sell people's &quot;souls.&quot; That's kinda the point. Vampire feeding can be super rapey too... I never do get why vampires can mind control people into making themselves food doesn't get dinged as somehow being super rapey, but demons that buy people's lives is somehow too far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I heard that a line about &quot;Beasts hurt people because it's good for them&quot; got into the book as an in universe truth and if true maybe White Wolf needs to go through it's developers and figure out who's the person obsessed with validating rape culture and remove them from the creative team because between this idea and Demon it seems like they might have a serious reactionary problem. </div> </div> </div>It's not true. Beasts hurt people because they're monsters (but hey, so do vampires, and werewolves, mages, and changelings...). They have to choose what kind of harm they're going to do though, and that choice is a big one. It's not &quot;good&quot; for them. It's a necessity of their existence (again just like vampires needing to, you know, drink people's blood). If they don't feed (which is generally bad for their victims, but they have a choice - which is again important - in how bad) their inner monster will do it on it's own without any control.<br /> <br /> Also... can we not devalue the very real issue of rape culture by tossing it around like this? Games about monsters doing horrible things because <i>they're monsters</i> isn't validation of rape culture even if it involves rape. One of the core elements of rape culture is victim blaming. Demon doesn't blame humans for demons buying their lives away from them, and Beast doesn't blame humans for Beasts having supernatural drives to indulge in. It's on those supernatural critters (just like the rest) for doing what they do (even if they're generally victims in their own right).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:47:57-07:00","id":919116,"title":"","content":"Well, that was an exciting thing to miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T09:17:07-07:00","id":919126,"title":"","content":"Riffing off that post, rather than responding, a week or two ago I was thinking about how the Big Three splats each have very specific territories that express their monstrousness. Vampires in how their territory is people, blood dolls, and the political relationships. Werewolf in how both the Hisil and the Flesh and their occupants are just pawns that they move around the board. Mage in how Mysteries are these intellectual puzzles that they lay claim to the privilege of studying. Whereas Prom/Chan/Hunter are about ideas of home, rather than territory: finding your home, making your home, defending your home.<br /> <br /> Not a lot of meat on those bones, but whatever. Sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T12:47:31-07:00","id":919274,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=3Comrades;n917255]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Onyx path makes a completely new system that is more like universal systems which would allow any idea we have to be a viable way to play, with little or no preset history/culture/cosmology to tie down our stories. </div> </div> </div>I think that CoD would make a great generic horror / playing as supernaturals system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:32:56-07:00","id":919318,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> It certainly was.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> I don't really agree with those. Werewolves don't play political games or treat people like pawns, and the mysteries as puzzles that only Mages have the privilege of studying isn't really even true; you can delve into Mysteries without being Awakened (and in 2e it seems to be <i>how</i> you Awaken). Promethean isn't really about finding a home, it's about the pilgrimage. Changeling is maybe about making a home, but really it's more about anachronistic social structures as part of a living narrative.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5685_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5685\" data-vbnamecard=\"5685\">Archivist</a> I know, right? I really love the core mechanics of WoD, and wish there was a generic version. I should really start paying attention to all that Scion stuff and look over the &quot;alpha slice&quot; of it, since <s>Sardonyx</s>Storypath seems like exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-22-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T18:11:52-07:00","id":919421,"title":"","content":"Here's my 2 cents on what's going on. I'll use D&amp;D 5e as an example, which is a perfectly fine system BTW.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If you like Fantasy RPG, but don't like D&amp;D 5e, there's a wealth of other alternatives with very active communities and publishers. If you like Horror / Play as supernatural, there are very few alternatives. Yes, there is CoC, Chill, Dresden Files, etc. but they tend to be very narrow games but they don't have very active communities and publishers. If you want to play Vampires that aren't horrible people, it's not like you can play that other super popular Vampire game not made by White Wolf (there isn't one)</li> <li>D&amp;D 5e is designed to appeal to the widest possible audience. You like Grim and Gritty, there's all sorts of dials to tweak in the DMG that let you do that. Onyx Path has made the decision with the CoD 2e books to just do whatever they think is the most interesting, challenging, creative take on the material. You want to play Prometheans that are dark superheroes, good for you! They didn't make that game.</li> <li>D&amp;D 5e wasn't really designed around a laser like focus on theme/mood/activity. Onyx Path made the decision in the CoD 2e books to design all the mechanics and fluff supporting a single theme/mood/activity. Werewolf is about the hunt, and walking the razor line of balance as a monstrous hunter. Promethean is about becoming human from an unnatural creature. If you change the theme/mood/activity, the mechanics don't fit that.</li> </ol>However, 1 is opposed to 2 and 3. It's great that I want to play the Angel TV show as an RPG, but the new CoD 2e wasn't built to do that. I can do it, but the system wasn't designed do whatever anyone felt they wanted to do with whatever theme/mood/activity. WoD isn't a really good alternative because the books are full of metaplot, lore, and assumptions that make them equally not hackable.<br /> <br /> Now, it's not Onyx Path's responsibility to change 2 and 3 to accomodate 1. It would be cool if they did, and produced new Mirrors / Chronicles books for CoD 2e to support that. Yea, that would be cool HINT HINT HINT HINT.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T20:34:34-07:00","id":919483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919421#post919421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and produced new Mirrors</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. And books like that 1e WtF book that had rule ideas for changing lots of things, kind of a WtF Unearthed Arcana.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T23:03:31-07:00","id":919528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919318#post919318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> I don't really agree with those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919318#post919318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves don't play political games or treat people like pawns,</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes they do. That's <i>exactly</i> how you manage the resonance of an area and that's why Uratha don't actually <i>belong</i> to either the Spirit or the Flesh. You're constantly asserting your dominance because <i>you know better</i> on what needs doing. Your opinion of when and who spirits can Urge is paramount. The ramifications in the Hisil of human activity are <i>your</i> problem. And to solve these things, a Werewolf must hunt. They need to harry spirits and humans into doing what needs to be done in order to cause shifts in resonance.<br /> <br /> They create a bloody scene at a park in order to attract fear spirits and push out the joy spirits. They scare a politician into denying the zoning permit for a building that would destroy an important locus. They run another pack out of the city because they're encouraging violence spirits near a preschool. Why do they do these things? Not because it's fun, but because it shifts their physical environment closer to their ideal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919318#post919318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the mysteries as puzzles that only Mages have the privilege of studying isn't really even true;</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of Mage society is to arbitrate between conflicts of interest between groups of Mages trying to study the same Mystery. The <i>entire</i> point.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying &quot;Mages not Sleepers&quot;. I'm saying &quot;Mages not other Mages&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919318#post919318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean isn't really about finding a home, it's about the pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't distinguish those two things. Home isn't just a house with a fence. Home is about <i>belonging</i>. It's about <i>safety</i>. It's about <i>resting</i>. It's the foundation of your life.<br /> <br /> &quot;Home is where the heart is.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919318#post919318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling is maybe about making a home, but really it's more about anachronistic social structures as part of a living narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>...no. That's not what Changeling is about at all. I ... you realize Changeling is primarily about a trauma metaphor, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T00:58:00-07:00","id":919579,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> Trauma metaphor doesn't mean making a home. It's about support groups that take the form of anachronistic social structures that gain supernatural protection through taking part in a shared narrative (this is literally how Freehold creation works in 2e). Heck, even then most of the support group stuff gives way to infighting and trying to be a psychedelic version of Game of Thrones. c.f.: Miami, <i>Rose Bride's Plight</i> and even a bit of <i>Fear-Maker's Promise</i>.<br /> Also, Werewolves can tend to their garden, but they're not having these political machinations the way that vampires or Changelings or Mages are. They don't backstab and dick each other over, or try to gain social leverage (not as a rule, at least). They work more like gangs.<br /> You're right that Mage society is primarily there to oversee who gets to do what, but it's not exactly putting up limits or anything. Even in the sample cities the Consilia aren't arresting people for not following the rules, just glaring at them or waggling a finger. Harsher groups might blackball you or try to knife you from several yards away, but for the most part they won't care if you do that to each other so long as your fighting doesn't bother anyone else.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5685_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5685\" data-vbnamecard=\"5685\">Archivist</a> Some of the games do allow for tweaking the tone and theme and setting. I mean, there were several 1e books for exactly that in the Chronicler's Guides, and it can be argued that 2e as a whole is really just that same principle applied to a new edition. <br /> But yes, for the love of God, a (better) Mirrors would be amazing. Shards was the best part of that book, and is a concept that needs more space. The Chronicler's Guides also have that kind of thing, but all of them don't get the space they deserve and tend to be loose suggestions. I want a book of Dark Eras style settings in alternate genres. Fantasy, Sci-Fi, Cyberpunk, Martial arts, Weird West, with lots of system Hacks to shake things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T01:40:54-07:00","id":919593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919579#post919579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> Trauma metaphor doesn't mean making a home. It's about support groups that take the form of anachronistic social structures that gain supernatural protection through taking part in a shared narrative (this is literally how Freehold creation works in 2e). Heck, even then most of the support group stuff gives way to infighting and trying to be a psychedelic version of Game of Thrones. c.f.: Miami, <i>Rose Bride's Plight</i> and even a bit of <i>Fear-Maker's Promise</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Support groups are about making a home. Again, read my definition of what a home is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919579#post919579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Werewolves can tend to their garden, but they're not having these political machinations the way that vampires or Changelings or Mages are. They don't backstab and dick each other over, or try to gain social leverage (not as a rule, at least). They work more like gangs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you actually read my initial post? I'm not saying that Werewolves are Vampires. I'm saying that they treat humans and spirits like a resource allocation board game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919579#post919579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right that Mage society is primarily there to oversee who gets to do what, but it's not exactly putting up limits or anything. Even in the sample cities the Consilia aren't arresting people for not following the rules, just glaring at them or waggling a finger. Harsher groups might blackball you or try to knife you from several yards away, but for the most part they won't care if you do that to each other so long as your fighting doesn't bother anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I'd expect a death mark for Mages who step out of line. The only real way to punish a Mage is to deny them access to knowledge. If you can't do that, you pretty much have a choice between letting him do what he wants or murdering him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T03:12:33-07:00","id":919619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">rape culture and remove them from the creative team because between this idea and Demon it seems like they might have a serious reactionary problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading this toxic post I quit this thread. This is a horror RPG forum and not &quot;politically correct&quot; leftist website.<br /> <span style=\"color:red\">Embedded video removed by moderator</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-23-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T03:20:45-07:00","id":919621,"title":"","content":"Guys you are both right to some degree. How to roleplay correctly(tm) some of these games as the one true way is a bit much to argue about. I will say that several of the splats can be seen as the horror is using others, Vampire is more explicit, certainly werewolf, Changeling,Promethean and Demon. Don't know about Beast and Mage I am too biased to give an objective opinion. Point is, it is part of the horror, but only a part. <br /> <br /> Getting into wishy/washy concepts like Find a Home can always count. How you want to define it can cover...Demon, Changeling, Promethean,Hunter and even Werewolf and Mummy. It's a vague concept that can mean many things at once. Nevermind nearly Any chronicle can have it as a central theme.<br /> <br /> They can be more than one thing at once. I always felt vampire's horror was about losing yourself to your own vices and how that effects the world around you, Feel WtF is about the entire world against them. Promethean to find what being human means(the classic robot story), and Changeling is about emotion and how deeply that effects us for good or bad. <i>But that isn't the only way to interpret these things and many of them overlap.</i> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> It's like arguing if Lord of the Rings is about Good vs Evil, Christian Motifs, reawakening of Mythological Themes, or just an epic Fantasy. They can all be true, and a game even more so as STs can't help but stress particular themes more than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T06:27:31-07:00","id":919674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919579#post919579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Werewolves can tend to their garden, but they're not having these political machinations the way that vampires or Changelings or Mages are. They don't backstab and dick each other over, or try to gain social leverage (not as a rule, at least). They work more like gangs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a rule at all. Nearly every book has examples of Forsaken screwing over other Forsaken. It's a prime factor in the creation of protectorates, including first edition's Silver Syndicate and was the plot point behind stories in the Idigam Fiction Anthology, most notably 'Only One Way To Win,' and the entire concept of the Brethren War.<br /> <br /> As has been pointed out, though it probably shouldn't have to be, it's fine if you want to play a game where these things don't exist, but that's how you're running it, not a part of the game as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-23-2016, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:09:27-07:00","id":919752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919619#post919619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After reading this toxic post I quit this thread. This is a horror RPG forum and not &quot;politically correct&quot; leftist website.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">You're responding to a comment that was deleted, from a poster who got banned for the comment, and you're criticizing it for being politically charged by embedding an equally politically charged video. This is textbook flame bait. Don't do this.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-23-2016, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:25:29-07:00","id":919764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919752#post919752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:red\">You're responding to a comment that was deleted, from a poster who got banned for the comment, and you're criticizing it for being politically charged by embedding an equally politically charged video. This is textbook flame bait. Don't do this.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the warning, I'll pay more attention next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:57:25-07:00","id":919778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=919621#post919621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys you are both right to some degree. How to roleplay correctly(tm) some of these games as the one true way is a bit much to argue about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing about how to roleplay. I'm arguing about whether or not a particular approach to characterizing the broad themes of each gameline is valid.<br /> <br /> If the approach is useful for people planning out a chronicle or writing further supplements or homebrews, then that's seriously the only reason I bothered writing it down. Well, that and wanting to actually move the conversation away from the... other thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, let's presume I have a point. That's easy for me, because I think I have a point. What's next? Territoriality is interesting, because it's about seizing and holding ground. It's about occupied land. It smacks of a paternalistic imperialism. Which means that a useful thread for thinking about not just Vampire, but <i>also</i> Werewolf and Mage, is to think about how their basic mode of being, the assumptions and presumptions they make mostly subconsciously just <i>being themselves</i>, inflict collateral damage onto the world around them. It means that you can, for instance, characterize the Guardians of the Veil as <i>pacifist</i>, and create parallels between them and, say, the Vietnam War protesters who argued against American overreach. It means that, for instance, you can look at the Pure and the Seers as those who are too privileged to see or care about the collateral damage their actions inflict, which is another dimension to why they're antagonists that you can explore.<br /> <br /> Y'know. Stuff and options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:29:13-07:00","id":919796,"title":"","content":"Oh i'm not saying your ideas are at all wrong. I think it is a cool idea, and could really improve all of our games. I meant you guys telling each other the correct way to interpret it could have escalated. I'm glad you shared ^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T22:07:39-07:00","id":927447,"title":"","content":"I was actually discussing this recently and felt like sharing. <br /> When we're talking about changing up the core elements and mechanics of a game to make it handle other concepts better what we're basically asking is if we can &quot;take it off road.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with wanting to take any car off road, but not every car is equally well designed to accomplish that. This isn't to say you can't modify a car to make it better at off-roading, but that's work you have to put in on your end if it's something you really want to make happen. By the same token there's nothing wrong with putting monster truck tires on a Ferrari, do what you want to do if it's your hobby, but some people are also going to look at it and wonder what the point was. Neither they nor you are wrong, but you look at the same idea and see differing levels of utility in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T22:49:41-07:00","id":927459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=927447#post927447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually discussing this recently and felt like sharing. <br /> When we're talking about changing up the core elements and mechanics of a game to make it handle other concepts better what we're basically asking is if we can &amp;quot;take it off road.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with wanting to take any car off road, but not every car is equally well designed to accomplish that. This isn't to say you can't modify a car to make it better at off-roading, but that's work you have to put in on your end if it's something you really want to make happen. By the same token there's nothing wrong with putting monster truck tires on a Ferrari, do what you want to do if it's your hobby, but some people are also going to look at it and wonder what the point was. Neither they nor you are wrong, but you look at the same idea and see differing levels of utility in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent analogy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T01:38:01-07:00","id":927493,"title":"","content":"Worth adding to that analogy is that not everyone who enjoys and is good at riding the car will have mechanical and technical acumen to modify it to suit the off-road, so sometimes it's either better to take it to a person with know-how, or buy a off road car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T20:51:33-07:00","id":929033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=927493#post927493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth adding to that analogy is that not everyone who enjoys and is good at riding the car will have mechanical and technical acumen to modify it to suit the off-road, so sometimes it's either better to take it to a person with know-how, or buy a off road car.</div> </div> </div> </div>Readme: sorry for all that crap about Carmageddon, but it's a game so polarising that it's perfect for all that I was trying to say.<br /> <br /> The post:<br /> It's funny because that analogy looks like it's telling that you cannot play Carmageddon... in Carmageddon!...<br /> Confusing the rule-set with the setting is easy, specially in narrative games like this, but changing what you or your group don't like is a given when you start a game, mostly if you don't have any alternative rule-set of the type of game you want to play.<br /> <br /> Honoring the theme and mood it's not the way a game should be played, honoring the game playing it it's much better.<br /> After all, isn't this a game in which you can use rules wise what you like and disregard the rest? isn't it perhaps a modular game with no metaplot in which you can use the setting elements you like and use the ones you don't as toilet paper? isn't it this game advertised in this way?<br /> <br /> A product starts to smell like a rotten fish in the same instant that it told you: you can do whatever you want, but you can't do whatever you want - which isn't the case, thanks god -.<br /> But the smell is even worst when the fanbase itself starts telling that you can't because even if the product it's telling you so, you're doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> So, changing that you don't like isn't missing the point, some people like racing, some people like killing things, ok, no problem, the game let's you do both and no one it's doing it wrong.<br /> and the ones who don't like killing things shouldn't say to the other group that they should search for another game because Carmageddon it's about racing, not about killing things.<br /> This it was that analogy is.<br /> <br /> maybe I misunderstood something somewhere, I don't know, but this is what I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nosolorol.com/nuevo/images/Fostern.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura","user":"Aura","date":".  correcting typos 07-09-2016, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura","name":"Aura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T21:19:07-07:00","id":929043,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1192\" data-vbnamecard=\"1192\">Aura</a>: I think you may have missed the point of the analogy. The whole idea is that there's nothing wrong with modifying the car how ever you want. But certain mods are going to take a lot of work to implement. That's ok if you are cool with putting in that work, just know what you're getting yourself into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T21:25:23-07:00","id":929045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=929033#post929033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny because that analogy looks like it's telling that you cannot play Carmageddon... in Carmageddon!...</div> </div> </div> </div>Carmageddon is a video game depicting an alternate reality, not a car. It has even more limits in what it can do. It can't drive you to work, you can't pack your belonging in it to move to your new house, it can't take you to across the country. It can only play Carmageddon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-10-2016, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T03:50:02-07:00","id":929153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=929043#post929043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1192\" data-vbnamecard=\"1192\">Aura</a>: I think you may have missed the point of the analogy. The whole idea is that there's nothing wrong with modifying the car how ever you want. But certain mods are going to take a lot of work to implement. That's ok if you are cool with putting in that work, just know what you're getting yourself into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I misunderstood, I'm very happy to know that, I hope that no offense was taken.<br /> I know that extreme modding is time consuming, but very easy too and the more you do, the fastest it became.<br /> Modular systems like Nwod/CroD are even easier as are constructed with that in mind: if you put or quit something it's still going to work perfectly.<br /> A lot of the published material let's you do extremes modification to the rule-set in less than a day if you don't have time for writing, Mirrors and the Chronicler's guide are very useful for skipping a lot of the writing for each system, well, it's not illegal when it's only for personal use right? and the Fate toolkit book works perfectly with CroD too.<br /> I'm only talking about the crunch though, the rules, the fluff is another beast, not doing your own is laziness and mala praxis.<br /> <br /> Even with that, sometimes it's not enough, I'm writing my own system from scratch, that's is really time consuming... and fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907459-changing-what-you-don-t-like-or-missing-the-point?p=929045#post929045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carmageddon is a video game depicting an alternate reality, not a car. It has even more limits in what it can do. It can't drive you to work, you can't pack your belonging in it to move to your new house, it can't take you to across the country. It can only play Carmageddon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misunderstood that analogy, but you seems like to misunderstood mine...<br /> I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nosolorol.com/nuevo/images/Fostern.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura","name":"Aura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}